s="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2.5 4H5l2.2 10.5h10.3L19.6 7H6"/><circle cx="9" cy="19" r="1.6"/><circle cx="16.5" cy="19" r="1.6"/></svg></span><span><strong>Groceries</strong><span class="t">About 6 minutes</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 3h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2zM12 7.5v9M7.5 12h9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Hospital</strong><span class="t">About 10 minutes</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach is a newer 55+ neighborhood of mostly one-story houses on short streets around ponds.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach has about 400 homes built so far, and its builder is still selling new ones. At least one person in each household must be 55 or older.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Owners share a clubhouse with an indoor lap pool, an outdoor pool