ranslate(113.4 231.6)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">7</text></g></g><g transform="translate(314.3 134)"><g class="k"><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">9</text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">Map of the twelve neighborhoods, numbered as on this page, with the nearest towns. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><div class="t"><table><caption>The HOA fee and tax a year, the drive to a beach, and the zoned schools</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Fee and tax a year</th><th scope="col">To a beach</th><th scope="col">Schools (district zones)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#parkview">1. Parkview</a></th><td>About $4,700</td><td>About 4 min</td><td>Myrtle Beach Elementary, Middle and High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#fairways-at-wild-wing">2. Fairways at Wild Wing</a></th><td>About $6,100</td><td>About 20 min</td><td>Carolina Forest Elementary, Ten Oaks Middle, Carolina Forest High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#sawgrass-east">3. Sawgrass East</a></th><td>About $6,000</td><td>About 20 min</td><td>Ten Oaks Elementary, Ten Oaks Middle, Carolina Forest High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#birchwood">4. Birchwood</a></th><td>About $2,400</td><td>About 20 min</td><td>Daisy Elementary, Loris Middle, Loris High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#golf-and-yacht-club">5. Golf and Yacht Club</a></th><td>About $2,100</td><td>About 15 min</td><td>St. James Elementary, Intermediate, Middle and High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#forestbrook-village">6. Forestbrook Village</a></th><td>About $3,000</td><td>About 13 min</td><td>Forestbrook Elementary, Forestbrook Middle, Socastee High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#victory-point">7. Victory Point</a></th><td>About $3,800</td><td>About 14 min</td><td>Pine Island Elementary, Ten Oaks Middle, Carolina Forest High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#amber-bluff">8. Amber Bluff</a></th><td>About $2,200</td><td>About 20 min</td><td>Waccamaw Elementary, Black Water Middle, Carolina Forest High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#villas-at-sandridge">9. Villas at Sandridge</a></th><td>About $4,600</td><td>About 7 min</td><td>Waterway Elementary, North Myrtle Beach Middle and High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#indigo-grove">10. Indigo Grove</a></th><td>About $2,000</td><td>About 13 min</td><td>Riverside Elementary, North Myrtle Beach Middle and High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#wynbrooke">11. Wynbrooke</a></th><td>About $6,500</td><td>About 9 min</td><td>St. James Elementary, Intermediate, Middle and High</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#polo-farms">12. Polo Farms</a></th><td>About $1,300</td><td>About 20 min</td><td>Daisy Elementary, Loris Middle, Loris High</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figcaption>The fee and tax are for a year, besides the mortgage and insurance, for a home you live in. The HOA fee includes water and sewer at Parkview, and usually at Sawgrass East and Wynbrooke. At the Fairways, only some homes list them in the fee. Drives have no traffic; in our experience, rush hour adds 5 to 10 minutes.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="property-tax"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Property tax">How much property tax will you pay?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take a $240,000 home that is your main home. <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Its yearly tax</a> depends on where it is:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Outside a town, or in Myrtle Beach: about $970.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">In Polo Farms: about $980. In Wynbrooke: about $1,030.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Inside <a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Conway</a>: about $1,570.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When you buy, the county values the home at about what it is worth that year, and the new value shows up on the next year's bill. These figures use the county's lower rate for a home you live in, which our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> explains.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="down-payment"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Down payment help">What help can you get with a down payment?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">SC Housing, the state's housing agency, gives buyers in Horry and Georgetown counties $10,000 toward the down payment and closing costs. It is forgivable: you do not pay it back if you stay in the home long enough. The program is called the <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/programs-homebuyers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Homebuyer Program</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You do not have to be a first-time buyer. The program has these limits:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">You must not own a home when you close.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Household income must be under about $115,000 for one or two people, and under about $134,000 for three or more.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The home price can be up to $450,000.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You apply through a lender that works with SC Housing. Our page on <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">down-payment help programs</a> explains the Homebuyer Program step by step, including the credit score it needs.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Dana rents an apartment in Myrtle Beach and wants a house of her own in Conway. She thinks she must save for years before she can buy.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Her Chapter3 agent shows her SC Housing's Homebuyer Program, which helps buyers here pay the down payment. The agent puts her in touch with a lender that works with the program.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Dana takes the homebuyer class and starts looking at houses, instead of saving for years first.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="affordable-places-near-myrtle-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Affordable places near Myrtle Beach: FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the cheapest neighborhood to buy a home near Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the neighborhoods within about 20 minutes of the beach where at least 10 homes sold in the past year, Parkview had the lowest prices. Its older townhomes usually sold for about $190,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where can you buy a new house near Myrtle Beach for less?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Birchwood, off SC 905 near Longs, new Lennar houses usually sold for about $225,000 in the past year. In Indigo Grove, off SC 90, they usually sold for about $245,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it cheaper to buy in Conway than in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A home that resold in Conway in the past year usually went for about $265,000. In the city of Myrtle Beach, a home usually went for about $420,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do you have to be a first-time buyer to get down-payment help?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No, not in Horry or Georgetown County. Palmetto Home Advantage, an SC Housing down-payment program, is open to repeat buyers too. Our page on down-payment help programs covers it and the Homebuyer Program.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county parcels</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county tax rates</a>, <a href="https://project-osrm.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap drive times</a>, <a href="https://schousing.sc.gov/homebuyers/programs-homebuyers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Housing</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/whispering_pines_golf_course.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.lennar.com/new-homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/longs/the-overlook" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lennar</a>. Not legal, tax or loan advice. The list: 10 or more sales and a beach access within about 20 minutes. Prices: the middle recorded sale, October 2025 to September 2026, without condos or manufactured homes. Drives from the middle of each place, no traffic. Homes from listings and builders; schools from zones. Tax for a home you live in, before the break at 65.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Parkview, beside 17th Avenue South, with Whispering Pines Golf Course, from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, resized it and added labels (place names and points from county records and OpenStreetMap).</div><div role="listitem">The old Myrtle Beach Speedway beside US 501, before Victory Point was built on part of its land. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, resized it and added labels (place names and points from county records and OpenStreetMap).</div><div role="listitem">Main Street in downtown Conway, the downtown closest to Amber Bluff. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conway_Downtown_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Polo Farms off SC 905, with Simpson Creek along its southwest side. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, resized it and added labels (place names and points from county records and OpenStreetMap).</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3re