+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Affordable places</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying on a budget</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Where are the most affordable places to buy a home near Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Twelve neighborhoods, and the best thing about each.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Affordable places near Myrtle Beach, with what the price buys in each: the house, the land and the drive.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Within about 20 minutes of a beach, these twelve neighborhoods near Myrtle Beach had the lowest prices last year. Homes in them usually sold for about $190,000 to $255,000, against about $420,000 for a Myrtle Beach home that is not a condo. Four of the twelve are neighborhoods of houses; the rest are townhomes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="compare"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The twelve at a glance">What does each neighborhood do best?</h2><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inse