+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Best Neighborhoods</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Choosing a neighborhood</p><h1 class="detail-h1">What are the best neighborhoods in Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Pick by what you love.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Thirteen neighborhoods near Myrtle Beach, grouped by what each does best.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a walk to the beach, the best neighborhood near Myrtle Beach is Cherry Grove. For a golf course neighborhood, Tidewater. For a new house, Deerfield. For a boat, Plantation Lakes. For a town center you can walk, The Market Common. For a lower price, Avalon.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="choose"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What each does best">What does each neighborhood do best?</h2><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.95);--g-sh:0 1px 2px rgba(28,32,40,.05),0 14px 36px -20px rgba(28,32,40,.3);--g-r:20px;--g-blur:saturate(1