ounty houses</strong><span class="t">about 4 months</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Homes with a price cut</strong><span class="t">over half</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Condos have room to bargain; most houses do not yet. The counts by price and town, what a home costs to own, and the South Carolina steps to buy.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across Horry County, the Myrtle Beach area, it is a buyer's market for condos. The condos for sale would take about 7.5 months to sell at the past year's pace.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses would take about 4 months, so sellers still have a slight edge. Houses at $700,000 and up are near the point where buyers gain the edge. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, condos have about a year of supply.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:cent