<path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Often no down payment</strong><span class="t">on VA and USDA loans</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Seller-paid closing costs</strong><span class="t">on FHA and VA</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span><strong>$10,000 from SC Housing</strong><span class="t">under its income limit</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Your cash to buy in Myrtle Beach is the down payment plus the closing costs, and a first-time buyer can often bring less of each.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Your down payment depends on your loan. Your lender gives you the figure when it pre-approves you, after checking your credit and income. Part of your cash is earnest money, the deposit you give with your offer. In an ordinary sale it is credited to you at closing.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A VA loan often needs no down payment. A USDA loan can cover the full price inside USDA's area, mostly around Conway, Loris, Aynor and Longs, for low- and moderate-income buyers. On an FHA loan, a credit score of 580 or more gets FHA's smallest down payment, and the seller can pay your closing costs. SC Housing adds $10,000 for buyers under its income limit.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Homes in your budget, checked for you</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me homes in my budget</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#cash" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Cash</a></li><li><a href="#what-it-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What it buys</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where</a></li><li><a href="#condo-or-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Condo or house</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly cost</a></li><li><a href="#qualify" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Qualify</a></li><li><a href="#steps" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Steps</a></li><li><a href="#first-time-home-buyer-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">First-time home buyer questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="cash"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Cash">How much cash do you need to buy a first home in Myrtle Beach?</h2><style>.c3-ft-ic{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:40px;height:40px;border-radius:13px;color:var(--brass);background:rgba(255,255,255,.85);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);box-shadow:0 6px 14px -10px rgba(28,32,40,.45)}.c3-ft-ways{list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.8rem;max-width:760px}@media (min-width:700px){.c3-ft-ways{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}.c3-ft-ways>li{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.8),rgba(255,255,255,.56));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.92);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.85),0 18px 40px -28px rgba(28,32,40,.45);border-radius:20px;margin:0;padding:1rem 1.1rem .95rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:40px 1fr;gap:.2rem .85rem;align-items:start;align