 Cherry Grove</a></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><a href="#myrtle-beach">Myrtle Beach, east of Kings Highway</a></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><a href="#surfside-to-murrells-inlet">Surfside Beach, Garden City and Murrells Inlet</a></li><li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><a href="#litchfield-and-pawleys-island">Litchfield and Pawleys Island</a></li></ol><figcaption>The tan strip is the land within half a mile of the ocean. Each dot is a public beach access on the state's map. The dots are close together from Garden City to Cherry Grove, and far apart at Huntington Beach State Park and on Pawleys Island. Shoreline: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line, public domain. Accesses: SC Department of Environmental Services. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><h3 id="north-myrtle-beach" class="nb-place" data-n="1">North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove</h3><p class="nb-line">Four old beach towns, marsh channels</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is four old beach towns that voted to join in 1968: Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero nb-side-ph nb-full" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="857" alt="Cherry Grove from above: rows of houses on narrow lots between dug channels, with docks behind them, the marsh beyond, and the ocean along the bottom, labelled Boat ramp, Heritage Shores, Channel houses and Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on the Cherry Grove channels, many with a dock behind them, between the marsh and the beach. The boat ramp and Heritage Shores are at the top.</figcaption></figure><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="The four old beach towns"><li><b>Cherry Grove</b>The quieter beach, at the north end. About 680 houses here are on long channels dug in the marsh, often with a dock. The city's boat ramp reaches the ocean through Hog Inlet. Heritage Shores Nature Preserve has about 7 acres of paths on an island in the marsh.</li><li><b>Ocean Drive</b>Main Street, and the Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve, with dunes 30 feet tall and a half-mile trail. In Ocean Drive and Crescent Beach, a pavilion drew crowds to dance the shag, now South Carolina's state dance.</li><li><b>Crescent Beach</b>South of Ocean Drive, with the 18th and Edge pocket park.</li><li><b>Windy Hill</b>Past the separate town of Atlantic Beach. Investors from Conway built it up after World War II. It has Yow Park and the 41st Avenue South pocket park.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses near the ocean here sold for about $625,000 at the middle in the last year. Our <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach page</a> covers each part of the city.</p><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><div class="hx-strip" data-place="beach-walk-north-myrtle-beach" data-name="North Myrtle Beach beach-walk houses" data-head="Houses a walk from the beach in North Myrtle Beach"></div><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Myrtle%20Beach">Have us find a house in North Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="myrtle-beach" class="nb-place" data-n="2">Myrtle Beach, east of Kings Highway</h3><p class="nb-line">The boardwalk, the busy beach, and the fewest houses in the flood zone</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Myrtle Beach, the main road near the ocean is Kings Highway, also called US 17 Business. We measured its distance from the ocean along its whole length in the city. For half of it, the road is within about half a mile of the ocean.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Listings say "east of 17" for the streets between Kings Highway and the sand. Houses marked east of 17 in our home search are a little under half a mile from the ocean at the middle.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero nb-side-ph" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Two-story houses on wide green lawns behind the dunes, with wooden walkways to the beach and oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on wide lawns facing the beach north of downtown Myrtle Beach, with Ocean Boulevard and streets of houses under oaks behind them.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown is the busy beach, with the boardwalk and volleyball. The Boardwalk is about 1.3 miles long, beside the ocean, with a raised wooden walk and a paved walk along the beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This stretch runs from Briarcliffe Acres south to Surfside Beach, and includes Arcadian Shores and Myrtle Beach State Park. Within half a mile of the ocean on this stretch, the middle sale price of a house was about $670,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach page</a> covers the city's neighborhoods and its rental rules.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Get the houses near the beach in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="surfside-to-murrells-inlet" class="nb-place" data-n="3">Surfside Beach, Garden City and Murrells Inlet</h3><p class="nb-line">A town pier, free county parking, and the marsh at Murrells Inlet</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This stretch is Surfside Beach, Garden City and Murrells Inlet, from north to south.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero nb-side-ph" style="max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A row of two- and three-story beach houses in blue, yellow and gray behind low dunes, seen across a wide sand beach under a blue sky at Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: BullDawg2021. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: BullDawg2021</a></span></div><figcaption>The oceanfront row of beach houses at Surfside Beach, seen from the sand.</figcaption></figure><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="The three beach places"><li><b>Surfside Beach</b>A town of about 1.9 square miles. Every home in it is within about 0.8 mile of Ocean Boulevard, the beach road. The concrete town pier is free to walk on, with two restaurants and an ice cream shop.</li><li><b>Life in Surfside Beach</b>On summer Sunday evenings, the town holds a free concert in Memorial Park. On Memorial Day, the Fourth of July and in December, golf cart parades go down Ocean Boulevard.</li><li><b>Garden City</b>Not a town: Horry County runs it. Its beach road is Waccamaw Drive, and houses on the marsh line Dogwood Drive. Horry County's oceanfront beach accesses here have free parking all year.</li><li><b>Murrells Inlet</b>The MarshWalk is a half-mile wooden boardwalk along the marsh, with restaurants and free live music.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This stretch has the highest prices of the three in Horry County: about $775,000 at the middle for a house within half a mile of the ocean. Our pages on <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a>, <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Garden City</a> and <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a> cover each town.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Ask about houses in Surfside Beach and Garden City<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="litchfield-and-pawleys-island" class="nb-place" data-n="4">Litchfield and Pawleys Island</h3><p class="nb-line">A barrier island of old beach houses, and the highest prices</p><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="Pawleys Island and Litchfield"><li><b>Pawleys Island</b>A barrier island less than 4 miles long, mostly one house wide, with salt marsh behind it. The town has a 25 mph speed limit and no lifeguards on the beach.</li><li><b>Life on the island</b>People crab and fish from the two marsh bridges, and the town still calls itself by its old nickname, "arrogantly shabby". On about 6 in 10 island houses, the last deed was not a sale, the way a house passes to children or an estate.</li><li><b>Litchfield</b>The beach between the island and Huntington Beach State Park. A bike path goes along US 17 from behind the island through Litchfield to Murrells Inlet.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There are fewer public paths here. Pawleys Island has the largest free beach parking lot in Georgetown County, at the south end, and 8 other public accesses. The state's map shows one about every 2,400 feet on the island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses for sale within half a mile of the ocean here ask about $2.1 million at the middle. This coast is in Georgetown County, outside the Horry County deed records we used, so we give asking prices here. Our <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island page</a> has the island's own sales and flood zones.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">Ask about houses on Pawleys Island<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What they cost">How much does a house near the beach cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The nearer the ocean, the more a house sold for. Houses within a quarter mile of the ocean sold for about $805,000 at the middle in the last year.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a house sold for, by distance from the ocean"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a house sold for, by distance from the ocean</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Distance from the ocean</span><span role="columnheader">Middle sale price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Under a quarter mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$805,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A quarter to half a mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.671" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$540,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Half a mile to 1 mile</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.634" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$510,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1 to 2 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.621" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$500,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2 to 5 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.484" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$390,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">5 to 10 miles</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.435" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$350,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">10 miles or more</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.36" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$290,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses sold in Horry County in the last year, from the county's deed records. The middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Gray bars: 2 miles or more inland.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The price is highest in the first tenth of a mile, about 500 feet. Houses there sold for about $1.33 million. From half a mile to 2 miles back, the price stays near $500,000. Our <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">waterfront homes page</a> covers houses on the ocean itself.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="under-400k"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Under $400,000">Where can you buy a house near the beach for under $400,000?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 1 in 6 house sales within half a mile of the ocean was under $400,000 in the last year. Most of those were in North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our count of houses for sale, 20 under $400,000 were a <span class="nb-nw">10-minute</span> walk or less from a beach path. Of those, 14 were in North Myrtle Beach, most of them in Crescent Beach.</p><table class="nb-tbl"><caption>Houses for sale a 10-minute walk or less from a beach path, by price</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Asking price</th><th scope="col">Houses</th><th scope="col">Middle size</th><th scope="col">Most have</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Under $400,000</th><td data-l="Houses">20</td><td data-l="Middle size">1,360 sq ft</td><td data-l="Most have">3 bedrooms</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">$400,000 to $600,000</th><td data-l="Houses">51</td><td data-l="Middle size">1,460 sq ft</td><td data-l="Most have">3 bedrooms</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="nb-note">Our count of the houses for sale on our site, with campground homes on leased sites left out. The walk follows mapped streets and paths. Middle size: half are bigger, half smaller.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In North Myrtle Beach, 12 of the 14 are on Edge Drive, Hillside Drive South and the numbered avenues South, such as 11th, 23rd and 28th Avenue South. In Myrtle Beach, 3 of the 5 are on Collins Street and North Oak Street.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="beach-walk-nmb-under-400k" data-name="beach-walk houses at $400,000 or less" data-head="Beach-walk houses in North Myrtle Beach at $400,000 or less"></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zones">Will you need flood insurance for a house near the beach?</h2><div class="nb-side"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Often, if the house is close to the ocean and you buy with a mortgage. About half of Horry County houses within a quarter mile of the ocean are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. A quarter to half a mile back, about 1 in 4 are.</p><div class="nb-aside"><figure class="c3-gchart nb-fig"><span class="cap nb-cap">Share of houses in the high-risk flood zone, by distance from the ocean</span><svg class="nb-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 230" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of the share of Horry County houses in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, by distance from the ocean in twentieths of a mile: 0.0 to 0.1 mile, 74 percent; 0.05 to 0.1 mile, 72 percent; 0.1 to 0.2 mile, 52 percent; 0.15 to 0.2 mile, 44 percent; 0.2 to 0.3 mile, 41 percent; 0.25 to 0.3 mile, 36 percent; 0.3 to 0.4 mile, 27 percent; 0.35 to 0.4 mile, 19 percent; 0.4 to 0.5 mile, 12 percent; 0.45 to 0.5 mile, 17 percent; 0.5 to 0.6 mile, 15 percent; 0.55 to 0.6 mile, 14 percent; 0.6 to 0.7 mile, 9 percent; 0.65 to 0.7 mile, 10 percent; 0.7 to 0.8 mile, 9 percent; 0.75 to 0.8 mile, 5 percent; 0.8 to 0.9 mile, 3 percent; 0.85 to 0.9 mile, 1 percent; 0.9 to 1 mile, 1 percent; 0.95 to 1 mile, 1 percent."><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="186" y2="186" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="34" y="191" text-anchor="end">0%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="132.3" y2="132.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="137.3" text-anchor="end">25%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="78.5" y2="78.5" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="83.5" text-anchor="end">50%</text><line x1="40" x2="352" y1="24.8" y2="24.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="34" y="29.8" text-anchor="end">75%</text><rect x="41.9" y="26.7" width="11.9" height="159.3" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="57.5" y="32.3" width="11.9" height="153.7" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="73.1" y="74.8" width="11.9" height="111.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="88.7" y="90.5" width="11.9" height="95.5" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="104.3" y="97" width="11.9" height="89" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="119.9" y="108.8" width="11.9" height="77.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="135.5" y="128.8" width="11.9" height="57.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="151.1" y="145.6" width="11.9" height="40.4" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="166.7" y="159.3" width="11.9" height="26.7" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="182.3" y="148.8" width="11.9" height="37.2" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="197.9" y="154.8" width="11.9" height="31.2" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="213.5" y="155.9" width="11.9" height="30.1" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="229.1" y="166" width="11.9" height="20" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="244.7" y="164.5" width="11.9" height="21.5" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="260.3" y="166.4" width="11.9" height="19.6" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="275.9" y="176.1" width="11.9" height="9.9" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="291.5" y="180.6" width="11.9" height="5.4" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="307.1" y="184.1" width="11.9" height="1.9" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="322.7" y="184.7" width="11.9" height="1.3" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><rect x="338.3" y="183.6" width="11.9" height="2.4" rx="2" fill="#d9b48f"/><line x1="40" x2="40" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="40" y="208" text-anchor="start">0</text><line x1="118" x2="118" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="118" y="208" text-anchor="middle">¼</text><line x1="196" x2="196" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="196" y="208" text-anchor="middle">½</text><line x1="274" x2="274" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="274" y="208" text-anchor="middle">¾</text><line x1="352" x2="352" y1="186" y2="191" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="352" y="208" text-anchor="end">1 mile</text><text x="196" y="226" text-anchor="middle">Distance from the ocean</text></svg><figcaption>Each column is a twentieth of a mile, about 260 feet. Darker: the first half mile. Horry County houses, with FEMA's flood zones from the county's map, at the middle of each lot.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the house is in the high-risk flood zone and you buy with a mortgage, the lender requires flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Past about three quarters of a mile from the ocean, fewer than 1 in 20 houses are in the high-risk zone.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Near the ocean, it depends on the town. Of the three Horry County stretches, Myrtle Beach has the fewest houses in the high-risk zone:</p><div class="nb-stat"><p class="k">Houses within half a mile of the ocean in the high-risk flood zone</p><ul><li><strong>About 1 in 11</strong><span>on the Myrtle Beach stretch, from Briarcliffe Acres to Surfside Beach</span></li><li><strong>About 4 in 10</strong><span>in North Myrtle Beach and Cherry Grove</span></li><li><strong>About half</strong><span>from Surfside Beach to Murrells Inlet</span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Horry County, a FEMA flood policy on a house the owner lives in cost about $1,070 a year at the middle inside the high-risk zone. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> covers wind and flood policies here. Our <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">page on undisclosed flooding</a> covers what we look up to learn whether a house has flooded before.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want a house near the sand and outside the high-risk flood zone?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the town. We send the houses for sale there that are outside FEMA's high-risk zone, with the walk to the beach from each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us find them</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pros-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living near the beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">With a house near the beach, you can walk to the sand, and you usually pay no HOA fee. You pay more for the house, and flood insurance is more likely.</p><div class="nb-pc"><div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The good</h3><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="The good"><li><b>You walk to the beach</b>From a house near the beach, the sand can be a <span class="nb-nw">5-minute</span> walk. From a house inland in Carolina Forest or Conway, the beach is a <span class="nb-nw">20- to 30-minute</span> drive with no traffic.</li><li><b>Usually no HOA fee</b>About 3 in 4 houses for sale in the first quarter mile report no homeowners association (HOA) fee. <span class="nb-nw">Two to 5</span> miles inland, about 1 in 10 report none. Our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA page</a> covers what that allows.</li><li><b>A few streets back costs much less</b>Past the first quarter mile, houses sold for about a third less at the middle. Half a mile from the ocean is still about a <span class="nb-nw">10-minute</span> walk.</li></ul></div><div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The hard</h3><ul class="nb-plain" aria-label="The hard"><li><b>Fewer houses, higher prices</b>Only about 1 in 16 house sales in Horry County was within half a mile of the ocean. Those houses sold for about 1.7 times as much as houses <span class="nb-nw">2 to 5</span> miles inland.</li><li><b>Flood insurance is more likely</b>Near the ocean, many houses are in the high-risk flood zone. We look up the zone and the policy cost for the house before you make an offer.</li><li><b>Many neighbors are part-time</b>At the 2020 Census, close to half the homes in North Myrtle Beach were held for seasonal or vacation use.</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="houses-near-the-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Houses near the beach FAQ</h2><style>.c3-faq details{border-top:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq details:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.2rem 0}.c3-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.c3-faq summary h3{margin:.9rem 0!important;flex:1}.c3-faq summary::after{content:"+";font:400 1.5rem/1 var(--sans);color:var(--brass);flex:none;width:1.5rem;text-align:center}.c3-faq details[open] summary::after{content:"\2212"}.c3-faq details p{margin:0 0 1rem!important}.c3-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brass);outline-offset:3px}</style><div class="c3-faq"><details open><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach in a flood zone?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Parts of it are. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, only about 1 in 23 houses is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. About 1 in 4 condos in the city is.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you rent out a house near the beach in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rules differ by city. In the City of Myrtle Beach, a rental of less than 90 days is legal only where the zoning allows it. About 96 in 100 houses there are not in those zones. North Myrtle Beach allows short-term rentals across the city, with a city business license renewed each year.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a condo near the beach cheaper than a house?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In North Myrtle Beach, yes. In its beach sections, a condo sold for about $310,000 to $360,000 at the middle in the last year. This page covers houses; our condos page covers condos.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is a second-row house at the beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A second-row house is in the row just behind the oceanfront houses. Our waterfront homes page covers the oceanfront row itself.</p></details></div><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/tiger-line-file.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census TIGER/Line</a>, <a href="https://gis.des.sc.gov/beachaccess/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDES beach access map</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/services/accessibility_information/index.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://parks.nmb.us/339/Beach-Accesses-Amenities" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/200/Beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/beach-access-parking/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pawleys Island</a>, <a href="https://horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/beach-accesses/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County beach accesses</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.org/US17Bus-RSA" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT</a>, <a href="https://routing.openstreetmap.de/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap foot router</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/nfip-redacted-policies-v3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA policies</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 U.S.C. 4012a</a>. Houses for sale: our count of the listings on our site, November 8, 2026, asking prices, in aggregate, from CCMLS. Distances: 