 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero nb-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1099px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Garden City Beach from over the ocean: the oceanfront row of houses, two more rows behind it, and the salt marsh behind them.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Where the houses a walk from the sand are near Myrtle Beach, what each beach town is like, what houses cost, and the flood zone.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On November 8, 2026, 186 houses for sale near the beach were a <span class="nb-nw">5-minute</span> walk or less from a public path to the sand. They are spread from Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island. About half the houses under $400,000 a 10-minute walk or less from the sand are in Crescent Beach, in North Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the last year, a Horry County house within half a mile of the ocean sold for about $675,000 at the middle. That means half sold for more and half for less. <span class="nb-nw">Two to 5</span> miles inland, the middle was about $390,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us your budget and how far you will walk. We send the houses that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us your budget</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#walk" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The walk</a></li><li><a href="#towns" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The beach towns</a></li><li><a href="#cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What they cost</a></li><li><a href="#under-400k" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Under $400,000</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zones</a></li><li><a href="#pros-cons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Pros and cons</a></li><li><a href="#houses-near-the-beach-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Houses near the beach FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="walk"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The walk">How far is the walk to the beach from a house near the beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We checked the walk to the sand from the houses for sale within 1.5 miles of the ocean. Each walk follows mapped streets and paths to the nearest public beach access on the state's map. A quarter mile takes about 5 minutes on foot, and half a mile about 10.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the beach towns, the state's map shows a public path to the sand about every 250 to 400 feet. North Myrtle Beach manages over 240 beach accesses, and Myrtle Beach counts 143.</p><div class="nb-stat"><p class="k">Houses for sale, by the walk to the nearest public path to the sand</p><ul><li><strong>186 for sale</strong><span>a <span class="nb-nw">5-minute</span> walk or less. Middle asking price about $950,000.</span></li><li><strong>109 for sale</strong><span>a <span class="nb-nw">5- to 10-minute</span> walk. Middle asking price about $680,000.</span></li><li><strong>104 for sale</strong><span>a <span class="nb-nw">10- to 20-minute</span> walk. Middle asking price about $650,000.</span></li></ul></div><p class="nb-note">These are asking prices for houses for sale today. The sale prices on this page are what houses sold for in the last year, from the county's deed records.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house that looks close on a map can still be a long walk. About 1 in 13 houses for sale within half a mile of the ocean is more than a mile on foot from a public path. Two in 3 of those are on the Litchfield and Pawleys Island coast, where the paths are far apart.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Parking at the beach, resident passes and the beach rules are on our <a href="/buyers/relocating/beaches/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">page on the beaches</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">How far is the walk from that house to the sand?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We measure the walk to the nearest public beach access and look up the flood zone the house is in.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us measure the walk</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="towns"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The beach towns">Which beach town near Myrtle Beach fits you?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The coast from Cherry Grove to Pawleys Island is four stretches of beach towns, one after another. Here they are from north to south.</p><figure class="nb-ma