 <section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">How to use these guides</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Start with the one that matches your situation</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every guide above is written for the Grand Strand specifically: the flood zones, the HOA rules, the insurance quirks, and the local programs that generic national advice misses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you only read one page, read the <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">complete guide to buying a home on the Grand Strand</a>. It covers every step from first look to keys. Then come back for the guide that fits your specific situation, and when you are ready, <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">talk to an agent</a> who does this every day.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Buying a home in Myrtle Beach: FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much do I need for a down payment to buy a home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Often less than you expect. VA and USDA loans allow zero down, FHA asks for a small down payment, and South Carolina down payment assistance programs can cover much of the rest. Our <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">down payment assistance guide</a> lists the current programs and amounts.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are the steps to buy a house in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Get pre-approved for a loan, tour and choose a home, make an offer, complete inspections, and close with a South Carolina attorney, which the state requires. Our <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">buying in Myrtle Beach guide</a> walks through each step and the local costs.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much are property taxes on a Myrtle Beach home?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Your legal residence is taxed at the 4 percent rate and is exempt from the school operating tax; a second home or rental is taxed at 6 percent, three to four times more. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Horry County property tax calculator</a> shows the exact bill for any price.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do I need flood insurance to buy in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It depends on the flood zone, and the zone alone does not settle it, since many homes outside the high-risk zones have still flooded. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance guide</a> explains how to check before you offer.</p></div></div></section>
