ef="/buyers/relocating/weather/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">weather page</a> has the numbers season by season, including the ocean temperature month by month.</p></div></section>
 
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Daily costs</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Groceries, gas and the power bill</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most daily costs are lower here. Groceries cost less than the Florida average and are untaxed in both states. The gas tax is about 11 cents a gallon lower, on top of the price difference at the pump. The typical electric bill is a few dollars a month lower. These numbers come from the same price data behind our <a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">cost of living calculator</a>, which compares your own metro against the Grand Strand.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">One cost is higher here: the general sales tax is 8 percent in unincorporated Horry County and 9 percent in the City of Myrtle Beach, against roughly 7 percent average combined in Florida.</p></div></section>
