-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Start here</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The five questions every relocator asks</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1.4rem">This page covers buying from out of state. These five cover everything else about the move, each with the real numbers and the sources behind them.</p><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(255px,1fr));gap:1rem;max-width:760px"><a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;text-decoration:none"><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">Cost of living calculator</span><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5">Compare your city with the Grand Strand across 387 metro areas, and see the income you would need here.</span></a><a href="/buyers/relocating/pros-and-cons/" style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;text-decoration:none"><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">Pros and cons, honestly</span><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5">What newcomers find hardest, what the weather really does, and the parts that make people leave.</span></a><a href="/buyers/relocating/moving-checklist/" style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;text-decoration:none"><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">Your first 45 days</span><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5">License, vehicle registration, county tax, utilities and the residence application, in deadline order.</span></a><a href="/buyers/relocating/schools/" style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;text-decoration:none"><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">Schools and attendance zones</span><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5">How to check the zone for an exact address, why zones change, and what to bring to register.</span></a><a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;text-decoration:none"><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">Property tax: 4% vs 6%</span><span style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5">The form that decides whether your tax bill is roughly a third of what it could otherwise be.</span></a></div></div></section>
