-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem">Relocation FAQ</h2>
-<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column">
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Do I need to visit Myrtle Beach before buying?</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Not necessarily before making an offer, but we strongly recommend one in-person visit before closing. We do live video walkthroughs of neighborhoods and properties before you travel so the trip is efficient. Most of our out-of-state buyers find their home on a single 2-day visit.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">How does a remote closing work in South Carolina?</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>SC law allows remote closings. You sign documents through a notary in your home state and submit them electronically to the closing attorney in South Carolina. We coordinate between the closing attorney, your lender, and you, so no step gets missed.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Which Myrtle Beach neighborhoods are best for relocators?</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Carolina Forest is the town relocating buyers ask about most. It has approximately 30 sub-neighborhoods across a range of price points and an active resale market. Market Common is the top pick for professionals who want walkability. Murrells Inlet and Pawleys Island attract those looking for a quieter lifestyle away from the tourist corridor.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">How is Myrtle Beach's cost of living compared to the Northeast?</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Overall cost of living in Myrtle Beach runs approximately 7% below the national average. Housing is significantly lower than markets in NC, NY, NJ, and PA. There is no state income tax on Social Security in SC, and property taxes are among the lowest in the region. The main cost surprises are coastal insurance and HOA fees on condos, which buyers from inland markets do not expect.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">What should I know about schools in Horry County?</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>School quality varies significantly by location in Horry County. Carolina Forest has the strongest school performance, including River Oaks Elementary and Carolina Forest High. Conway, Socastee, and Saint James districts are also solid options. Myrtle Beach city schools trend lower in performance ratings. If schools are a priority, filter your search to the Carolina Forest and North Myrtle Beach areas.</p></div></div>
-</div>
-</div>
-<div>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem">Mistakes Relocators Make</h2>
-<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column">
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Buying in the wrong neighborhood for their lifestyle</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>The Grand Strand is not one market. A family relocating from the suburbs of Charlotte who buys an oceanfront condo in Myrtle Beach city often finds the area too touristy and lacking the suburban feel they expected. Spend time in multiple neighborhoods on your visit before narrowing down. We build a neighborhood tour into every relocation plan.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Underestimating coastal insurance costs</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Buyers from inland markets are accustomed to one homeowners insurance policy. In coastal SC you need three: homeowners, wind/hail, and flood. Together these can add $400 to $700 per month to your housing cost. Get insurance quotes during your due diligence period, not after.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Not getting pre-approved before shopping</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Out-of-state buyers sometimes start touring before completing their pre-approval, assuming they can transfer a pre-approval letter from their current state. SC lenders underwrite coastal properties differently, particularly for condos, flood-zone properties, and investment purchases. Get your pre-approval with a SC-licensed lender before you tour. Our preferred lender, BrickWood Mortgage, is SC-licensed and can pre-approve you directly.</p></div></div>
-<div class="accordion-item"><h3 class="accordion-q">Relying on Zillow neighborhood data instead of local knowledge</h3><div class="accordion-a"><p>Zillow's neighborhood ratings do not reflect the block-by-block differences in the Grand Strand market. A zip code that looks average in the statistics may contain a golf-cart-friendly community or a high-performing STR corridor. Ask your agent for a block-by-block breakdown before drawing conclusions from online ratings.</p></div></div>
-</div>
-</div>
-</div>
