-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Who moves here</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Where our relocating clients come from</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More people move to the Myrtle Beach area than almost anywhere else in the country, and our clients reflect it. The single biggest wave is from <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">North Carolina</strong> right next door, followed by the Northeast, mainly New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania, plus Ohio. They come for the same handful of reasons: the coast, dramatically lower taxes and cost of living than up north, and a slower pace without giving up a real housing market. If you are one of them, start with <a href="/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">why everyone is moving here</a>, in one read. Then the tax and housing comparison in full, state by state: moving from <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-north-carolina/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">North Carolina</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">New York</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-jersey/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">New Jersey</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-pennsylvania/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Pennsylvania</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Ohio</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-maryland/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Maryland</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-virginia/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Virginia</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-connecticut/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Connecticut</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-massachusetts/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Massachusetts</a> and <a href="/buyers/relocating/from-florida/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Florida</a>. For Florida the case is the house and the town rather than the taxes, and we say so. Each covers the taxes in both directions, including the lines that cost more here, and each carries a calculator that puts your income tax and property tax now next to what you would pay here. Beyond the taxes, seven pages answer what life here looks like. They cover <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">which Grand Strand town fits</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/jobs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">jobs and the economy</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/healthcare/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">healthcare and hospitals</a>, and <a href="/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">every hurricane since Hugo</a>. They also cover <a href="/buyers/relocating/weather/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">the weather in numbers</a>, <a href="/buyers/relocating/getting-around/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">getting around, from the airport to the roads</a>, and <a href="/buyers/relocating/beaches/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">the beach rules, town by town</a>. Our <a href="/submarkets/">neighborhood guides</a> break down which Grand Strand towns fit which kind of move.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">You don&rsquo;t have to be here yet</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">You can buy before you finish moving</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of our relocating buyers start the search from hundreds of miles away, and that&rsquo;s completely normal here. We do video walkthroughs and pull the same investor-grade reports we run for our investors: permits nearby, what the block is like, and what a seller might not volunteer. We handle the process so you can make a confident offer without flying down for every showing.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A lot of Grand Strand homes are bought with cash by out-of-state buyers. To compete with a cash offer you need a strong pre-approval and an agent who can move fast. That is easier when your agent and your lender already work together.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The real hurdle</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">The hard part is usually the mortgage, not the house</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Relocating often means a job change, and a new job, a gap between jobs, or self-employment income can complicate a mortgage right when you&rsquo;re trying to buy. This is exactly where our preferred lender, <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497)</strong>, makes the biggest difference. Because our lending partner works with us daily, we can structure the timeline around your situation instead of forcing your life to fit a rigid loan process. Read <a href="/buyers/programs/" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">how our preferred lender relationship works</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The single biggest mistake we see relocators make is putting in an offer before they have a job lined up here. You can get approved for the mortgage with a signed job offer letter, so line the job up first. When people do it the other way around, go under contract and then start job hunting, the deal too often falls through. We have seen buyers lose the home they were under contract on because they could not line up a job they liked here before their contract deadline. Get the job, then we will move fast on the house.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Sort out your job and income first, because the mortgage depends on it. Then move fast on the house.</strong></p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">A real relocation we handled</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What it can take, and why the preferred lender matters</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An older couple relocating to the coast found their home, but they were still lining up new jobs here, and you generally need to show income to qualify for the mortgage. <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Three separate contract extensions</strong> were negotiated with the seller to buy them time while they landed those jobs. Because they had a pet and needed somewhere to stay, they were put up in a pet-friendly short-term rental at a steep discount in the meantime.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">After a lot of back-and-forth between the agent and the lender, they closed on their coastal home. An agent and a lender with no working relationship would likely have lost that deal.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The honest version</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Your money goes further here. Protect the difference.</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost everyone who moves down is surprised how much further their money goes on taxes, insurance, and day-to-day costs. The mistake we see: people celebrate the savings by overspending in the first year and end up tighter than they were up north. Enjoy the head start, just don&rsquo;t give it all back. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">cost of living calculator</a> compares your current city with this one line by line, and if you&rsquo;re retiring here, our <a href="/buyers/retirees/">retirees guide</a> lays out the specific South Carolina tax breaks in detail.</p>
-<p style="margin-bottom:0"><a href="/buyers/second-home/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Buying a second home &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">How buying here works &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a href="/submarkets/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Compare submarkets &rarr;</a></p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The real monthly number</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Lower prices, but build the real monthly number first</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost every relocator sees Grand Strand prices and feels relief. Homes here usually cost less than the Northeast and less than many big metros. That part is true. The mistake is stopping at the sticker price. On the coast, three things move the monthly cost that you may not have paid up north.</p>
-<ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Coastal insurance.</strong> Near the water you often need more than one policy, and it can add hundreds of dollars a month. We flag this in the mistakes list above and get you real quotes early, not after closing. The buyer mistakes that are not relocation-specific have their own page: <a href="/buyers/common-mistakes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">common Myrtle Beach buyer mistakes</a>.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Flood zones.</strong> FEMA, the federal agency that maps flood risk, marks some areas as more likely to flood. If your home is in one, a lender will require flood insurance. Two homes a block apart can be rated differently, so we check the map before you commit.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">HOA or condo regime fees.</strong> Many Grand Strand condos and planned communities charge a monthly fee that covers shared insurance and upkeep. On some buildings it is small; on others it is a big part of the payment. Always ask for the current figure.</li>
-</ul>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:0">None of this means the coast is expensive. It usually is not. It means the honest number to compare against your old home is the all-in monthly cost, not the price tag. We build that number with you before you commit. For the city-by-city comparison see the <a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">cost of living calculator</a>, and for a town-by-town look at prices, our <a href="/submarkets/" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">neighborhood guides</a>.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="padding:2.6rem 1.5rem;display:flex;gap:1.3rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto"><div style="flex:1 1 340px"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.4rem;color:var(--ivory);margin:0 0 .4rem">Not sure which town fits you yet?</p><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.93rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.65);margin:0;line-height:1.6">Tell us your budget and what you want to be near. We shortlist the areas that match and send real listings in each.</p></div><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Build my shortlist</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135" style="color:var(--ivory);border-color:rgba(244,239,232,.4)">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></section>
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">You do not know the area yet</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How to pick a Grand Strand town before you know the area</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When you are moving from far away, every Grand Strand town sounds the same at first. They are not the same. Before you tour, it helps to answer a few honest questions about how you want to live. The town most relocating buyers ask about has its own guide: <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Carolina Forest</a>.</p>
-<ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Beachfront or a few minutes inland?</strong> Right on the water costs more and can mean more tourists and traffic in summer. A short drive inland often gets you more house for the money and a quieter street.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Busy and tourist-heavy, or year-round and quiet?</strong> Some areas are lively all summer and slow in winter. Others feel like a normal neighborhood every month of the year.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">How far is your daily drive?</strong> If you or your partner will commute, check the drive to where the jobs are: Conway, the Market Common district in Myrtle Beach, and the main hospitals such as Grand Strand Medical Center and Conway Medical Center. Conway is the county seat, home to local government and Coastal Carolina University.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Schools or a 55-plus community?</strong> School quality varies a lot by area, which we cover in the FAQ above, and some communities are age-restricted.</li>
-</ul>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:0">We do not expect you to know this yet. That is our job. We match your answers to the right towns, then set up a tour so you feel the difference in person. For the full profile of each town, use our <a href="/submarkets/" style="color:var(--brass);text-decoration:none">neighborhood guides</a>.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Buying from far away</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How out-of-state buyers close remotely, step by step</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You do not need to be in South Carolina to get a home under contract. Most of our out-of-state buyers do the early steps from home and make one short trip. This is the usual order.</p>
-<ol style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.3rem">
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Get pre-approved with a South Carolina lender first.</strong> Pre-approval is a lender's written estimate of what you can borrow. Coastal condos and flood-zone homes are reviewed differently here, so a letter from your old state may not hold up. Our preferred lender can do this remotely.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tell us how you want to live, and we build a shortlist.</strong> We match your budget and must-haves to the right towns and send only homes worth your time.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">We tour for you on live video.</strong> We walk the home and the street on a video call, point the camera where you ask, and tell you what a photo will not, like road noise, the neighbors, and the real condition.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Make your offer from home.</strong> You sign the offer digitally. You can be under contract before you ever move.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Inspect during your due diligence period.</strong> That is the window after your offer when you can inspect the home and still back out. We line up the inspections and get your insurance and flood quotes so the monthly number is accurate.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Close remotely.</strong> In South Carolina an attorney handles the closing. You sign the final papers in front of a local notary, a person authorized to witness signatures, and send them in, or sign on a planned trip. Then the home is yours.</li>
-</ol>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:0">One in-person visit before closing is still smart, and we build one efficient trip into the plan. Many buyers find their home on a single two-day visit.</p>
-</div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.2rem 1.5rem">
-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Why relocators pick us</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How Chapter3 Realty helps relocators specifically</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Moving is hard enough. Our whole process is built so you can do most of it from where you are now, and so the loan does not fall through when your job is changing.</p>
-<ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">A remote-friendly process.</strong> Video tours, digital signing, and a local agent who checks the home and neighborhood in person for you. You can run the whole search from your current home.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:.7rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">A preferred lender for a changing job.</strong> Relocating often means a new job, a gap between jobs, or remote or self-employed income. Because our lending partner, BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497), works with us daily, we can time the loan around your situation instead of forcing your life to fit a rigid process.</li>
-<li style="margin-bottom:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Local research before you commit.</strong> We run the same checks we do for our investors: what the block is like, nearby permits and plans, flood-zone status, and what a seller may not volunteer. You commit with the facts, not a guess.</li>
-</ul>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1.4rem">An agent and a lender working together, with real local data, is how we get out-of-state buyers to closing without surprises. Start with a free 15-minute call and we will build your shortlist before you buy a plane ticket.</p>
-<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Start My Relocation Plan</a>
-</div></section>
