-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I buy a home while I&rsquo;m still relocating from out of state?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">Yes, most of our relocating buyers start from hundreds of miles away. We handle video walkthroughs, local due diligence, and the paperwork remotely so you can make a confident offer without flying down for every showing.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I get a mortgage if I&rsquo;m changing jobs to move here?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">Often yes, but a new job or an income gap can complicate qualifying. Because our lending partner, BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497), works with us daily, the loan timing and the contract timing can move together, and we&rsquo;ve negotiated contract extensions with sellers to buy clients time to get their income in place.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Where do most people relocating to Myrtle Beach come from?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">North Carolina is the single biggest state we see, since it sits right next door. After that, the largest groups come from the Northeast, mainly New York, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania, plus Ohio. Most are moving for the coast, the lower taxes and cost of living, and a slower pace.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Are property taxes lower in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">For a primary residence, usually yes. Owner-occupied homes in South Carolina are assessed at 4 percent and exempt from school operating taxes, which keeps effective rates among the lowest in the country.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I buy in Myrtle Beach before I move?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. Remote purchases are routine on the Grand Strand, with video tours, digital signing, and a mail-away or remote closing coordinated through a South Carolina attorney.</p></div></div></section>
-</main>
