ding:1.6rem 1.2rem 1.7rem!important;border-radius:24px!important}}</style></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">When relocating to Myrtle Beach from another state, you can sign, inspect and close on a home from where you live now.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you are relocating to Myrtle Beach, you can buy a home before you move. The offer can be signed electronically, and a South Carolina attorney may close by mail, so you do not have to be at the closing.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the latest IRS count, about 15,000 households moved into Horry County in one year, and about 9,100 moved out. In Myrtle Beach, a January day averages a high of about 56 degrees. An owner who lives in the home here typically pays about $944 a year in property tax. Our guide to <a href="/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">why so many people move here</a> gives the four reasons, with numbers.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Moving here? Tell us where from and what you want.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Plan my move with us</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#buy-before-you-move" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Buy before you move</a></li><li><a href="#your-state" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your state</a></li><li><a href="#guides" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Every moving guide</a></li><li><a href="#lead-form" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Contact us</a></li><li><a href="#questions-about-relocating" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Questions about relocating</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="buy-before-you-move"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Buy before you move">Can I buy a house in Myrtle Beach before I move?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do most of the work here while you stay where you are. These are the seven steps, in order.</p><ol class="rl-steps"><li><b>Pick the towns first.</b>Tell us how you want to live, and we narrow the search to the towns that fit. Start with our <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">13 towns near Myrtle Beach, compared</a>.</li><li><b>See the houses.</b>We tour the homes you like for you, and we tell you what the listing photos do not show. If you want to see a house yourself, we plan the showings around your trip.</li><li><b>Know the insurance before you offer.</b>When you buy with us, we get an insurance quote for the address before you make an offer.</li><li><b>Offer from home.</b>Under <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t26c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">South Carolina law</a>, an electronic signature on a contract has the same effect as one in ink. You can sign the offer from anywhere.</li><li><b>Inspect.</b>A home inspection is <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c050.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the buyer's job</a> in South Carolina. We line up the inspection.</li><li><b>Choose the closing attorney.</b>Every South Carolina home closing must be supervised by a <a href="https://www.sccourts.org/media/opinions/HTMLFiles/SC/25508.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">South Carolina attorney</a>. We work with several closing attorneys and can recommend them once we are working with you.</li><li><b>Sign the closing papers at home.</b>In a <a href="https://www.scbar.org/for-lawyers/quicklinks/legal-resources/ethics-advisory-opinions/ethics-advisory-opinion-05-16/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">closing by mail</a>, the papers are sent to you to sign and return. The attorney must be reachable by phone or email to explain them. You sign the deed or mortgage before a notary where you live, with two witnesses, and it <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t30c005.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">is filed here</a>. A lender may set its own signing rules.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You will not be the only buyer doing this from afar. About 3 in 10 homes sold in Horry County in the latest year went to a buyer whose tax bill goes to another state or country. For condos it was more than half.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The market and <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/#steps" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the steps to buy a house in South Carolina</a> are in our buying guide. Still own a home where you live now? <a href="/sell/sell-or-buy-first/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Sell first or buy first</a> shows the three ways to time the two sales.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying from another state? Send us the homes you like.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We set up the showings, get the insurance quote before you offer, and keep the attorney and the papers on schedule while you are still at home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the homes you like</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="your-state"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Your state">Which moving guide is for your state?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 8 in 10 out-of-state buyers here come from these ten states. Each state has its own moving guide.</p><div class="rl-tw"><table class="rl-tab"><caption>North Carolina sends the most out-of-state buyers, by far<span class="k">Buyers in a year from each state, and the road miles to Myrtle Beach</span></caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Buyers in a year</th><th scope="col">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-north-carolina/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Carolina</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">916</span><span class="bar" style="--f:1.000" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 50</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Brunswick County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">New York</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">438</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.478" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 750</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Suffolk County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-pennsylvania/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pennsylvania</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">376</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.410" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 610</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Allegheny County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-new-jersey/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">New Jersey</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">262</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.286" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 640</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Ocean County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-virginia/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Virginia</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">256</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.279" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 440</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Fairfax County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-maryland/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Maryland</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">169</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.184" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 500</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Baltimore County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-ohio/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Ohio</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">149</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.163" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 590</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Franklin County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-massachusetts/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Massachusetts</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">131</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.143" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 840</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Worcester County</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-connecticut/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Connecticut</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">129</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.141" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 790</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from the Hartford area</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/buyers/relocating/from-florida/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Florida</a></th><td><span class="l">Buyers in a year</span><span class="v">76</span><span class="bar" style="--f:0.083" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="l">Road miles to Myrtle Beach</span><span class="v">about 690</span><span class="u"> road miles</span><span class="z"> from Broward County</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p class="nt">Buyers: Horry County homes bought in a year by people with a tax bill in that state. Miles are by road from the middle of the county in that state that sends the most households here. Tap a state for its moving guide.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Carolina's largest source of new households is next door: Brunswick County, which borders Horry County.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Moving from somewhere else? Start with <a href="/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/#where-from" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">where movers to Myrtle Beach come from</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="guides"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Every moving guide">What should I know before moving to Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each question below has its own guide. Where it helps, we give the one fact movers ask about first.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it the right move?</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/why-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Why so many people are moving to Myrtle Beach</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/pros-and-cons/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The honest pros and cons of living here year-round</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/retirees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Retiring to Myrtle Beach, and how the state taxes retirement income</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ communities near Myrtle Beach, compared</a></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where should I live?</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">13 towns near Myrtle Beach, compared</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/best-neighborhoods/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The best neighborhoods, by what you love</a></li><li><a href="/submarkets/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">A guide to each part of the Grand Strand</a></li></ul><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/garden-city-pier-and-beach-road-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/garden-city-pier-and-beach-road-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-where-to-buy/garden-city-pier-and-beach-road-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Garden City Beach from over the ocean: the pier, shops along the beach road, mid-rise condo buildings and raised houses, with the salt marsh behind" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="USGS photo, 2011. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">USGS photo, 2011</a></span></div><figcaption>Garden City Beach from over the ocean in 2011: raised houses and condos along the sand, with the salt marsh behind them.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What will it cost?</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/cost-of-living/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The cost of living, compared with your city</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/cost-to-own/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What owning a home costs each month, line by line</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Horry County property tax: 4% vs 6%</a><span>A home you live in and apply for is taxed on 4 percent of its value, and <a href="/buyers/second-home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a second home</a> or rental on 6 percent. The 4 percent rate is not automatic: you apply after you buy.</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What home, wind and flood insurance cost here</a></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Work, health care and school</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/jobs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Who hires here, and what jobs pay</a><span>About half of the buyers who come to us from the northern states arrive with a remote job.</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/healthcare/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Hospitals and health care near Myrtle Beach</a></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/schools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How school zones, choice and registration work</a></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Weather, storms and the beach</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/weather/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach weather by month</a><span>The ocean at Myrtle Beach averages the low 70s in October.</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/beaches/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Beach rules, town by town: dogs, tents, parking and golf carts</a><span>From November 1 through February 28, golf carts with a valid state permit and a licensed driver may go on the beaches <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/about-our-beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County runs</a>. Those are its unincorporated stretches outside the towns, which include the Horry County part of Garden City Beach.</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/hurricanes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Every damaging hurricane since 1989</a></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Getting here and getting around</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/getting-around/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The four road names to learn, and the airport in town</a></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The move itself</h3><ul class="rl-guides"><li><a href="/buyers/relocating/moving-checklist/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Your first 45 days, in order</a><span>When you move here for good, you have 45 days to get a South Carolina driver's license and 45 days to register your car here.</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/common-mistakes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The buyer mistakes that cost the most</a></li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Not sure which town fits your move?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us how you want to live and where you will work. We send you the towns that fit, and the homes for sale in them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us pick towns for you</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="lead-form"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Contact us">Talk to a local agent about your move</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Leave your name and number. A licensed agent calls you to talk through the towns, the homes and the timing of your move.</p><div id="ldWrap" class="rl-form"><div class="idx-lead"><input class="idx-input" id="ldName" placeholder="Your name" aria-label="Your name" autocomplete="name"><input class="idx-input" id="ldPhone" placeholder="Phone" aria-label="Phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel"></div><div class="idx-lead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><input class="idx-input" id="ldEmail" placeholder="Email (optional)" aria-label="Email (optional)" type="email" autocomplete="email"></div><div class="idx-lead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr"><textarea class="idx-input" id="ldNote" rows="3" placeholder="Where you are moving from, and when (optional)" aria-label="Where you are moving from, and when (optional)"></textarea></div><label class="rl-consent"><input type="checkbox" id="ldConsent"><span>I consent to receive calls and text messages from Chapter 3 Realty about my property inquiry, showing appointments, and listing information I requested, at the phone number provided, including calls placed using an automated system or an artificial or prerecorded voice. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help, STOP to opt out. Consent is not a condition of any purchase.</span></label><p id="ldErr" class="rl-err" role="alert"></p><button type="button" class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" onclick="ldSubmit()">Talk to us about your move</button><p class="rl-tel">Prefer to talk now?</p><a class="btn btn-outline rl-call" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div><div id="ldOk" class="rl-ok">Thanks. A local agent will call you about your move.</div><script>function ldSubmit(){var n=document.getElementById('ldName').value.trim(),ph=document.getElementById('ldPhone').value.trim(),em=document.getElementById('ldEmail').value.trim(),nt=document.getElementById('ldNote').value.trim(),c=document.getElementById('ldConsent').checked,err=document.getElementById('ldErr');function fail(m){err.textContent=m;err.style.display='block';}err.style.display='none';if(!n||!ph){fail('Add your name and a phone number so we can call you.');return;}if(!c){fail('Check the consent box to send the request.');return;}c3SendForm({name:n,phone:ph,email:em,message:'Relocation enquiry. '+nt,consent:c?'yes':'no'},'Relocating page');document.getElementById('ldWrap').style.display='none';document.getElementById('ldOk').style.display='block';}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="questions-about-relocating"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Questions about relocating</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I sign my closing papers on a video call?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not with a South Carolina notary. South Carolina law has no remote (video) notarization. Ask your closing attorney how you will sign.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who picks the closing attorney?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You do, when you buy with a home loan for personal or family use. The lender must ask which attorney you want for the closing and follow your choice.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which state do most out-of-state buyers come from?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Carolina, by far. Our count of Horry County deeds over one year found 916 buyers with a tax bill in North Carolina. New York was next, with 438.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I move to Myrtle Beach before I have a job here?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Most of our buyers who move here find work within a month or two. That is our clients' experience, not a promise.</p><p style=