ofs of your new South Carolina address, from two different organizations, dated within nine months</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">: a lease or closing statement, a utility bill or approved application for service, a bank statement, an insurance bill, a pay stub, or the Postal Service change-of-address confirmation. One proof gets you a standard license; two get you a REAL ID at the same price.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">Your out-of-state driver&#39;s license.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">You surrender it.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">The name of an auto insurer licensed in South Carolina.</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">Switch your policy before the DMV visit; the county wants it too.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">For each vehicle</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6">the current out-of-state registration or title, and the lienholder&#39;s name if there is a loan.</span></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(150px,220px) 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:.85rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--sans)"><span style="font-size:.86rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.5">If married</span><span style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--