uto}.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:640px}.c3-aerial-ctop .c3ph-cr{top:0;bottom:auto;padding:.35rem .6rem 1.6rem 2.6rem;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 0%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0))}@media (max-width:699px){.c3ph-cards>:last-child:nth-child(odd){grid-column:1/-1}}.c3-maps{display:grid;gap:0 1.5rem;max-width:1136px}@media (min-width:900px){.c3-maps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-maps figure{max-width:none!important;margin:1.4rem 0 .4rem!important}.c3-maps svg,.c3-maps img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.c3-map-links{row-gap:0!important}.c3-map-links a{padding:.55rem 0}ul[role=list][style*="minmax(13rem,1fr)"]{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(13rem,100%),1fr))!important}</style><style>.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero,.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:760px}</style><style>main#main .c3-rc{list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(19rem,100%),1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px}main#main .c3-rc li{margin:0;min-width:0;padding:1rem 1.05rem 1.05rem;border-radius:18px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.78),rgba(255,255,255,.55));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.8);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.9),0 10px 28px -16px rgba(28,32,40,.35)}main#main .c3-rc .q{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .45rem}main#main .c3-rc .q .i{flex:none;display:flex;width:2.3rem;height:2.3rem;border-radius:50%;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--brass-ink);background:rgba(196,120,58,.12)}main#main .c3-rc .a{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0}@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:reduce){main#main .c3-rc li{background:#fbf8f3}}</style><style>main#main .c3w-map{max-width:760px}main#main .c3w-map figure{margin:1.2rem 0 .5rem!important}main#main .c3w-key{list-style:none;margin:0 0 1.2rem;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.35rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.4;color:var(--navy)}main#main .c3w-key li{margin:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.45rem}main#main .c3w-key b{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:1.5rem;height:1.5rem;border-radius:50%;background:#fff;border:1.5px solid var(--navy);font-size:.85rem}main#main .c3w-states{list-style:none;margin:.4rem 0 1.2rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(9rem,100%),1fr));gap:.2rem 1rem}main#main .c3w-states li{margin:0;padding:.3rem 0}</style><style>.c3-glance{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(var(--n),minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px}.c3-glance li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;margin:0;padding:.5rem .6rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;line-height:1.25}.c3-glance .i{flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;width:2rem;height:2rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center}.c3-glance strong{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:.9rem;font-weight:500}.c3-glance span.t{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:1rem}@media (max-width:699px){.c3-glance{gap:.3rem}.c3-glance li{flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-start;text-align:center;gap:.2rem;padding:.4rem .1rem}.c3-glance .i{width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem}.c3-glance strong{font-size:.875rem}.c3-glance span.t{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.2}}</style><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>Growth</strong><span class="t">22% since 2020</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Born in another state</strong><span class="t">6 in 10</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>January high</strong><span class="t">About 56°F</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Movers come to Horry County for the beach and the water, a short and mild winter, a lower home price and a low property tax.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most households moving to Myrtle Beach and the rest of Horry County come from another state. In most of the out-of-state counties that send the most, a typical home costs more than one here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They come for the beach and the water, a short winter and, for most out-of-state movers, a much lower property tax bill. In the latest count, about 15,000 households moved in and about 9,100 moved out.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Find out what the money from your house buys here.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask us what it buys</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#four-reasons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The four reasons</a></li><li><a href="#life-here" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Life here</a></li><li><a href="#still-growing" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Still growing?</a></li><li><a href="#overcrowded" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Overcrowded?</a></li><li><a href="#where-from" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where from</a></li><li><a href="#what-your-house-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What your house buys</a></li><li><a href="#jobs-and-pay" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Jobs and pay</a></li><li><a href="#taxes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Taxes and insurance</a></li><li><a href="#why-people-leave" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who leaves, and why</a></li><li><a href="#should-you-move" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Should you move?</a></li><li><a href="#moving-to-myrtle-beach-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Moving to Myrtle Beach FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="four-reasons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The four reasons">Why are so many people moving to Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The City of Myrtle Beach is in Horry County, South Carolina, and the coast here is called the Grand Strand. People move here for the beach and the water, a short winter, lower house prices and low property tax.</p><ul class="c3-rc" role="list"><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span>The beach and the water</span></p><p class="a">The ocean still averages the low 70s in October. Behind the beach towns are the Intracoastal Waterway, the Waccamaw River and the Murrells Inlet marsh, each with public boat landings.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span>The winter is short and mild</span></p><p class="a">A January day averages a high of about 56 degrees and a low of about 37. Snow averages about an inch a year, and about two winters in three bring none.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span>A house costs less than in most places movers leave</span></p><p class="a">A typical home in Horry County is valued at about $320,000. Around Charlotte it is about $415,000, and on Long Island about $730,000 or more.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span>The property tax is low</span></p><p class="a">An owner who lives in the home here typically pays about $944 a year. On Long Island the typical bill is $10,000 or more.</p></li></ul><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/myrtle-beach-beach-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/myrtle-beach-beach-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/myrtle-beach-beach-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="The wide sand beach, the dunes and the ocean in Myrtle Beach, seen from a high floor" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: 28bytes. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: 28bytes</a></span></div><figcaption>The beach in Myrtle Beach in late November, seen from a high floor.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="life-here"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Life here">What do people do in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown, the Boardwalk is about 1.3 miles long, beside the ocean, with a raised wooden walk and a paved path along the sand.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The wide beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, with the SkyWheel, rows of blue umbrellas and towers along the shore" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0. License: CC BY-SA 2.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 2.0">Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0</a></span></div><figcaption>The beach downtown, by the SkyWheel on the Boardwalk.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet is known for seafood. Its restaurants grew from the oyster roasts of the inlet's founding families. The MarshWalk there is a half-mile wooden boardwalk on the salt marsh, with restaurants and free live music.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From October through May, anyone with a South Carolina saltwater fishing license may gather oysters and clams on the inlet's public grounds. Parts of the grounds close at times for bacteria.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/murrells-inlet-boats-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="759" alt="White fishing boats tied up at a marina on calm water in Murrells Inlet, South Carolina" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pollinator. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Pollinator</a></span></div><figcaption>Fishing boats tied up in Murrells Inlet.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inland, Conway's Riverwalk follows the Waccamaw River for about 1.5 miles, with a kayak launch and a public boat landing beside it.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing, shaded by trees, beside old wooden buildings in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The Riverwalk in Conway, beside the old riverfront warehouses on the Waccamaw River.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Intracoastal Waterway in Carolina Forest, the county's Bike and Run Park has about 7 miles of trails. Huntington Beach State Park, south of Murrells Inlet, has 3 miles of beach and a freshwater lake known for alligators.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach's first golf course, Pine Lakes, opened in 1927. Anyone who lives or owns a home in Horry County can buy the Myrtle Beach Golf Passport for $72 a year. It gives member rates at the courses that take it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The off season is quieter, not closed: in our team's experience, only the tourist attractions and water parks close in winter. One mover from Maryland noticed that farm stands and butchers fill the gap the grocery stores leave in organic food.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="still-growing"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Still growing?">Is Myrtle Beach still growing?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Horry County grew about 22 percent from the 2020 census to the latest estimate. The growth is people moving in: in the latest year, about 39 more people a day arrived from other parts of the country than left.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="People living in Horry County, now and projected"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">People living in Horry County, now and projected</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">When</span><span role="columnheader">people</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2020 census</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.675" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 351,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Latest estimate</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.822" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 427,600</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2030, projected</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.952" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 495,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Census Bureau counts. The 2030 figure is South Carolina's own projection, not a count.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Among the country's metro areas, the Myrtle Beach area, which is all of Horry County, grew the second fastest from mid-2024 to mid-2025. Only Ocala, Florida grew faster.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="overcrowded"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Overcrowded?">Is Myrtle Beach getting overcrowded?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of the growth is not in the beach towns. The City of Myrtle Beach itself has about 41,000 people. About three in four Horry County residents live outside any city or town.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About four in five of the people added since 2020 settled outside city limits, in places such as Carolina Forest, Socastee, Murrells Inlet and Little River.</p><div class="c3w-map"><figure style="margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:760px"><svg style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-the-city-of-myrtle-beach" viewBox="0 0 360 324" width="360" height="324" role="img" aria-label="Map of the Grand Strand from Little River to Murrells Inlet, with the ocean, the Intracoastal Waterway and the main roads. Five outlines are numbered: 1, the City of Myrtle Beach along the coast; 2, Carolina Forest; 3, Socastee; 4, Murrells Inlet; 5, Little River, all four outside any city." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec