ng>Beach</strong><span class="t">4 to 15 min</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M16 10h4a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-4l-4 7H9l2-7H7l-2 2H3l2-4-2-4h2l2 2h4L9 3h3z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Nonstops</strong><span class="t">50+ cities</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Retire here and pay no state tax on Social Security. Each 55+ community on this page is 3 to 10 minutes from a hospital.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A retired couple on Social Security and a modest pension can owe no South Carolina income tax. Property tax here is lowest on a home you live in full time. Outside the city limits, a $400,000 house you live in is taxed about $1,290 a year at 65, with the $50,000 exemption. That exemption takes the first $50,000 of the home's value off the tax.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The four 55+ communities on this page are 4 to 15 minutes by car from the beach. Homes in them usually sell for about $300,000 in Myrtle Trace to about $665,000 for a house in Del Webb at Grande Dunes.</p><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#good-place-to-retire" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Good place to retire?</a></li><li><a href="#retired-life" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">A retired week</a></li><li><a href="#communities" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">55+ communities</a></li><li><a href="#hospitals" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Hospitals</a></li><li><a href="#hurricanes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Hurricanes and flooding</a></li><li><a href="#weather" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Weather</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly cost at 65</a></li><li><a href="#income-tax" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Income tax</a></li><li><a href="#retiring-to-myrtle-beach-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Retiring to Myrtle Beach FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="good-place-to-retire"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Good place to retire?">Is Myrtle Beach a good place to retire?</h2><style>main#main .c3-glance li{line-height:1.4}@media (min-width:700px){main#main .detail-h1{text-wrap:balance}}main#main .detail-h1 em{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.5vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:.55rem;text-wrap:balance}@media (max-width:959px){main#main .detail-h1 em{color:#8a5226!important}}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2){padding:.9rem 0 1.4rem!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{display:block!important;text-align:center!important;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.96),rgba(28,32,40,.98))!important;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14)!important;border-radius:28px!important;padding:2.2rem 1.6rem!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap>h2{color:var(--ivory)!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap>p{color:rgba(244,239,232,.82)!important}@media (max-width:699px){main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{padding:1.6rem 1.2rem 1.7rem!important;border-radius:24px!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap>h2{font-size:1.5rem!important;line-height:1.25}}main#main .hx-feed .hx-fb,main#main .hx-feed .hx-fb-ai,main#main .hx-feed .hx-fb-q{min-width:0!important;max-width:100%!important;box-sizing:border-box}@media (min-width:1000px) and (max-width:1120px){.header-ctas .hdr-phone-num{display:none}}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 128,700 people in Horry County are 65 or older, about 3 in 10 residents. In South Carolina and in the U.S. as a whole, it is about 2 in 10. Whether it suits you depends most on how you will use the home.</p><style>main#main .c3-decide{list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(17rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:880px}main#main .c3-decide li{margin:0;padding:1rem 1.05rem 1.05rem;border-radius:18px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.78),rgba(255,255,255,.55));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.8);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.9),0 10px 28px -16px rgba(28,32,40,.35)}main#main .c3-decide .q{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.6rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.4;margin:0 0 .45rem}main#main .c3-decide .q .i{flex:none;display:flex;width:2.3rem;height:2.3rem;border-radius:50%;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:var(--brass-ink);background:rgba(196,120,58,.12)}main#main .c3-decide .a{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0}@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:reduce){main#main .c3-decide li{background:#fbf8f3}}</style><ul class="c3-decide" role="list"><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span>If you will live here most of the year</span></p><p class="a">Apply for the lower tax rate on a home you live in, called the 4 percent rate, as soon as you close. At 65, apply for the $50,000 exemption too: it takes $50,000 off the value you are taxed on.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span>If it will be a second home for a few years first</span></p><p class="a">A second home pays the higher rate: about $4,820 a year on a $400,000 house, until it becomes your legal home.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span>If you live on Social Security and a modest pension</span></p><p class="a">You may owe no South Carolina income tax. The <a href="#income-tax" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">calculator below</a> works out yours.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span>If you want to live near the beach</span></p><p class="a">Each of the four 55+ communities below is 4 to 15 minutes by car from the beach.</p></li><li><p class="q"><span class="i" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8.5h10.5a3 3 0 1 0-3-3M3 12.5h15a3 3 0 1 1-3 3M3 16.5h6"/></svg></span><span>If you would rather not plan a hurricane evacuation</span></p><p class="a">Three of the four 55+ communities are outside every hurricane evacuation zone.</p></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="retired-life"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="A retired week">What is a retired week like in Myrtle Beach?</h2><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}.c3ph-gal{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:1.5rem;margin:1.6rem 0;padding:0;list-style:none}.c3ph-gal>figure{margin:0;min-width:0}.c3ph-gal img{aspect-ratio:var(--c3ph-r,4/3)}.c3ph-gal figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.45;margin-top:.5rem}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-gal{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(var(--c3ph-n,3),minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;overflow:visible;padding:0}.c3ph-gal>figure{min-width:0}}@media (max-width:699px){.c3ph-gal.c3ph-row{display:flex;gap:.75rem;padding:0 var(--c3ph-bleed,1.4rem) .4rem;margin:1.6rem calc(-1*var(--c3ph-bleed,1.4rem)) 0;overflow-x:auto;scroll-snap-type:x mandatory;scroll-padding:0 var(--c3ph-bleed,1.4rem);-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;scrollbar-width:none}.c3ph-row::-webkit-scrollb