5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>45%</strong><span class="t">of paid Florence claims were insured outside FEMA's zone</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Five checks show it: FEMA's claim records, two flood maps, the county's records, repair permits and the house itself. You get all five for any house you send.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA's records of flood insurance claims on a house go only to its owner, so we ask the seller for them. We put the house on FEMA's flood map and the county's map of the flooding from Hurricane Florence. We ask the county's staff about past floods and look for permits behind repairs. At the showing, we look for clues at the house and on its street.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We run these checks before you offer. If you learn of a flood after you sign, the South Carolina REALTORS sales contract gives you a due diligence period to end it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Have us check a house's flood history</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us the address</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="checks"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The five checks">How do you find out if a house has flooded before?</h2><style>.c3-uf-steps{list-style:none;counter-reset:s;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.8rem;max-width:760px}.c3-uf-steps>li{background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.8),rgba(255,255,255,.56));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.92);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.85),0 18px 40px -28px rgba(28,32,40,.45);border-radius:20px;counter-increment:s;margin:0;padding:1rem 1.15rem 1rem 4.1rem;position:relative;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.6}.c3-uf-steps>li::before{content:counter(s);position:absolute;left:1rem;top:1rem;width:2.2rem;height:2.2rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--navy);color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.c3-uf-steps .k{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:650;font-size:1.1rem;line-height:1.35;margin:.1rem 0 .4rem}.c3-uf-tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.3;color:var(--navy);background:rgba(255,255,255,.85);border:1px solid rgba(145,89,43,.35);border-radius:999px;padding:.2rem .7rem .2rem .45rem;margin:0 0 .55rem}.c3-uf-tag.own{border-color:rgba(28,32,40,.4)}.c3-uf-tag span{display:inline-flex;color:var(--brass)}.c3-uf-tag.own span{color:var(--navy)}.c3-uf-steps p{margin:0 0 .5rem}.c3-uf-steps p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.c3-uf-steps .miss{border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.12);padding-top:.5rem;margin-top:.6rem;font-size:1rem}.c3-uf-steps .miss b{color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:650}.c3-uf-steps a{color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline}@media (max-width:519px){.c3-uf-steps>li{padding: