+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is an HOA the same as a POA in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Under the South Carolina Homeowners Association Act, the name does not matter. A group is an HOA when papers filed with the county make the owners pay it dues, except a timeshare plan."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a POA put a lien on my house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if its papers filed with the county give it a lien for unpaid dues, as an HOA's papers can. That is a claim on your house for the unpaid dues. About one in five of the more than 500 associations that recorded a lien for unpaid charges in Horry County in 2025 had \"property owners\" or \"POA\" in the name."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a POA voluntary in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only when no papers filed with the county make the owners pay it. A group with no such papers, such as a voluntary civic club, is not an HOA under South Carolina's HOA Act. If the papers on your home make you pay, the dues are not voluntary, whatever the group calls itself."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a regime fee in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The condo fee. South Carolina's condo law calls a condo a horizontal property regime, so the fee its owners pay is called a regime fee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What do I own in a condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your unit alone, plus a share of the shared parts, given as a percentage in the condo's founding papers. No owner can force the shared parts to be split up, and selling a unit sells its share with it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a home have two HOAs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A home in a master-planned community can belong to a master association and to a neighborhood or condo association inside it, each with its own papers and fee. Grande Dunes, Barefoot Resort and Prince Creek each have more than one association."}}]}</script>
