+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/hoa/">HOA Guide</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">HOA vs POA</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">HOA Guide</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Is a POA the same as an HOA in South Carolina?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Fees by kind of home, and why some homes pay two associations.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Yes. In South Carolina law they are the same. Also what you own in a Grand Strand condo, who fixes the roof, and how a condo can change the loan.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. In South Carolina, a property owners association (POA) and a homeowners association (HOA) are the same thing in law. Under the South Carolina Homeowners Association Act, a group is an HOA when papers filed with the county make the owners pay it dues.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The kind of home changes the fee. On the Grand Strand, the typical fee on a condo for sale is about $650 a month, and on a house about $95. Condo owners share the building, and the association insures it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us an address. We find every association it belongs to.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us check a property</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#hoa-vs-poa" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HOA vs POA</a></li><li><a href="#condo-vs-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Condo vs house</a></li><li><a href="#what-you-own" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What you own</a></li><li><a href="#regime-fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Regime fees</a></li><li><a href="#two-associations" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Two associations</a></li><li><a href="#surprises" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Surprises</a></li><li><a href="#what-we-check" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What we check</a></li><li><a href="#loans" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Loans</a></li><li><a href="#pros-and-cons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Pros and cons</a></li><li><a href="#hoa-vs-poa-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HOA vs POA questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="hoa-vs-poa"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="HOA vs POA">What is the difference between an HOA and a POA?</h2><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.95);--g-sh:0 1px 2px rgba(28,32,40,.05),0 14px 36px -20px rgba(28,32,40,.3);--g-r:20px;--g-blur:saturate(150%) blur(16px);background-color:#f8f4ee;background-image:radial-gradient(44rem 26rem at 4% 460px,rgba(232,201,154,.30),rgba(232,201,154,0) 70%),radial-gradient(40rem 26rem at 98% 1000px,rgba(196,120,58,.08),rgba(196,120,58,0) 70%),radial-gradient(46rem 26rem at 16% 1500px,rgba(232,201,154,.22),rgba(232,201,154,0) 70%),radial-gradient(40rem 24rem at 94% 1960px,rgba(42,48,64,.045),rgba(42,48,64,0) 70%);background-size:100% 2400px;background-repeat:repeat-y}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"],main#main .detail-hero{background:transparent!important}main#main .detail-hero{border-bottom:0}main#main .detail-hero.bg-grid{background-image:none}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]+section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]{border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.7)}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]{padding-bottom:2.25rem}main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]:not(.detail-hero+section){padding-top:2.25rem}@media (min-width:700px){main#main>section[style*="background:var(--ivory"]{padding-bottom:3.5rem}main#main>sectio