n><strong>Your unit flood policy</strong><span class="t">About $495 a year</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 8.5h10.5a3 3 0 1 0-3-3M3 12.5h15a3 3 0 1 1-3 3M3 16.5h6"/></svg></span><span><strong>Example share, 5% storm deductible</strong><span class="t">About $6,500</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The building's policy, your own HO-6, the storm deductible and flood, with Fannie Mae's rules and FEMA's numbers for Horry County condos.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The condo building's master policy, paid through your condo fee, insures the structure and the shared areas. Your HO-6 insures your belongings, your liability, and whatever the master policy leaves out inside your unit.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On this coast, ask first for the building's storm deductible. For a typical Horry condo building of 10 or more units, a 5 percent storm deductible split evenly would come to about $6,500 for each owner. A basic condo policy pays only a small set amount toward that bill, unless you buy a higher limit.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Name the building. We read its insurance papers with you.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us read the papers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#difference" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The two policies</a></li><li><a href="#inside" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Inside your unit</a></li><li><a href="#mortgage" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HO-6 for a mortgage</a></li><li><a href="#deductible" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The storm deductible</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood</a></li><li><a href="#before-you-buy" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Before you buy</a></li><li><a href="#master-policy-and-ho-6-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Master policy and HO-6 FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="difference"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The two policies">What is the difference between a condo master policy and an HO-6?</h2><style>@media (min-width:700px){main#main .detail-h1{text-wrap:balance}}main#main .detail-h1 em{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.5vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:.55rem;text-wrap:balance}@media (max-width:959px){main#main .detail-h1 em{color:var(--g-ink,#8a5226)!important}}main#main .c3-glance li{line-height:1.4}main#main .c3-glance span.t{line-height:1.3}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-glance{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)!important;gap:0!important}main#main .c3-glance li{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;flex-direction:row!important;text-align:left!important;justify-content:flex-start!important;align-items:center!important;gap:.7rem!important;padding:.55rem 0!important}main#main .c3-glance li:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main .c3-glance li>span:last-child{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:.1rem;flex:1;min-width:0}main#main .c3-glance strong{font-size:1rem!important;flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0}main#main .c3-glance span.t{white-space:nowrap;flex:0 0 auto}}main#main h2{text-wrap:balance}main#main .sr{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}main#main .c3-ins-tab{max-width:720px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem}main#main .c3-ins-tab table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem}main#main .c3-ins-tab th,main#main .c3-ins-tab td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:.6rem .8rem .6rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid r