-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/hoa/south-carolina-hoa-laws/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the South Carolina Homeowners Association Act?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A 2018 law, S.C. Code Title 27 Chapter 30, that applies to communities and horizontal property regimes where owners must pay assessments. It requires governing documents to be recorded to be enforceable, sets certain meeting notice requirements, gives owners access to the budget and membership list, and requires the Department of Consumer Affairs to collect HOA complaint data."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who regulates HOAs in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No agency regulates them in the way most owners expect. The Department of Consumer Affairs collects HOA complaints because the statute requires it and publishes an annual report, but it does not administer or enforce the Act. Its process is voluntary mediation and it cannot compel participation or dictate an outcome."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I complain about my HOA to the state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can file a complaint with the South Carolina Department of Consumer Affairs, and it will be counted in the annual report. Understand what it is: voluntary mediation. In the 2026 report only about one percent of complainants were recorded as satisfied with the outcome."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do HOA governing documents have to be recorded in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Under the Act, governing documents must be recorded in the public records of the county where the property sits to be enforceable, and associations existing when the law took effect were given a deadline to record."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does an HOA have to give notice before raising the budget?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only some must. An HOA that is not a nonprofit corporation must give homeowners notice at least 48 hours before the meeting at which a decision to increase the annual budget is made. An HOA incorporated as a nonprofit follows its bylaws instead, and state law requires no notice to owners before its board meets."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a seller have to disclose an HOA in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The residential property condition disclosure requires a seller to disclose that the property is governed by a homeowners association."}}]}</script>
