e-height:1.55;margin:1.1rem 0 0;padding:0}@media (max-width:699px){.c3-gchart{padding:1rem .95rem .9rem}.c3-gchart .b{width:calc((100% - 6.2rem) * var(--f))}}</style><style>.c3-glance{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(var(--n),minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px}.c3-glance li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;margin:0;padding:.5rem .6rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;line-height:1.25}.c3-glance .i{flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;width:2rem;height:2rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center}.c3-glance strong{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:.9rem;font-weight:500}.c3-glance span.t{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:1rem}@media (max-width:699px){.c3-glance{gap:.3rem}.c3-glance li{flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-start;text-align:center;gap:.2rem;padding:.4rem .1rem}.c3-glance .i{width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem}.c3-glance strong{font-size:.875rem}.c3-glance span.t{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.2}}</style><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>No cap on fines</strong><span class="t">in the HOA Act or the condo law</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>About 700</strong><span class="t">association papers recorded in Horry County in the past 12 months</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>10 of 416</strong><span class="t">Horry County complaints ended with the owner satisfied</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The three state laws, the rules they leave to each community's recorded papers, and how Horry County's 416 HOA complaints to the state ended.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina has no one complete law on how an HOA must run. Under the 2018 HOA Act, an HOA's papers must be recorded at the county to be enforced, and money disputes up to $7,500 can go to magistrate court.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fines, dues limits, rental rules and developer turnover are not in South Carolina HOA laws. Your community's recorded papers have those rules. Consumer Affairs records complaints, but the law bars it from acting as a referee.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying into an HOA? We read its recorded papers before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask us about a community</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#laws" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The laws</a></li><li><a href="#which-law" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which applies</a></li><li><a href="#other-states" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Other states</a></li><li><a href="#unenforceable" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Unenforceable rules</a></li><li><a href="#records" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Records and meetings</a></li><li><a href="#who-enforces" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who enforces</a></li><li><a href="#complaint" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Complaints</a></li><li><a href="#changes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Changes</a></li><li><a href="#south-carolina-hoa-law-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">South Carolina HOA law FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="laws"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The laws">What are South Carolina's HOA laws?</h2><style>@media (min-width:700px){main#main .detail-h1{text-wrap:balance}}main#main .detail-h1 em{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.5vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:.55rem;text-wrap:balance}@media (max-width:959px){main#main .detail-h1 em{color:var(--g-ink,#8a5226)!important}}main#main .c3-glance li{line-height:1.4}main#main .c3-glance span.t{line-height:1.3}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-glance{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)!important;gap:0!important}main#main .c3-glance li{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;flex-direction:row!important;text-align:left!important;justify-content:flex-start!important;align-items:center!important;gap:.7rem!important;padding:.55rem 0!important}main#main .c3-glance li:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main .c3-glance li>span:last-child{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.05rem;flex:1;min-width:0}main#main .c3-glance strong{font-size:1rem!important}}main#main h2{text-wrap:balance}main#main .c3-sl-tab{max-width:720px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.4rem}main#main .c3-sl-tab table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--navy);font-size: