"/></svg></span><span><strong>$7,800 a year</strong><span class="t">deductible on a condo rented all year at the middle Horry County dues</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><span><strong>About 11 times</strong><span class="t">a year of dues against the property tax on a Myrtle Beach condo its owner lives in</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">On a Horry County condo with the middle HOA fees of $650 a month, the nights you rent it decide how much is deductible.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HOA fees on a home you live in are not tax deductible. On a condo or house you rent out, the dues are a rental expense, taken off the rent on Schedule E, the IRS form for rental income.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you rent it out and also stay there, you deduct the rented share. Divide the nights rented at a fair price by those nights plus your personal nights. The same rules on dues apply on the South Carolina return.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Looking at a condo? Get its dues and what they include before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us check the dues</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#the-answer" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The answer by how you use the home</a></li><li><a href="#rented-share" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your rented share</a></li><li><a href="#dues-by-area" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Dues by area</a></li><li><a href="#property-tax" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">HOA fees and property tax</a></li><li><a href="#special-assessments" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Special assessments</a></li><li><a href="#south-carolina" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">South Carolina and owners out of state</a></li><li><a href="#schedule-e" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 