-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The expense stack</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Myrtle Beach short-term rental expenses, line by line</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.2rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:760px"><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Management: 20 to 30 percent</strong> for a full-service offsite manager, 10 to 15 for booking-only services, and 35 to 45 percent on an onsite condotel rental desk. Travel-agent commissions and program fees push the effective condotel split higher. This one line changes the result more than any rate or occupancy assumption.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">HOA dues: $400 to $1,200 a month</strong> on oceanfront towers, usually covering water, cable, internet, pool, and the building's wind insurance, and often electric in condotels. Coastal master-policy premiums pushed many buildings' dues up 15 to 30 percent over the past two years.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Property tax at the 6 percent rate,</strong> plus the school operating tax. The math and a calculator are on our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax page</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Insurance at two to three times a standard homeowner policy</strong> for STR use, roughly $2,000 to $3,000 a year on a house before wind and flood, which cost more near the beach.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Platform fees: budget 15.5 percent for Airbnb in 2026,</strong> not the old 3 percent. Airbnb is migrating hosts to a host-only fee this year; Vrbo's pay-per-booking model charges about 8 percent in total.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Licenses and lodging taxes:</strong> a business license in every jurisdiction, and roughly 13 percent in guest-paid lodging taxes that Airbnb mostly collects and remits. The full stack, city by city, is in our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">short-term rental rules guide</a>.</span></li></ul><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:1.5rem;margin-top:1.75rem"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.6rem">What management costs, and why two quotes are rarely comparable</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:.9rem">Management is the biggest single variable in what you keep, and the Grand Strand has two models. Hands-off, all-in management, where the company handles marketing, guest communication, accounting, taxes, maintenance and repairs, costs about <strong style="color:var(--navy)">40 to 60 percent of gross profit</strong>. You do nothing and you keep the rest.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:.9rem">A basic plan covering marketing, guest communication and basic accounting, with condition and financial reporting; repairs and tax help billed separately on request, costs about <strong style="color:var(--navy)">12.62 to 17.45 percent of gross profit</strong>. The difference is not service quality, it is how much of the work stays with you.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin:0">Before you compare two quotes, ask each manager which model they are pricing and what the percentage is taken from. A number quoted on gross bookings and a number quoted on gross profit are not the same number. <span style="font-size:.82rem">Ranges we observe on the Grand Strand as of 2026-08-15, not a quoted price.</span></p></div></div></section>
