div role="table" aria-label="Murrells Inlet's average Airbnb took in nearly twice the Myrtle Beach area's"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Murrells Inlet's average Airbnb took in nearly twice the Myrtle Beach area's</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, the homes</span><span role="columnheader">a year from guests</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/">Murrells Inlet</a></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">most listings are houses</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$47,603</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/">Surfside Beach</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.901" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$42,902</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/garden-city/">Garden City Beach</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.866" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$41,223</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/">North Myrtle Beach</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.723" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$34,401</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/">Pawleys Island</a></span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.66" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$31,430</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/">Myrtle Beach area</a></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">4 in 5 listings are condos</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.542" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$25,807</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/conway/">Conway</a></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">few listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.492" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$23,426</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n"><a href="/submarkets/little-river/">Little River</a></span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">few listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.314" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$14,963</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>What the average Airbnb took in over a year, all sizes: money from guests, cleaning fees included, before any cost. AirROI, 12 months to September 2026. Its areas do not follow city limits.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The gap between towns is mostly the kind of home, as the labels show. For a two-bedroom alone, Murrells Inlet took in only about a tenth more than the Myrtle Beach area.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-tools/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/invest-str-tools/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-and-houses-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/invest-str-tools/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-and-houses-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Four oceanfront towers with balconies and pools behind the dune in Myrtle Beach, with streets of houses and woods behind them, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, with streets of houses behind them, seen from over the ocean.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average Myrtle Beach area listing was booked on about 36 percent of the nights it was open. AirROI has no Airbnb market for Carolina Forest, which is inland.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="by-size"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="By size">How much does a two-, three- or four-bedroom Airbnb make in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For two- and three-bedroom homes, seven of the eight towns are close; Little River takes in less. An average three-bedroom took in about $28,000 to $39,000 a year in those seven.</p><span class="ai-cap" id="ai-size-cap">What the average Airbnb took in a year, by bedrooms</span><table class="ai-sz" aria-labelledby="ai-size-cap"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Town</th><th scope="col">2 bedrooms</th><th scope="col">3 bedrooms</th><th scope="col">4 bedrooms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Murrells Inlet</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$27,900</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$32,900</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$58,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Surfside Beach</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$22,800</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$33,600</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$73,300</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Garden City Beach</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$26,900</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$38,700</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$54,900*</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">North Myrtle Beach</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$20,700</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$29,700</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$47,800</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pawleys Island</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$22,900</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$27,800</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$41,600</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Myrtle Beach area</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$25,100</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$37,100</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$57,400</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Conway</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$24,000*</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$31,500*</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>none</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Little River</th><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">2 bedrooms</span>$11,800</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">3 bedrooms</span>$19,100</td><td><span class="l" aria-hidden="true">4 bedrooms</span>$31,300*</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="ai-note">Condos and houses together, cleaning fees included, before any cost. * Fewer than thirty listings. Conway has no four-bedroom listings in the data.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is the average Airbnb income the typical result?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle two-bedroom listing takes in less than the average two-bedroom in every town, because listings that take in far more than most raise the average. In North Myrtle Beach the middle one took in about $15,000, against an average of $21,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Murrells Inlet the two are within about 1 percent. In the other seven towns the middle two-bedroom took in 12 to 31 percent less than the average. Both figures also count part-year listings.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much more does a bigger home take in?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Bigger homes take in far more. An average listing with four bedrooms or more took in about two to four times what a two-bedroom took in, in the same town. In Garden City Beach the average five-bedroom or larger took in about $98,000.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="str-garden-city-beach-houses" data-name="Garden City Beach" data-head="Houses for sale in Garden City Beach"></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want homes where nightly stays are allowed?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the town and the bedrooms. We send homes for sale there and leave out the ones whose zoning or building rules ban nightly stays.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send me homes for nightly rentals</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="by-month"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="By month">How much does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb make each month?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a typical month, the middle Myrtle Beach area Airbnb took in $2,530 from guests. The middle half of listings took in $1,270 to $4,330, and the top tenth $6,770 or more.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">A Myrtle Beach Airbnb takes in about five times as much in July as in January</span><svg class="ai-cols" viewBox="0 0 360 230" role="img" aria-label="Column chart of what the average Myrtle Beach area Airbnb took in from guests in each month: January $1,300, February $1,700, March $2,500, April $2,800, May $3,300, June $6,100, July $6,800, August $4,400, September $2,600, October $2,200, November $1,600, December $1,600."><line x1="58" x2="354" y1="196" y2="196" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35"/><text x="52" y="201" text-anchor="end">$0</text><line x1="58" x2="354" y1="124.9" y2="124.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="52" y="129.9" text-anchor="end">$3k</text><line x1="58" x2="354" y1="53.7" y2="53.7" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".12"/><text x="52" y="58.7" text-anchor="end">$6k</text><rect x="61.5" y="164.2" width="17.8" height="31.8" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="70.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="74" y="156.2" text-anchor="middle">$1,300</text><rect x="86.1" y="156.2" width="17.8" height="39.8" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="95" y="218" text-anchor="middle">F</text><rect x="110.8" y="136" width="17.8" height="60" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="119.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="135.5" y="129.6" width="17.8" height="66.4" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="144.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="160.1" y="118.5" width="17.8" height="77.5" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="169" y="218" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="184.8" y="52.1" width="17.8" height="143.9" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="193.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="209.5" y="34.7" width="17.8" height="161.3" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="218.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><text class="v" x="218.3" y="26.7" text-anchor="middle">$6,800</text><rect x="234.1" y="91.7" width="17.8" height="104.3" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="243" y="218" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="258.8" y="135.5" width="17.8" height="60.5" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="267.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="283.5" y="145" width="17.8" height="51" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="292.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">O</text><rect x="308.1" y="157.6" width="17.8" height="38.4" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="317" y="218" text-anchor="middle">N</text><rect x="332.8" y="158.3" width="17.8" height="37.7" rx="3" fill="#dcc0a3"/><text x="341.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">D</text></svg><figcaption>Average from guests per Myrtle Beach area listing open that month, over the last two years. AirROI. The darker columns are June, July and August.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">June, July and August bring in 47 percent of a year's income in the Myrtle Beach area. Pawleys Island's June, July and August bring the smallest share of its year, 37 percent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The monthly figures count only listings open that month. The yearly average is lower than a typical month would suggest, because it also counts part-year listings. A long winter stay with one guest is a <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">mid-term rental</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="managers"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Managers">What does an Airbnb manager take in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Vacation rental managers here that publish their fees charge 10 to 25 percent of the booking.</p><ul class="ai-list"><li><b>A basic plan</b><span>In what we have seen here, a basic plan costs about 13 to 17 percent. It covers marketing, guest messages and basic accounting.</span></li><li><b>Full service</b><span>It adds taxes, maintenance and repairs, and is priced as a share of the profit.</span></li><li><b>A resort's rental program</b><span>One large oceanfront resort in Myrtle Beach took 38.6 percent of gross rental income on its 2017 terms, before its other charges. Our page on <a href="/invest/rental-program-vs-airbnb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a rental program or Airbnb</a> compares the two.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you will not be here, a manager or a cleaner you trust matters. The worst short-term rental mistake we see here is an owner running it alone with the cheapest cleaner. Theft and damage followed. Our page on <a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property management</a> covers hiring a manager.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="worth-it"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Worth it?">Is an Airbnb in Myrtle Beach a good investment?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An Airbnb here can pay, when the HOA fee is low or the home is open all year. At the nights the average listing books, a two-bedroom condo with a low HOA fee keeps money after its bills. One in a high-fee oceanfront tower keeps money only when it is open all year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/invest/str-tools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb calculator</a> works out what one condo keeps, with its own fee and tax, and the nights it needs to pay its bills. It also covers <a href="/invest/str-tools/#more-hosts" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how many more Airbnbs there are than a year ago</a>.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="str-garden-city-beach-condos" data-name="Garden City Beach" data-head="Best Airbnb opportunities in Garden City Beach"></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What do the busiest Myrtle Beach Airbnbs take in?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A listing at the top-quarter mark in the Myrtle Beach area, run all year, took in about $44,000.</p><p class="ai-story">A friend who ran a hotel in Boston bought three condos in one oceanfront building. They gross about $120,000, roughly half of it profit. He now helps manage fourteen units. These are his real numbers, not a promise.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What should you weigh next?</h3><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Whether a yearly lease would keep more: our page on <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">an Airbnb or a long-term rental</a> compares the same home both ways.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The return on the price: our <a href="/invest/rental-returns/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental returns</a> page works it out by area.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Where nightly stays are allowed: our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules</a> page lists the rules by city.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Weighing an Airbnb against a yearly lease?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the home. We work out what it would keep as a nightly rental and as a yearly lease, side by side.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us compare both</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-beach-airbnb-income-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach Airbnb income questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much does an Airbnb make a month in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a typical month, half of Myrtle Beach area listings took in more than $2,530 from guests, and half took in less. July brings in about five times as much as January.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much does a four-bedroom Airbnb make in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the Myrtle Beach area the average four-bedroom took in about $57,000 a year from guests, before any cost. The average two-bedroom took in about $25,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do these Airbnb income figures include the cleaning fee?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. They are what guests paid, the nightly rate plus the cleaning fee, before Airbnb's fee or any other cost. The cleaning fee pays the cleaner.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What occupancy does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb get?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests booked about 36 percent of the nights the average Myrtle Beach area listing was open. Our Airbnb calculator works out the nights one condo needs to pay its bills.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is there Airbnb income data for Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI has no Airbnb market for Carolina Forest, an inland area, so there is no figure for it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/1857" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb host fees</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County 2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/statmast.php?title=12&chapter=43" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Code 12-43-220</a>, <a href="https://www.mbvacationhomerentals.com/owners-thank-you/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A manager's published fees</a>. Income: AirROI's update of October 1, 2026, for the 12 months to September 2026, with guests' cleaning fees in the income. What a condo keeps: the arithmetic of our Airbnb calculator. Not legal or tax advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, with streets of houses behind them, seen from over the ocean. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blan