-  /* ------------------------------------------------------------------
-     GREEN KEY, ON THE GPU.
-     Measured on this project: keying in canvas 2D costs 50-59ms per frame on
-     a fast desktop, which is ~200ms on the Moto G that PageSpeed emulates -
-     unusable. The same key as a WebGL fragment shader costs 0.10ms. That is
-     the entire reason this is WebGL and not getImageData.
-
-     The key is a chromaticity test, not a colour-distance test: how far green
-     exceeds the larger of red and blue. Call that k. Measured over five real
-     frames of this clip, k splits cleanly: 39.5% of pixels sit below 0.05 (the
-     subject) and 51.5% sit at or above 0.20 (the backdrop), with only 9% in
-     between. Shadowed backdrop lands around 0.15, which is why the upper edge
-     has to come down to 0.15 and not sit at 0.26 - swept against the real
-     frames, 0.06-0.26 left 19.9% of the frame on partial alpha, a green haze,
-     while 0.07-0.15 leaves 1.5% and that residue is the genuine matte edge on
-     the fanning paper.
-
-     It degrades in every direction: no WebGL, no shader, no green file, or a
