+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a condotel in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A condo building run like a hotel. Each unit has its own owner, and the resort or the HOA rents units to vacationers by the night, with guest registration and cleaning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use an FHA loan on a Myrtle Beach condotel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. FHA will not insure a loan on a condotel or approve a building with a required rental pool. None of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory is on HUD's approved condo list."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use a VA loan on a condotel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only for a home you will live in, because a VA buyer certifies that they will move in. At least 6 of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory have an accepted VA record."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a condotel and a non-warrantable condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every condotel is non-warrantable, but not every non-warrantable building is a condotel. A building can fail the lender rules for other reasons, and our non-warrantable condo guide covers them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do condotel loans need a bigger down payment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A DSCR loan on a condotel usually takes more down than a DSCR loan on other homes. The lenders' own figures are in our non-warrantable condo guide."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I stay in my own condotel unit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each building has its own rules on owner stays, and they matter for the loan. Fannie Mae counts limits on owner stays as a sign of a hotel, and one condotel program will not take a building with them. We read the rules before you offer."}}]}</script>
