ems:baseline;gap:.65rem;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .7rem;line-height:1.3}main#main .cf-n{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:1.75rem;height:1.75rem;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(196,120,58,.16);color:#8a5226;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:700;font-size:.95rem;position:relative;top:-.12rem}main#main .cf-b+.hx-strip:not(:empty){margin-top:1.1rem}main#main .cf-b+.hx-strip+.hx-fallback .c3-offer{margin:.4rem 0 .6rem}main#main .cf-after{margin-top:1.8rem;padding-top:1.3rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16);max-width:720px}main#main .cf-disc{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);max-width:640px;margin:.4rem 0 1.2rem;padding:.75rem 1rem;border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:rgba(255,255,255,.45);border-radius:0 12px 12px 0}@media (max-width:379px){main#main .hx-fb,main#main .hx-fb>*{min-width:0;max-width:100%}main#main .hx-fb-ai,main#main .hx-fb-q{min-width:0!important;max-width:100%!important;flex-wrap:wrap;box-sizing:border-box}main#main .hx-fb-q textarea{min-width:0;flex:1 1 100%;width:100%}main#main .hx-fb-go{flex:1 1 100%}}@media (min-width:1000px) and (max-width:1100px){.header-ctas .hdr-phone{display:none!important}}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2){padding:.9rem 0!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{display:block!important;text-align:center!important;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.95),rgba(28,32,40,.97))!important;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14)!important;box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.14),0 26px 60px -30px rgba(28,32,40,.6)!important;border-radius:28px!important;padding:2.2rem 1.6rem!important;margin-left:auto!important;margin-right:auto!important}@media (max-width:699px){main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{padding:1.6rem 1.2rem 1.7rem!important;border-radius:24px!important}}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Which loans close on a Myrtle Beach condotel unit, which units qualify, and which oceanfront buildings run like hotels.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac and FHA loans do not work in a Myrtle Beach building run like a hotel. About 8 in 10 oceanfront condos for sale here say the unit is in a rental program.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condotel loans do work when the unit itself is big enough. One published condotel program asks for 500 square feet, a separate bedroom and a full kitchen. More than 3 in 4 rental-program condos for sale have the size and the bedroom.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send us the building and the unit. We tell you which loan fits it.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask which loan fits</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#which-loans" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which loans work</a></li><li><a href="#what-is-a-condotel" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What a condotel is</a></li><li><a href="#buildings" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Hotel-run buildings</a></li><li><a href="#requirements" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What the unit needs</a></li><li><a href="#worth-it" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Worth it?</a></li><li><a href="#lenders" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who lends</a></li><li><a href="#condotel-financing-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Condotel financing FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-loans"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which loans work">Can you get a mortgage on a condotel in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, but not with the loans most buyers know. Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, <a href="https://www.fhfa.gov/about/fannie-mae-freddie-mac" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the two companies Congress created to buy mortgages from lenders</a>, will not buy a loan in a condo hotel. FHA will not insure one. The rule is about the building, so a strong credit score does not change it.</p><div class="cf-tw"><table class="cf-tab"><caption>Which loans work on a unit in a Myrtle Beach building run like a hotel</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Loan</th><th scope="col">Works?</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Conventional loans (Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac)</th><td class="ans"><span class="l">Works?</span>No</td><td class="why"><span class="l">Why</span>Fannie Mae will not take a building run as a hotel, or one with a rental pool. A resort company that manages the building and rents units for owners rules it out too. <a href="https://guide.freddiemac.com/app/guide/section/5701.3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freddie Mac</a> will not take a condo hotel.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">FHA</th><td class="ans"><span class="l">Works?</span>No</td><td class="why"><span class="l">Why</span>FHA <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/Housing/documents/40001-hsgh-Update-18-Redline.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">will not insure a loan on a condotel</a>, or approve a building with a required rental pool. None of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory is on <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD's approved condo list</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">VA</th><td class="ans"><span class="l">Works?</span>Only a home you live in</td><td class="why"><span class="l">Why</span>A VA buyer certifies that they will live in the home. At least 6 of the 47 buildings in our directory have an accepted record on <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the VA's condo list</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Condotel loans</th><td class="ans"><span class="l">Works?</span>Yes, if the unit qualifies</td><td class="why"><span class="l">Why</span>These loans are made outside the Fannie Mae, Freddie Mac and FHA rules. Each lender makes its own rules for the unit and the building.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One kind of condotel loan, <a href="/invest/strategies/dscr-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a DSCR loan</a>, qualifies on the unit's rent instead of your income. A cash buyer needs no lender to approve the building.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-is-a-condotel"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What a condotel is">What makes a Myrtle Beach condo a condotel?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condotel is a condo building run like a hotel. Each unit has its own owner, but the building is managed and operated as a hotel. These are the signs <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae lists</a>, put as what you see on a visit:</p><ul class="cf-plain"><li><b>Guest registration and short stays</b>Guests register with the building, and the HOA or its manager rents units by the day or for short stays.</li><li><b>Hotel services</b>Daily cleaning, a central phone line and a central key system.</li><li><b>A rental pool</b>Owners pool their units with the HOA or the manager and share the rent, whether the papers require it or not.</li><li><b>A resort company in charge</b>A hotel or resort company manages the building and also rents units for owners.</li><li><b>Limits on owners</b>Rules on when owners may stay or how they decorate, or an HOA licensed as a hotel or resort.</li><li><b>A resort name</b>Fannie Mae will not take a building whose name contains hotel, motel or resort, unless the word only refers to the building's past use. Hotel marketing and a hotel rating on booking sites count too.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">23 of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory go by a name with Resort or a hotel brand in it. Freddie Mac has its own tests, and it reads the building's papers and services to decide what is a condo hotel.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every condotel is non-warrantable. Not every non-warrantable building is a condotel. <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our non-warrantable condo guide</a> covers the other reasons a building fails the lender rules.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Not sure your building counts as a condotel?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us its name. We read its rental program papers and tell you which loan fits.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="buildings"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Hotel-run buildings">Which Myrtle Beach oceanfront buildings run like hotels?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of them do. That is the 8 in 10 oceanfront listings in Horry County that name a rental program. Buildings like these are usually non-warrantable because so many owners are investors. We see that as a good sign too: the building is run for renting, which is what you want.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.3rem 0 1.5rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/hoa-reserves/myrtle-beach-oceanfront-towers-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="675" alt="A row of oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach with flat roofs, stacked balconies and pools behind the dunes, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront towers in Myrtle Beach, with pools and rows of beach umbrellas behind the dunes, seen from a plane over the ocean.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These four Grand Strand resorts show what a resort's desk does for an owner, and what the unit's size means for the loan.</p><div class="cf-b" id="landmark-resort"><h3 class="cf-bh"><span class="cf-n">1</span><span>Landmark Resort: three 40-foot slides for the resort's own guests</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Landmark's <a href="https://www.landmarkresort.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">H2Oasis water park</a> has three 40-foot slides, and it is open only to guests who book through the resort's on-site rental program. The desk that sells those stays also fills an owner's calendar. Units run from hotel rooms to three-bedroom penthouses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The typical unit for sale is about 430 square feet, and more than half are studios. Here the one unit decides the loan.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="landmark-resort" data-name="Landmark Resort" data-head="Own at Landmark, where the resort's guests get three 40-foot slides"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Landmark%20Resort">Send me units at Landmark Resort<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="cf-b" id="ocean-creek-resort"><h3 class="cf-bh"><span class="cf-n">2</span><span>Ocean Creek Resort: 13 water features and its own booking desk</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.oceancreek.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Creek</a> has 13 water features, from the oceanfront pool at the Beach Club to an indoor pool and whirlpool. The resort books its guests on its own site, and says TripAdvisor gave it a Traveler's Choice award.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The typical unit for sale is about 830 square feet, and most have one or two bedrooms. Most units here clear the size line with room to spare.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="ocean-creek-resort" data-name="Ocean Creek Resort" data-head="Ocean Creek condos, with 13 water features and its own booking desk"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Creek%20Resort">Send me units at Ocean Creek Resort<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="cf-b" id="compass-cove"><h3 class="cf-bh"><span class="cf-n">3</span><span>Compass Cove: a resort that calls its owners partners</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.compasscove.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Compass Cove</a> tells owners, "you are our partner and we treat your property as if we own it." Its desk takes guests' reservations, and it says its aim is to earn owners the most rent. Guests have six indoor and outdoor pools and seven hot tubs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The typical unit for sale is about 550 square feet, and about 4 in 10 are studios. The size and the bedroom decide each unit's loan.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="compass-cove" data-name="Compass Cove" data-head="Compass Cove condos, at a resort that calls its owners partners"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Compass%20Cove">Send me units at Compass Cove<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="cf-b" id="seawatch-resort"><h3 class="cf-bh"><span class="cf-n">4</span><span>SeaWatch Resort: a concierge for your guests</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.seawatchresort.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SeaWatch</a> calls itself one of the best hotels in South Carolina. Its site lists a concierge, a business center and a golf and entertainment desk for guests. It books stays on its own site.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most units for sale have a bedroom, and the typical one is just over 500 square feet, right at the size line. We check the one unit before you offer.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="seawatch-resort" data-name="SeaWatch Resort" data-head="Own at SeaWatch, a resort that calls itself one of S.C.'s best hotels"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=SeaWatch%20Resort">Send me units at SeaWatch Resort<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="cf-after"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Resorts market themselves as hotels, and lenders read it. Every oceanfront building, with its fee and what it offers, is in <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our oceanfront condo building directory</a>.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="requirements"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What the unit needs">Condotel loan requirements: what does the unit need?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.newrezwholesale.com/media/b0hbzabm/smart-product-project-checklist-3-2026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">One published condotel program</a> asks for at least 500 square feet, a separate bedroom and a full kitchen. The kitchen means a sink, a refrigerator, a range or cooktop, and an oven.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fannie Mae's own warning line is lower. A unit under 400 square feet, or one with no full-size kitchen appliances, makes a lender look harder.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><div role="table" aria-label="More than 3 in 4 rental-program condos for sale have 500 square feet and a bedroom"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">More than 3 in 4 rental-program condos for sale have 500 square feet and a bedroom</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Size and bedrooms</span><span role="columnheader">Condos for sale</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">500 sq ft or more, with a bedroom</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">678 condos</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Under 500 sq ft, with a bedroom</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.041" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">28 condos</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Studios, any size</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.264" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">179 condos</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Oceanfront condos for sale in Horry County whose listing says the unit is in a rental program, 885 in all, our count on November 10, 2026. Sizes as the listing gives them. The lines are one published condotel program's.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Five buildings in our directory have a typical unit for sale under 500 square feet: Sea Mist, Sands Ocean Club, Landmark, Ocean Reef and Bluewater. There the one unit decides the loan, so we check its size, its bedroom and its kitchen before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The building has rules too. The program above looks for three things, and makes exceptions case by case:</p><ul class="cf-plain"><li><b>No rental pool</b>It will not take a building whose rental desk pools the units, by choice or by rule.</li><li><b>Owners free to stay</b>Owners may use the unit all year, with no blackout dates.</li><li><b>The money in order</b>Reserves set aside for repairs, and few owners behind on their dues.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These loans take more cash at closing. A DSCR loan on a condotel usually takes more down than a DSCR loan on other homes. The lenders' own figures are in <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our non-warrantable condo guide</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us check a unit before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We confirm the size, the bedroom, the kitchen and the building's rental rules, before you pay for an offer or an inspection.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check my unit</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="worth-it"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Worth it?">Is a condotel worth the harder loan?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condotel is worth the harder loan for a buyer who wants the resort to do the renting. What you gain, and what it costs you:</p><p class="cf-sub">What you gain</p><ul class="cf-plain"><li><b>The resort does the hotel work</b>Its desk takes the bookings and its staff cleans between guests. At <a href="https://www.sandsresorts.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sands Resorts</a>, the company says only its rental program's guests get all of the resort's amenities.</li><li><b>Units that sell</b>About 780 units sold in a year in 43 of the directory's oceanfront buildings, about 1 in 15 of their units. In a resort of 300 units, that is about 20 sales a year.</li></ul><p class="cf-sub">What it costs you</p><ul class="cf-plain"><li><b>Fewer lenders, now and when you sell</b>Fewer lenders make condotel loans, and your next buyer needs one too, unless they pay cash.</li><li><b>Fees to buy in</b>Expect an HOA transfer fee and a few months of dues held in escrow at closing, as in most HOAs. <a href="/hoa/estoppel-and-transfer-fees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our guide to transfer fees</a> has the details.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether a beach condo makes a good rental is in <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our guide to Myrtle Beach condos as investments</a>. What a resort's program keeps from the rent is in <a href="/invest/rental-program-vs-airbnb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental program vs Airbnb</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="lenders"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who lends">Who makes condotel loans for Myrtle Beach buildings?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our affiliated lender, BrickWood Mortgage, a separate company, arranges condotel and non-warrantable loans through wholesale lenders that accept these buildings.</p><p class="cf-disc">Chapter3 Realty Corp has a business relationship with BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497). Because of this relationship, this referral may provide Chapter3 Realty a financial or other benefit. You are never required to use BrickWood. You are free to shop any lender.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer, our agents read the building's rental program papers and confirm the unit's size and kitchen. It is part of the building review we run on every condo purchase: the bylaws, the budget, the reserves, <a href="/buyers/condo-in-litigation/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">any lawsuit</a> and the rental history.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="condotel-financing-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Condotel financing FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is a condotel in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo building run like a hotel. Each unit has its own owner, and the resort or the HOA rents units to vacationers by the night, with guest registration and cleaning.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use an FHA loan on a Myrtle Beach condotel?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. FHA will not insure a loan on a condotel or approve a building with a required rental pool. None of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory is on HUD's approved condo list.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use a VA loan on a condotel?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only for a home you will live in, because a VA buyer certifies that they will move in. At least 6 of the 47 oceanfront buildings in our directory have an accepted VA record.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the difference between a condotel and a non-warrantable condo?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every condotel is non-warrantable, but not every non-warrantable building is a condotel. A building can fail the lender rules for other reasons, and our non-warrantable condo guide covers them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do condotel loans need a bigger down payment?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A DSCR loan on a condotel usually takes more down than a DSCR loan on other homes. The lenders' own figures are in our non-warrantable condo guide.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I stay in my own condotel unit?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each building has its own rules on owner stays, and they matter for the loan. Fannie Mae counts limits on owner stays as a sign of a hotel, and one condotel program will not take a building with them. We read the rules before you offer.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae B4-2.1-03</a>, <a href="https://guide.freddiemac.com/app/guide/section/5701.3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freddie Mac 5701.3</a>, <a href="https://www.fhfa.gov/about/fannie-mae-freddie-mac" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FHFA</a>, <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/Housing/documents/40001-hsgh-Update-18-Redline.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Handbook 4000.1</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/condlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD condo list</a>, <a href="https://lgy.va.gov/lgyhub/condo-report" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA condo report</a>, <a href="https://www.newrezwholesale.com/media/b0hbzabm/smart-product-project-checklist-3-2026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Newrez Smart checklist</a>, <a href="https://www.landmarkresort.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Landmark Resort</a>, <a href="https://www.oceancreek.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Creek</a>, <a href="https://www.compasscove.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Compass Cove</a>, <a href="https://www.seawatchresort.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SeaWatch</a>, <a href="https://www.sandsresorts.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sands Resorts</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County deeds</a>. Condos for sale: our count of the listing feed on November 10, 2026, in total only. Sales: our count of county deeds, one unit at a time, over a year. The directory is the 47 oceanfront buildings on our building directory.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credi