+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long should I hold a rental property before selling in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Until a sale pays back the buying and selling costs and the tax rule you need is met. A financed buyer at the example commission in our net proceeds calculator needs the price to rise 10.5 percent. At 3 percent a year that is about three years. Since 2001, three-year holds cleared that bar 66 times out of 100 in the Myrtle Beach metro, and every 15-year hold ended above its start."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much has Myrtle Beach real estate appreciated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Zillow's typical home value for the Myrtle Beach metro was $339,738 in September 2026. That is +0.6 percent over one year and −2.1 percent over three years. Over five years it is +21.7 percent, or 4.0 percent a year. Over ten years it is +80.0 percent, or 6.1 percent a year. From the March 2007 peak the value fell 34.1 percent and did not recover until December 2020."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to hold a rental for a year before selling?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No law requires it. A house held one year or less is taxed as ordinary income when sold. A house held more than one year gets the lower long-term capital gains rate. A flip is inventory and is taxed as ordinary income at any length."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do I have to hold a property before a 1031 exchange?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The statute has no minimum. The house must be held for investment or business use, not for sale. The only IRS time test is a safe harbor for a house you also use yourself. It must be owned and rented for 24 months before the exchange, with personal use inside the limits. The same 24 months apply after."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do I have to live in a rental to avoid capital gains?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two of the last five years as your main home, and you must sell within three years of moving out. That excludes up to $250,000 of gain, or $500,000 on a joint return, except the depreciation taken while it was rented. If you rented it first and moved in later, the rental years before the move are taxed in proportion."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should an all-cash investor sell one rental to buy two?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not two of the same kind, because the sale only adds the selling and buying costs. Trading one expensive house that leaves little rent for two cheaper houses that leave more can pay back the costs in about 3 years, through a 1031 exchange. Saved rent alone does not buy a second house for 13 years or more in any Horry County area."}}]}</script>
