-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Mid-term rentals</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Furnished, by the month</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Can you rent a Myrtle Beach home by the month where Airbnb is banned?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Yes, at 90 days.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge, 30+ years on the Grand Strand &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 6, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">South Carolina does not treat a stay of 90 continuous days as a short-term rental. Residential neighborhoods in the city that ban nightly rentals allow a 90-day stay.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A mid-term rental is a furnished home rented by the month, for stays of about one to six months. The tenants are travel nurses on 13-week contracts, people between homes, workers on a project, and families waiting on a closing. On the Grand Strand the number that matters is 90. A stay of 90 continuous days pays no accommodations tax and no county hospitality fee. The City of Myrtle Beach does not count it as a short-term rental. That makes a 90-day furnished lease legal in residential zones where nightly rentals are banned. Below: who the tenants are, the rules, the platforms, and how to price it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is a mid-term rental?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A mid-term rental is a furnished home rented by the month, for stays of about one to six months. The rent usually includes utilities and internet. The tenant brings clothes and a laptop, not a sofa.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It sits between the two rentals most owners know. A short-term rental is rented by the night and pays the accommodations tax. A long-term rental is unfurnished on a twelve-month lease. The mid-term rental is furnished and monthly, and it is outside the nightly-rental rules once the stay is long enough.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tenants are travel nurses on contracts, people between homes, workers on a project, families waiting on a closing, and insurance placements after a fire or a flood.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Why is 90 days the number on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three rules use the same line. <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state accommodations tax</a> applies to stays under 90 consecutive days and stops at 90 continuous days to the same person. <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County's hospitality fee</a> stops at 90 consecutive days at the same location to the same guest. <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The City of Myrtle Beach</a> does not count a stay of 90 or more consecutive days as a short-term accommodation.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Zoning follows the same line inside the city. <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The city's planning office</a> says a property cannot be rented for less than 90 days unless it is zoned for short-term rentals. Most residential neighborhoods are not. A stay of 90 days or more is not a short-term rental, so a 90-day furnished lease is allowed where a nightly one is not.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">National advice says 30 days. Inside the Myrtle Beach city limits the floor is 90 nights, because a 30-day stay is still a short-term rental there. Set the minimum at 90.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One exception applies to oceanfront buildings. In December 2024 the city adopted <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/2024-069%20Conversion%20Overlay_Short%20Term%20Rentals%20(1st).pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">an overlay zone</a> between Kings Highway and the ocean. In it, a building of more than two units that was built or used for nightly rental may not be leased for 90 days or more. The 90-day plan works in the neighborhoods, not in the oceanfront towers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach</a> has no zoning limit on rental length and licenses every rental. <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/1246?fileID=6196" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a> allows stays under 30 days only in its R3 and C3 districts and defines a long-term rental as 365 days or more. It does not define the months between, so ask the town before you count on a 90-day plan there.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Who rents by the month here?</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Tenant</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">How long</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What sets the stay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Travel nurses</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13 weeks, the standard contract, often extended</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The hospital's contract dates. The Grand Strand's hospitals are Grand Strand Medical Center in Myrtle Beach, Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital in Murrells Inlet, Conway Medical Center in Conway, and McLeod Health Seacoast in Little River.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Insurance and relocation placements</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Months, set by the claim or the move</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The insurer or the employer pays. The platform that began with travel nurses now lists relocating families and insurance placements too.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Seasonal workers</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to four months in summer</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Student visa holders in the summer work program. Sponsors must help arrange housing. <a href="/invest/j1-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">J-1 rentals, explained</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Winter visitors</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two or three months</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The cold months up north.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Buyers between homes</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Until a closing or a build finishes</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Buyers waiting on a closing or a new build.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Thirteen weeks is 91 days. <a href="https://healthtrustjobs.com/careers/travel-nursing-jobs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">One hospital staffing company</a> says assignments usually last 13 weeks, and <a href="https://www.ayahealthcare.com/travel-nursing/travel-nursing-questions/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">a national agency</a> says nurses take agency housing or a housing stipend and find their own place. A 91-day contract clears the 90-day line by one day.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want it run both ways?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send the address. We run it furnished by the month and unfurnished on a year lease, and we check the zoning and the HOA minimum lease term.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How do you price a furnished monthly rental?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is no public rent index for furnished monthly stays here. One public reference exists. <a href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-book/per-diem-rates/per-diem-rates-results?action=perdiems_report&fiscal_year=2026&state=SC&city=Myrtle%20Beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The federal lodging rate for Horry County</a> is $110 a night from October through March, $132 in April and May, and $182 from June through August. It is a reimbursement ceiling for government travelers, not a market rent, and a nurse's stipend is set by the agency.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Price it three ways and take the middle.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The unfurnished rent for the same home, plus the furnishing, utilities and internet you now carry.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The comparable furnished listings on the platforms for the same month.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The stipend a tenant tells you they have.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Then run it against the alternatives. <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The investor analyzer</a> takes a rent figure; put the furnished number in and compare it with the unfurnished one. <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Short-term against long-term</a> covers the nightly case.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Where do you list it?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.furnishedfinder.com/list-your-property" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Furnished Finder</a> charges a flat $199 a year to list, takes no commission and no booking fee, and handles stays of 30 days or more. It began with travel nurses. <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2729" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb</a> counts 28 nights or longer as a monthly stay, lets you set a monthly discount, and collects the rent in monthly installments.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On Airbnb, set the minimum stay to 90 nights inside the Myrtle Beach city limits. Airbnb collects South Carolina taxes only on reservations of 89 nights and shorter, which matches the state line. <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb's South Carolina tax page</a> lists what it collects.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ask the hospital's housing office and the agency's housing desk once the home is ready. Both place nurses directly.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which lease and which insurance do you need?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A 90-day stay is a tenancy, not a hotel stay. <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c040.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state landlord and tenant law</a> excludes transient occupancy in accommodations that pay the accommodations tax, and a 90-day stay does not pay it. Use a written lease with an end date, take a deposit under the deposit rules, and give the tenant the owner notice. <a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The deposit and notice rules</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether a stay of 30 to 89 days counts as transient occupancy is not written in the statute. Ask a South Carolina attorney before you lease for less than 90 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Insurance changes with the use. <a href="https://doi.sc.gov/954/Second-Home-Insurance-What-You-Need-to-K" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state insurance department</a> says renting a vacation home to others will likely raise the cost and may need added coverage. A homeowners policy is written for the home you live in. Ask for a landlord policy that covers the furnishings you own, and place wind and flood where the zone requires. <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Coastal insurance, explained</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which Grand Strand properties fit?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two- and three-bedroom homes and townhomes within a short drive of a hospital. Carolina Forest and Socastee for Grand Strand Medical Center. Murrells Inlet and Surfside Beach for Tidelands Waccamaw. Conway for Conway Medical Center and the university. Little River for McLeod Health Seacoast.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway has a second calendar. <a href="https://www.coastal.edu/news/fall2025/ccubreakstotalenrollmentrecordforthirdconsecutiveyear/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Coastal Carolina University</a> enrolled 12,006 students in fall 2025, a record, and its semesters set two move-in waves a year. Ask us what furnished homes near the campus have rented for.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Read the covenants before you offer. Many associations set a minimum lease term of 30, 90 or 180 days, and some cap the number of leases a year. A 90-day plan needs a 90-day minimum or shorter.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Looking near a hospital or an employer?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the hospital or the employer. We list the homes within a short drive that allow a 90-day lease.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a neighborhood</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Mid-term rental FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a 30-day rental legal in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city limits, not in residential zones. The city counts any stay under 90 days as a short-term rental, and zones that begin with R do not allow them. A 90-day stay is not a short-term rental.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a 90-day tenant pay accommodations tax?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The state tax stops at 90 continuous days to the same person, and the county hospitality fee stops at 90 consecutive days. Stays under 90 days pay both.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How long is a travel nurse contract?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Thirteen weeks is the standard, which is 91 days. Agencies also offer shorter and longer assignments, and many nurses extend.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use Airbnb for monthly stays?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Airbnb treats 28 nights or longer as a monthly stay, lets you set monthly discounts, and collects payment in monthly installments. Set your minimum nights to 90 inside the Myrtle Beach city limits.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I need a landlord policy for a furnished rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A homeowners policy is written for the home you live in. Renting it out changes the coverage, and the state insurance department says to expect a higher cost and added coverage.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">South Carolina Department of Revenue, accommodations tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County, hospitality fee</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Myrtle Beach, planning and zoning</a>, <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/1246?fileID=6196" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Town of Surfside Beach, zoning uses</a>, <a href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-book/per-diem-rates/per-diem-rates-results?action=perdiems_report&fiscal_year=2026&state=SC&city=Myrtle%20Beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GSA, per diem rates for Horry County</a>. Read September 6, 2026. Educational only, not legal or tax advice. Ask the planning office for the rule at your address.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">The 90-day lease is the legal option where Airbnb is banned.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send the address. We run it furnished by the month and unfurnished on a year lease, and check the zoning and the HOA minimum.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div></section></main>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Mid-term rentals</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Furnished, by the month</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Can you rent a Myrtle Beach home by the month where Airbnb is banned?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Yes, at 90 days.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">South Carolina does not treat a stay of 90 continuous days as a short-term rental. Residential neighborhoods in the city that ban nightly rentals allow a 90-day stay.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A mid-term rental is a furnished home rented by the month, for stays of about one to six months. The tenants are travel nurses on 13-week contracts, people between homes, workers on a project, and families waiting on a closing. On the Grand Strand the number that matters is 90. A stay of 90 continuous days pays no accommodations tax and no county hospitality fee. The City of Myrtle Beach does not count it as a short-term rental. That makes a 90-day furnished lease legal in residential zones where nightly rentals are banned. Below: who the tenants are, the rules, the platforms, and how to price it.</p><div style="margin-top:1.4rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-is-a-mid-term-rental" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What is a mid-term rental?</a></li><li><a href="#why-is-90-days-the-number-on-the-grand-strand" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Why is 90 days the number on the Grand Strand?</a></li><li><a href="#who-rents-by-the-month-here" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who rents by the month here?</a></li><li><a href="#how-do-you-price-a-furnished-monthly-rental" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How do you price a furnished monthly rental?</a></li><li><a href="#where-do-you-list-it" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where do you list it?</a></li><li><a href="#which-lease-and-which-insurance-do-you-need" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which lease and which insurance do you need?</a></li><li><a href="#which-grand-strand-properties-fit" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which Grand Strand properties fit?</a></li><li><a href="#mid-term-rental-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Mid-term rental FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-a-mid-term-rental"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is a mid-term rental?</h2><style>@media (min-width:700px){main#main .detail-h1{font-size:clamp(2.3rem,3.9vw,3.4rem);line-height:1.08;text-wrap:balance}}main#main .detail-h1 em{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.5vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:.55rem;text-wrap:balance}@media (max-width:959px){main#main .detail-h1 em{color:#8a5226!important}}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A mid-term rental is a furnished home rented by the month, for stays of about one to six months. The rent usually includes utilities and internet. The tenant brings clothes and a laptop, not a sofa.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It sits between the two rentals most owners know. A short-term rental is rented by the night and pays the accommodations tax. A long-term rental is unfurnished on a twelve-month lease. The mid-term rental is furnished and monthly, and it is outside the nightly-rental rules once the stay is long enough.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tenants are travel nurses on contracts, people between homes, workers on a project, families waiting on a closing, and insurance placements after a fire or a flood.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="why-is-90-days-the-number-on-the-grand-strand"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Why is 90 days the number on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three rules use the same line. <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state accommodations tax</a> applies to stays under 90 consecutive days and stops at 90 continuous days to the same person. <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County's hospitality fee</a> stops at 90 consecutive days at the same location to the same guest. <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The City of Myrtle Beach</a> does not count a stay of 90 or more consecutive days as a short-term accommodation.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Zoning follows the same line inside the city. <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The city's planning office</a> says a property cannot be rented for less than 90 days unless it is zoned for short-term rentals. Most residential neighborhoods are not. A stay of 90 days or more is not a short-term rental, so a 90-day furnished lease is allowed where a nightly one is not.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">National advice says 30 days. Inside the Myrtle Beach city limits the floor is 90 nights, because a 30-day stay is still a short-term rental there. Set the minimum at 90.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One exception applies to oceanfront buildings. In December 2024 the city adopted <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/2024-069%20Conversion%20Overlay_Short%20Term%20Rentals%20(1st).pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">an overlay zone</a> between Kings Highway and the ocean. In it, a building of more than two units that was built or used for nightly rental may not be leased for 90 days or more. The 90-day plan works in the neighborhoods, not in the oceanfront towers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach</a> has no zoning limit on rental length and licenses every rental. <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/1246?fileID=6196" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a> allows stays under 30 days only in its R3 and C3 districts and defines a long-term rental as 365 days or more. It does not define the months between, so ask the town before you count on a 90-day plan there.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="who-rents-by-the-month-here"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Who rents by the month here?</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Tenant</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">How long</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What sets the stay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Travel nurses</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13 weeks, the standard contract, often extended</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The hospital's contract dates. The Grand Strand's hospitals are Grand Strand Medical Center in Myrtle Beach, Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital in Murrells Inlet, Conway Medical Center in Conway, and McLeod Health Seacoast in Little River.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Insurance and relocation placements</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Months, set by the claim or the move</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The insurer or the employer pays. The platform that began with travel nurses now lists relocating families and insurance placements too.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Seasonal workers</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to four months in summer</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Student visa holders in the summer work program. Sponsors must help arrange housing. <a href="/invest/j1-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">J-1 rentals, explained</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Winter visitors</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two or three months</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The cold months up north.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Buyers between homes</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Until a closing or a build finishes</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Buyers waiting on a closing or a new build.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Thirteen weeks is 91 days. <a href="https://healthtrustjobs.com/careers/travel-nursing-jobs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">One hospital staffing company</a> says assignments usually last 13 weeks, and <a href="https://www.ayahealthcare.com/travel-nursing/travel-nursing-questions/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">a national agency</a> says nurses take agency housing or a housing stipend and find their own place. A 91-day contract clears the 90-day line by one day.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want it run both ways?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send the address. We run it furnished by the month and unfurnished on a year lease, and we check the zoning and the HOA minimum lease term.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="how-do-you-price-a-furnished-monthly-rental"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How do you price a furnished monthly rental?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is no public rent index for furnished monthly stays here. One public reference exists. <a href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-book/per-diem-rates/per-diem-rates-results?action=perdiems_report&fiscal_year=2026&state=SC&city=Myrtle%20Beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The federal lodging rate for Horry County</a> is $110 a night from October through March, $132 in April and May, and $182 from June through August. It is a reimbursement ceiling for government travelers, not a market rent, and a nurse's stipend is set by the agency.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Price it three ways and take the middle.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The unfurnished rent for the same home, plus the furnishing, utilities and internet you now carry.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The comparable furnished listings on the platforms for the same month.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The stipend a tenant tells you they have.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Then run it against the alternatives. <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The investor analyzer</a> takes a rent figure; put the furnished number in and compare it with the unfurnished one. <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Short-term against long-term</a> covers the nightly case.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where-do-you-list-it"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Where do you list it?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.furnishedfinder.com/list-your-property" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Furnished Finder</a> charges a flat $199 a year to list, takes no commission and no booking fee, and handles stays of 30 days or more. It began with travel nurses. <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2729" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb</a> counts 28 nights or longer as a monthly stay, lets you set a monthly discount, and collects the rent in monthly installments.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On Airbnb, set the minimum stay to 90 nights inside the Myrtle Beach city limits. Airbnb collects South Carolina taxes only on reservations of 89 nights and shorter, which matches the state line. <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb's South Carolina tax page</a> lists what it collects.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ask the hospital's housing office and the agency's housing desk once the home is ready. Both place nurses directly.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-lease-and-which-insurance-do-you-need"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which lease and which insurance do you need?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A 90-day stay is a tenancy, not a hotel stay. <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c040.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state landlord and tenant law</a> excludes transient occupancy in accommodations that pay the accommodations tax, and a 90-day stay does not pay it. Use a written lease with an end date, take a deposit under the deposit rules, and give the tenant the owner notice. <a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The deposit and notice rules</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether a stay of 30 to 89 days counts as transient occupancy is not written in the statute. Ask a South Carolina attorney before you lease for less than 90 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Insurance changes with the use. <a href="https://doi.sc.gov/954/Second-Home-Insurance-What-You-Need-to-K" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state insurance department</a> says renting a vacation home to others will likely raise the cost and may need added coverage. A homeowners policy is written for the home you live in. Ask for a landlord policy that covers the furnishings you own, and place wind and flood where the zone requires. <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Coastal insurance, explained</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-grand-strand-properties-fit"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which Grand Strand properties fit?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two- and three-bedroom homes and townhomes within a short drive of a hospital. Carolina Forest and Socastee for Grand Strand Medical Center. Murrells Inlet and Surfside Beach for Tidelands Waccamaw. Conway for Conway Medical Center and the university. Little River for McLeod Health Seacoast.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway has a second calendar. <a href="https://www.coastal.edu/news/fall2025/ccubreakstotalenrollmentrecordforthirdconsecutiveyear/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Coastal Carolina University</a> enrolled 12,006 students in fall 2025, a record, and its semesters set two move-in waves a year. Ask us what furnished homes near the campus have rented for.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Read the covenants before you offer. Many associations set a minimum lease term of 30, 90 or 180 days, and some cap the number of leases a year. A 90-day plan needs a 90-day minimum or shorter.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Looking near a hospital or an employer?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the hospital or the employer. We list the homes within a short drive that allow a 90-day lease.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about a neighborhood</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="mid-term-rental-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Mid-term rental FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a 30-day rental legal in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city limits, not in residential zones. The city counts any stay under 90 days as a short-term rental, and zones that begin with R do not allow them. A 90-day stay is not a short-term rental.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a 90-day tenant pay accommodations tax?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The state tax stops at 90 continuous days to the same person, and the county hospitality fee stops at 90 consecutive days. Stays under 90 days pay both.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How long is a travel nurse contract?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Thirteen weeks is the standard, which is 91 days. Agencies also offer shorter and longer assignments, and many nurses extend.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use Airbnb for monthly stays?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Airbnb treats 28 nights or longer as a monthly stay, lets you set monthly discounts, and collects payment in monthly installments. Set your minimum nights to 90 inside the Myrtle Beach city limits.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I need a landlord policy for a furnished rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A homeowners policy is written for the home you live in. Renting it out changes the coverage, and the state insurance department says to expect a higher cost and added coverage.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">South Carolina Department of Revenue, accommodations tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County, hospitality fee</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Myrtle Beach, planning and zoning</a>, <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/1246?fileID=6196" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Town of Surfside Beach, zoning uses</a>, <a href="https://www.gsa.gov/travel/plan-book/per-diem-rates/per-diem-rates-results?action=perdiems_report&fiscal_year=2026&state=SC&city=Myrtle%20Beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GSA, per diem rates for Horry County</a>. Educational only, not legal or tax advice. Ask the planning office for the rule at your address.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">The 90-day lease is the legal option where Airbnb is banned.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send the address. We run it furnished by the month and unfurnished on a year lease, and check the zoning and the HOA minimum.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Send the address</a></div></section></main>
