ayment, Fannie Mae condo requirements, Fannie Mae single entity ownership, condo master policy deductible Fannie Mae"}</script>
+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a warrantable and a non-warrantable condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A warrantable condo is in a building that meets Fannie Mae's project rules, so a conventional loan there can be sold to Fannie Mae or Freddie Mac. A non-warrantable condo is in a building that fails one of those rules."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a list of non-warrantable condos in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Fannie Mae publishes no list for buyers to search. A lender reviews each building from its papers. Our table shows the public signs for 43 oceanfront buildings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use an FHA or VA loan on a non-warrantable condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in a building on that agency's own list. Of the oceanfront buildings in our directory, only Sea Mark Tower at the Caravelle is FHA-approved, and at least 6 have an accepted VA record."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do you need down for a non-warrantable condo?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a rental you will not stay in more than 14 days a year, about 25 percent down, against about 20 percent in a warrantable building. Figures from BrickWood Mortgage. For a home you will use, plan on a larger down payment."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a non-warrantable condo become warrantable?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. When the building fixes the reason, such as a new master policy or a lawsuit that ends, a lender can review it again."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy a non-warrantable condo as a second home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, with cash or a loan made outside Fannie Mae's rules. Plan on a larger down payment than for a conventional loan."}}]}</script>
