/span><span><strong>Half to one month's rent</strong><span class="t">to place a tenant</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>About $2,200 to $2,400</strong><span class="t">a year on a $1,600 rent</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Five local fee schedules, a year of fees worked out, and when an owner needs a manager.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Four of the five property managers serving Horry County that print their fees take 10 percent of each month's rent on a yearly lease. Most add half a month to a full month's rent each time they place a new tenant. On a <span style="white-space:nowrap">3-bedroom</span> house renting for about $1,600 a month, that comes to about <span style="white-space:nowrap">$2,200 to $2,400</span> a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A vacation rental manager costs more. In the rentals we have seen, a basic plan takes about 13 to 17 percent of the bookings. Full service takes about 40 to 60 percent of the profit after costs, not of the bookings. Chapter3 does not manage property. We work out what you keep after the manager's fee.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Know the manager's real fee before you buy.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What managers charge</a></li><li><a href="#a-year" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Cost in a year</a></li><li><a href="#vacation-rentals" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Vacation rentals</a></li><li><a href="#do-you-need-one" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do you need one</a></li><li><a href="#extra-fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Fees on top</a></li><li><a href="#taxes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Rental taxes</a></li><li><a hr