 fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">high</text><text x="187.0" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">A</text><rect x="200.3" y="49.5" width="12.0" height="20.4" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>September</title></rect><text x="206.3" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">S</text><rect x="219.7" y="60.9" width="12.0" height="9.0" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>October</title></rect><text x="225.7" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">O</text><rect x="239.0" y="69.9" width="12.0" height="23.8" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>November</title></rect><text x="245.0" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">N</text><rect x="258.3" y="69.9" width="12.0" height="57.0" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>December</title></rect><text x="264.3" y="168.4" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">D</text></svg><svg class="rp-w" viewBox="0 0 680 245" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of asking rents against the year's trend, by month. Rents are above the trend from June to October, highest in August, about half a percent above. They are below it from November to April, lowest in January, about 1.4 percent below."><line x1="39" x2="674" y1="20.8" y2="20.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="33" y="25.4" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">+1%</text><line x1="39" x2="674" y1="97.0" y2="97.0" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".45"/><text x="33" y="101.6" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">trend</text><line x1="39" x2="674" y1="173.3" y2="173.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="33" y="177.8" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">−1%</text><rect x="49.1" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="102.9" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>January</title></rect><text x="65.5" y="214.9" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">low</text><text x="65.5" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Jan</text><rect x="102.0" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="80.0" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>February</title></rect><text x="118.4" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Feb</text><rect x="154.9" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="32.8" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>March</title></rect><text x="171.3" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Mar</text><rect x="207.8" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="14.5" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>April</title></rect><text x="224.2" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Apr</text><rect x="260.7" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="1.5" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>May</title></rect><text x="277.1" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">May</text><rect x="313.6" y="78.7" width="32.8" height="18.3" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>June</title></rect><text x="330.0" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Jun</text><rect x="366.6" y="62.7" width="32.8" height="34.3" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>July</title></rect><text x="383.0" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Jul</text><rect x="419.5" y="52.1" width="32.8" height="45.0" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>August</title></rect><text x="435.9" y="46.2" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">high</text><text x="435.9" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Aug</text><rect x="472.4" y="64.3" width="32.8" height="32.8" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>September</title></rect><text x="488.8" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Sep</text><rect x="525.3" y="82.5" width="32.8" height="14.5" rx="3" fill="#c4783a"><title>October</title></rect><text x="541.7" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Oct</text><rect x="578.2" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="38.1" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>November</title></rect><text x="594.6" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Nov</text><rect x="631.1" y="97.0" width="32.8" height="91.5" rx="3" fill="#7d8291"><title>December</title></rect><text x="647.5" y="239.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" fill="#4a4f5c">Dec</text></svg><figcaption>Zillow's rent index, every kind of home, Myrtle Beach metro: each month's average distance from the trend, 2015 to 2026.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The swing is small, about $40 a month on a house. Near the college, the month you list makes more difference to empty weeks than to the price.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/coastal-carolina-bell-tower-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/coastal-carolina-bell-tower-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-rent-prices/coastal-carolina-bell-tower-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 680px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="675" alt="A clock and bell tower on a red brick base beside a pink crape myrtle and flower beds on the Coastal Carolina University campus" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Sk5893. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Sk5893</a></span></div><figcaption>The bell tower at Coastal Carolina University in Conway. New students arrive in August and look for homes to rent.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If your house is near Coastal Carolina University, end the lease in August and start marketing the house a month before it ends. New students arrive in August and need a home to rent. In our experience, August turnover near the college has been no problem, and it is the month we have found best for no empty weeks. More on <a href="/invest/student-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">student rentals near the college</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="your-house"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What will my house rent for">How much can I rent my house for in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For one house, an agent at Chapter3 works out what it will rent for from current local leases and listings, at no cost, before you write the offer. The figures on this page are where we start.</p><div class="rp-ex" role="group" aria-label="Worked example"><p class="k">Worked example: a 3-bedroom house in Carolina Forest, bought empty</p><dl><div><dt>3-bedroom homes rented in Carolina Forest, with utilities</dt><dd>about $1,980</dd></div><div><dt>Less the utilities a house tenant pays</dt><dd>about $200</dd></div><div><dt>Rent, with the tenant paying the utilities</dt><dd>about $1,780</dd></div><div><dt>Homes listed now in ZIP 29579, every kind of home</dt><dd>about $1,770</dd></div><div><dt>Listed in August, not January</dt><dd>about $40 more</dd></div></dl><p><b>List a 3-bedroom house there from about $1,780 a month, with the tenant paying the utilities.</b> The Census figure counts old leases with new ones, and new leases cost more. Before you offer, we check the leases and listings near the one house.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A furnished home on a lease of a few months is priced another way: <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">mid-term rentals</a>. For a quick screen, <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our investment analyzer</a> takes any Grand Strand address and returns an estimated market rent with the cash flow. It is a screening estimate, not an appraisal. <a href="/invest/rental-returns/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What return a Myrtle Beach rental should make</a>, by area and after costs, is on its own page. What a manager charges is on <a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our property management cost page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want this worked example done for one house?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which house. We price it the same way, from the leases and listings near it, at no cost.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us what it will rent for</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="fair-market-rent"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Fair market rent">What is the fair market rent in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fair market rent matters to a landlord who takes housing vouchers (Section 8). The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) publishes it each year. For Horry County, it is $1,823 a month for three bedrooms in the fiscal year 2027 schedule, with utilities.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is not the average rent. About four in ten recent movers into a standard home pay that much or less.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="HUD fair market rent a month, Horry County"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">HUD fair market rent a month, Horry County</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Home</span><span role="columnheader">fair market rent, with utilities</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Studio</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.583" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,155</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1 bedroom</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.635" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,258</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">2 bedrooms</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.759" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,504</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">3 bedrooms</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.92" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,823</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">4 bedrooms</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,981</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>HUD's schedule for the Myrtle Beach-North Myrtle Beach-Conway metro area, from October. The figures include the utilities, except the telephone.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The voucher program uses it to work out what it pays. The rules for landlords who take vouchers are on our <a href="/invest/section-8-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Section 8 rentals</a> page. The three-bedroom figure has risen about 55 percent in ten years.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="raising-the-rent"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Raising the rent">Can a landlord raise the rent in South Carolina?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A new lease can state a higher rent. During a lease, the rent is the amount the lease states.</p><div class="rp-law"><div><b>No local rent limits</b><p>South Carolina does not let a city or county limit rents on privately owned homes.</p></div><div><b>Thirty days' notice</b><p>Either side can end a month-to-month lease with thirty days' written notice.</p></div><div><b>No raise to retaliate</b><p>A landlord may not raise the rent above market value to punish a tenant who complained to a code agency or to the landlord.</p></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Deposits, notices and the rest of the landlord's rules are on our <a href="/invest/landlord-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">South Carolina landlord rules</a> page.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rent-prices-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Rent prices FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the average rent in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The middle rent for every rented home in Horry County is about $1,110 a month before utilities. It counts houses, apartments, condos and mobile homes, on old leases and new.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is rent for a 4-bedroom house in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across every rented home with four bedrooms in Horry County, old leases and new, the middle rent is about $1,530 a month with utilities. The survey has too few rented 4-bedroom houses alone for a firm figure.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where is rent cheapest on the Grand Strand?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Among ten Grand Strand ZIP codes, the asking rent is lowest in the north end of Myrtle Beach (29572). It is about $1,530 a month across every kind of home listed for rent. Little River (29566) is next, about $1,560.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Did the fair market rent go down?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For four bedrooms, yes: it fell from $2,111 to $1,981 a month in the fiscal year 2027 schedule. The three-bedroom figure rose.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT5Y2024.B25064?g=050XX00US45051" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS rent tables</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/microdata.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS microdata</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow research data</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD fair market rents</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-24/subtitle-B/chapter-VIII/part-888/subpart-A/section-888.113" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">24 CFR 888.113</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c039.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-39</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c040.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-40</a>. Census: 2020-2024 American Community Survey 5-year estimates, 2024 dollars. "Most of Horry County" leaves out the Loris, Aynor and Green Sea area; Chapter3 computed those medians from the Census microdata. Zillow's metro area includes Brunswick County, NC; Zillow's data is through September 2026. No rent or value for any one address. Not legal advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses in Carolina Forest from above. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a 1600 x 1200 px view from one NOAA map tile, raised the contrast and color slightly, and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">The bell tower at Coastal Carolina University. Photo: Sk5893, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spadoni_Park_Circle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resiz