 the cheaper third above. The listings earning this revenue are mostly beach properties, not the cheapest houses in the area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest has no nightly figure because our data source does not measure it. That is not the same as no demand. It sits beside the new Carolina Forest hospital, and a furnished monthly rental there serves traveling nurses on 13-week contracts. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Furnished monthly rentals</a> covers that, and <a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">where to buy</a> has the nightly-rental rules, which ban them in most neighborhoods.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-area-is-best-for-each-number"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which area is best for each number?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hover an area, or tap it, for its numbers. The buttons change what the color shows. Darker is higher.</p>
