+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a business license for an Airbnb in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, any rental needs a city business license. North Myrtle Beach asks every short-term rental for one, renewed each year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an Airbnb make in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average one took in about $26,000 from guests in a year, before any cost. Our Airbnb income page breaks it down by town, size and month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many nights does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb condo need to book?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The count depends most on the HOA fee. The four typical condos in the chart above need about 42 to 110 booked nights a year to pay their bills if the owner runs them, and more with a manager."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What percentage does Airbnb take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most hosts, 15.5 percent of each booking. The list of costs above shows what else comes off before the HOA fee."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is an Airbnb cleaning fee in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About $150 is typical. The guest pays it, and it goes to the cleaner, so the owner keeps none of it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the lodging tax on a Myrtle Beach Airbnb?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The guest. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach the lodging taxes add about 13 percent to the price, and Airbnb collects them on stays under 90 nights."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the slow season for a Myrtle Beach Airbnb?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"November to February are the four slowest months. The season chart above shows each month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you finance an Airbnb condo?","accepted