+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a good DSCR for a rental property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Our target is 1.25, which leaves a fifth of the rent after the whole monthly bill. The three program sheets we read ask for 1.00 or more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a DSCR loan in South Carolina without tax returns?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A DSCR loan is judged on the home's rent and its monthly bill. You sign that the home is a rental for business and that you will not live in it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a DSCR loan if the rent does not cover the bill?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes. Our affiliated lender, BrickWood Mortgage, a separate company, starts writing DSCR loans at a ratio of 0.75. Below 1.00, you pay the rest of the bill each month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use Airbnb income for a DSCR loan in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At some lenders. They count 75 to 80 percent of the nightly-rental estimate, and two of the three sheets we read take it only on a refinance. The city and the HOA must allow nightly rentals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a DSCR loan need an appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The rent the lender counts is the appraiser's market rent, written on a rent schedule with the appraisal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I get a DSCR loan in an LLC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A DSCR loan can close in your name or in an LLC. The investor clients we work with usually close in an LLC."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a first-time home buyer get a DSCR loan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not at the three programs we read. A first-time investor who already owns a home can qualify at some programs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Canadians get a DSCR 