-<li style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The ratio.</strong> Purchases want 1.10 to 1.25 or better. Refinances can go as low as 0.75, but over 1.00 is the goal.</p></li>
-<li style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Your credit.</strong> A score in the high 600s and up.</p></li>
-<li style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The down payment.</strong> 15 to 25 percent on most DSCR purchases here, and more on a condotel. Figures from BrickWood Mortgage.</p></li>
-<li style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Short-term rental income.</strong> Appraisers here often estimate high, so only 75 percent of a short-term estimate counts toward the ratio.</p></li>
