-<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.8rem 0 .6rem">What if the ratio is below 1.00?</h3>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A ratio of 1.00 means the rent exactly matches the payment. Above 1.00, our preferred lender asks for a standard investor down payment. Below 1.00, BrickWood Mortgage still writes the loan, down to a 0.75 ratio, with a larger down payment and a higher rate. Our agents run that ratio on a Grand Strand address before you offer, so you know which side of 1.00 you are on.</p>
