-<p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Local wrinkles</p>
-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Where DSCR loans get tricky on the Grand Strand</h2>
-<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr));gap:1rem">
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem">Buying in an oceanfront tower?</strong> <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Let us check whether the building meets a lender&#39;s warrantable condo guidelines</a>. If it does not, that affects your mortgage and your future sale. Full guide: <a href="/invest/condotel-financing/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">condotel and non-warrantable condo financing</a>.</div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem">Counting on nightly rental income?</strong> Lenders cut 25 percent from the appraiser&#39;s short-term rental estimate before they use it. <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Compare nightly rental with a yearly lease</a>.</div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem">Refinancing after a fix-up?</strong> A DSCR loan is the refinance step of the <a href="/invest/strategies/brrrr/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">BRRRR method</a>: buy, fix, rent, refinance, repeat.</div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem">Test a deal before you commit</strong> Run any Grand Strand address through our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">rental analyzer</a>. It tells you whether the address is a buy or not.</div>
-<div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.1rem 1.3rem;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)"><strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;display:block;margin-bottom:.25rem">We bring the deal</strong> Most agents wait for you to send them listings. Our agents search the Grand Strand for the DSCR deals that work and send them to our investors. One buyer came to us after a year of sending Zillow links to his old agent and hearing yes every time. A DSCR purchase stands on the rent-to-payment math. Finding the property is the hard part, and it is the part most agents leave to you. Our agents screen the Coastal Carolinas MLS and watch for Grand Strand sellers with a reason to move quickly. <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Send us your criteria</a>.</div>
-</div>
-</div></section><section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Let us help with your next investment.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.62);max-width:580px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Send us an address you are looking at, or have us send you an investment property for sale. We will run the rent, the expenses and the association documents before you write an offer, at no cost.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135" style="font-size:1.15rem;letter-spacing:.02em">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is a good DSCR for an investment property?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Most lenders want 1.10 to 1.25 or higher on a purchase. That means the rent covers the payment with room to spare. A 1.00 ratio breaks even. Our preferred lender starts writing DSCR loans at a 0.75 ratio. Below 1.00, BrickWood Mortgage still finances the deal, with a larger down payment and a higher rate.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I get a DSCR loan in South Carolina with no income verification?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. DSCR loans do not use personal income, tax returns, or debt-to-income ratios. The property's rent and the appraisal carry the application, which is the main reason investors choose them over conventional financing.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much down payment does a DSCR loan require?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Expect 15 to 25 percent down on most Grand Strand DSCR loans, from the current BrickWood Mortgage investor programs. Condotels and non-warrantable condos ask for more, and a larger down payment improves both the rate and the qualifying ratio.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I use short-term rental income to qualify?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Sometimes. Some DSCR lenders accept short-term rental income. Around the Grand Strand, appraisers often provide high short-term rental income estimates, but only 75 percent of that figure can be counted as qualified income, so the number used to qualify is more conservative than the appraisal suggests. Long-term lease income is simpler to qualify on.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can a DSCR loan close in an LLC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes, and many investors prefer it. Closing in an LLC keeps a portfolio organized and supports partnerships, and a single-owner LLC does not break a 1031 exchange because the tax rules treat you and that LLC as the same taxpayer. Chapter3 coordinates the property and the loan together so the structure is right at closing.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can I get a DSCR loan if the property does not cash flow?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. BrickWood Mortgage writes DSCR loans down to a 0.75 ratio. That suits beach properties you buy for the appreciation, where the rent does not fully cover the payment. Expect a larger down payment and a higher rate. Above 1.00, the program asks for a standard investor down payment.</p></div></div></section>
-</div>
