x;padding:1.1rem 0 .4rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)}main#main .smf-place h4{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .5rem;line-height:1.3}main#main .smf-place .c3-offer{margin:.2rem 0 .6rem}@media (max-width:379px){main#main .hx-fb,main#main .hx-fb>*{min-width:0;max-width:100%}main#main .hx-fb-ai,main#main .hx-fb-q{min-width:0!important;max-width:100%!important;flex-wrap:wrap;box-sizing:border-box}main#main .hx-fb-q textarea{min-width:0;flex:1 1 100%;width:100%}main#main .hx-fb-go{flex:1 1 100%}}@media (min-width:1000px) and (max-width:1100px){.header-ctas .hdr-phone{display:none!important}}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2){padding:.9rem 0!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{display:block!important;text-align:center!important;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.95),rgba(28,32,40,.97))!important;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14)!important;box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.14),0 26px 60px -30px rgba(28,32,40,.6)!important;border-radius:28px!important;padding:2.2rem 1.6rem!important;margin-left:auto!important;margin-right:auto!important}@media (max-width:699px){main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{padding:1.6rem 1.2rem 1.7rem!important;border-radius:24px!important}}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">About 1,270 buildings of 2 to 4 homes stand in Horry County, most of them near the ocean, and few come up for sale.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On November 10, 2026, 55 buildings listed as 2 to 4 units were for sale in Horry County. Their middle asking price was about $680,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year, 58 sold at a middle price of about $520,000. Those within a quarter mile of the ocean sold for about $842,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you will live in one unit, you can buy a building of up to four units with an FHA or VA loan. On an FHA loan, you may not rent any unit for under 30 days.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us your budget and whether you will live in one unit. We send the buildings that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me buildings that fit</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#steps" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Steps</a></li><li><a href="#for-sale" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">For sale</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where</a></li><li><a href="#rents" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Rents</a></li><li><a href="#worth-it" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Worth it</a></li><li><a href="#live-in-one" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Live in one</a></li><li><a href="#fha-test" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">FHA test</a></li><li><a href="#airbnb" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Airbnb</a></li><li><a href="#duplex-and-fourplex-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Duplex and fourplex FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="steps"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Steps">How do you buy a duplex or fourplex in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A duplex, triplex or fourplex is two, three or four homes in one building, bought in one purchase with one loan. You can live in one unit and rent the others, or rent them all. Buying one takes five steps:</p><ol class="ex-steps"><li><b>Pick the kind of building and the place</b>Buildings by the ocean cost more. Buildings away from the old beach blocks cost less. We send you the buildings for sale on the Grand Strand in the place you pick.</li><li><b>Add up the rent roll</b>The rent roll is the rent from every unit added together. For one building, our agents run the number for each unit from current local leases and listings, at no cost, before you write the offer.</li><li><b>Look at the whole building</b>We go through the expenses and any association documents with you before you write an offer.</li><li><b>Choose how you will pay</b>If you will live in one unit, you can buy it with an FHA, VA or conventional loan. If you will not, you can use an investor loan such as a DSCR loan. We introduce our affiliated lender, BrickWood Mortgage, a separate company, for the numbers.</li><li><b>Offer and close</b>We write the offer with you and work with you up to closing. The seller gives you the state's disclosure form before you both sign the contract, the same form a house comes with.</li></ol></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="for-sale"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="For sale">How many duplexes are for sale in Myrtle Beach, and what do they cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few. Half of the 55 buildings for sale ask between about $485,000 and $980,000.</p><div class="ex-tw"><table class="ex-tab"><caption>Buildings of 2 to 4 units for sale in Horry County, our count on November 10, 2026. Asking prices are rounded.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Mailing address</th><th scope="col">For sale</th><th scope="col">Middle asking price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">North Myrtle Beach</th><td><span class="l">For sale</span>26</td><td><span class="l">Middle asking price</span>about $840,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Myrtle Beach</th><td><span class="l">For sale</span>11</td><td><span class="l">Middle asking price</span>about $715,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Surfside Beach</th><td><span class="l">For sale</span>9</td><td><span class="l">Middle asking price</span>about $575,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Murrells Inlet, Little River, Conway, Atlantic Beach and Longs</th><td><span class="l">For sale</span>9</td><td><span class="l">Middle asking price</span>too few to say</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">All of Horry County</th><td><span class="l">For sale</span>55</td><td><span class="l">Middle asking price</span>about $680,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach has the most and the highest asking prices. We checked each listing's distance to the ocean: 32 of the 55 stand within a quarter mile.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They sell rarely too. 58 sold in the past year, about 4 in every 1,000 home sales in the county. Of those, 45 were duplexes, 5 triplexes and 8 fourplexes. The middle duplex sold for about $512,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where">Where are the duplexes and fourplexes on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By the ocean. Horry County's tax records put about 1,270 parcels with a building under the land-use codes we read as two-, three- and four-family buildings, about 3,000 homes in all.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nearly 3 in 4 of them stand within a mile of the ocean, in a straight line, and more than a third within a quarter mile. Of the 439 with a North Myrtle Beach mailing address, 354 stand within a quarter mile.</p><figure style="margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-where-the-largest-groups" viewBox="0 0 360 364" width="360" height="