roke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">5</text><text class="l" x="15" y="5.3"><tspan x="15">Windtree Estates</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">Where the largest groups of 2 to 4 unit buildings stand, each marked at the middle of its buildings. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><figure class="c3-gchart"><div role="table" aria-label="Buildings of 2 to 4 homes near the ocean sell for more"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Buildings of 2 to 4 homes near the ocean sell for more</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Distance from the ocean, sales</span><span role="columnheader">Middle sale price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Within a quarter mile</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">28 sales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$842,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">A quarter mile to a mile</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">16 sales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.594" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$500,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">1 to 3 miles</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">7 sales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.487" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$410,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">More than 3 miles</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">5 sales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.291" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$245,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle sale price in the past year, by straight-line distance from the ocean, with the number of sales in each group. Two of the 58 sales had no address point to measure.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach towns</h3><div class="smf-place"><h4>North Myrtle Beach's old beach towns</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach was <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess117_2007-2008/prever/1325_20080423.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">formed in 1968 from four beach towns</a>: Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill. About 340 of the city's 439 duplexes, triplexes and fourplexes stand on the old streets of these towns and of Ingram Beach beside them. The middle building in each stands about 160 to 340 yards from the ocean.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.1rem 0 1.3rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Streets of two-story beach houses among trees behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="USGS photo, 2011. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">USGS photo, 2011</a></span></div><figcaption>The streets behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t01c001.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The shag</a> is South Carolina's official state dance, by law since 1984, and the state Senate calls North Myrtle Beach its home. Each November, the <a href="https://www.cammy.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Carolina Beach Music Awards</a> weekend brings beach music bands to the stages of the shag clubs on Main Street.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Within a quarter mile of the ocean, buildings like these sold for about $842,000 at the middle in the past year.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="north-myrtle-beach-duplexes" data-name="North Myrtle Beach" data-head="Live in one, rent the rest in North Myrtle Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Myrtle%20Beach">Get the duplexes for sale in North Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></div><div class="smf-place"><h4>Surfside Beach: Ocean Terrace and Ocean Pines</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/212/Surfside-Beach-Fishing-Pier" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Surfside Beach Fishing Pier</a> is 814 feet long, all concrete, owned by the town and opened in 2024. Walking on it is free.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Terrace has 54 of these buildings and Ocean Pines 32. The middle building in each stands about 0.4 to 0.5 mile from the ocean. In Ocean Terrace, 20 of the 54 are taxed at the owner's 4 percent rate on all or part.</p></div><div class="smf-place"><h4>Garden City</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.pieratgardencity.com/story" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Garden City Pier</a> was rebuilt after Hurricane Hugo destroyed the old one in 1989. At its far end, the rain shelter has a bandstand and a dance floor bar. People learn line dances there, out over the ocean.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Garden City, where the mail goes to Murrells Inlet, has 42 of these buildings, about 0.6 mile from the ocean at the middle. A quarter mile to a mile from the ocean, as here and in Surfside Beach, buildings sold for about $500,000 at the middle.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="surfside-garden-city-duplexes" data-name="Surfside Beach and Garden City" data-head="Your own beach-town rental in Surfside Beach and Garden City"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach%20and%20Garden%20City">Get the duplexes for sale in Surfside Beach and Garden City<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Away from the old beach blocks</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three large groups away from the old beach blocks cost less. The county's middle value for tax is about $230,000 to $255,000 in these groups, and about $447,000 to $685,000 in the largest beach groups. It is a figure for the tax bill, not a sale price.</p><div class="smf-place"><h4>A Place at the River, Little River</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The old Little River waterfront is about a mile from A Place at the River, about 4 minutes by car. Each October, more than 200 vendors and two stages of live music set up there for <a href="https://littlerivershrimpfest.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Little River ShrimpFest</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">All 22 buildings in A Place at the River are duplexes, about 2.7 miles from the ocean.</p></div><div class="smf-place"><h4>Tarpon Bay II, near Forestbrook</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">All 75 buildings in Tarpon Bay II are duplexes, the largest group of them away from the beach. More than 3 miles from the ocean, as here, buildings sold for about $245,000 at the middle, the least of any distance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The neighborhood is near Forestbrook, outside any town limits, about 5 miles from the ocean in a straight line. The nearest beach is about 12 minutes by car.</p></div><div class="smf-place"><h4>Windtree Estates, Myrtle Beach</h4><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Windtree Estates is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, around 62nd to 67th Avenue North. From the middle of it, the beach is about a 15-minute walk. <a href="https://www.mygrandstrandhealth.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Strand Medical Center</a>, a hospital with a heart surgery program, is about 6 minutes by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">All 49 buildings in Windtree Estates are fourplexes. 23 of the 49 are taxed at the owner's rate on all or part, the highest share of the large groups.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="myrtle-beach-duplexes" data-name="Myrtle Beach" data-head="Several rents, one closing: Myrtle Beach duplexes and fourplexes"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Get the duplexes and fourplexes for sale in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="rents"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rents">What does a duplex unit rent for in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In most of Horry County, a 2&#8209;bedroom unit in a building of 2 to 4 units rents for about $1,000 a month. With the utilities the tenant pays, the total is about $1,135.</p><ul class="ex-plain"><li><b>Any unit in these buildings</b>About $950 a month, or about $1,100 with utilities.</li><li><b>A house, for comparison</b>About $1,400 a month in rent.</li><li><b>Bedrooms</b>About 6 in 10 rented units in these buildings have 2 bedrooms, and about 2 in 10 have one.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are the rents tenants pay now, on leases of every age. <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our rent prices guide</a> has what landlords ask for a new lease, by ZIP code. South Carolina does not let a city or county limit rents on privately owned homes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="worth-it"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Worth it">Is a duplex a good investment in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, if you will live in one unit. You can buy it with an FHA or VA home loan. On FHA, the other units' rent can count toward your income. Your own unit can be taxed at the owner's 4 percent rate.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you will rent every unit, the whole building is taxed at 6 percent, and you borrow a smaller share of the price. Then two things count most: what each home costs, and where the building stands.</p><ul class="ex-plain"><li><b>What each home costs</b>Per home, the middle duplex sold for about $256,000. In the same 12 months, a resold house or other home sold for about $350,000 and a resold condo for about $215,000.</li><li><b>Where you buy</b>At the middle, a building within a quarter mile of the ocean sold for more than 3 times as much as one over 3 miles away.</li><li><b>How often one comes up</b>About 4 in every 1,000 home sales in the county are one of these buildings. We send you each new one in your price range as it lists.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/invest/run-the-numbers/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How to run the numbers on a rental</a> lists the costs of owning one building.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us run the rents and costs on one building.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out each unit's rent from current local leases and listings, and the expenses, before you write an offer, at no cost.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="live-in-one"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Live in one">Can you live in one unit and rent the others? FHA and VA in Horry County</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Living in one unit and renting the others is called house hacking. <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/Housing/documents/40001-hsgh-Update-18.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FHA insures loans</a> on buildings of one to four units that the buyer will live in as their main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At least one buyer must move in within 60 days of signing and plan to live there for at least a year.</p><div class="ex-tw"><table class="ex-tab ex-two"><caption>FHA's largest loan in Horry County, 2026</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Building</th><th scope="col">Loan limit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">One home</th><td><span class="l">Loan limit</span>$541,287</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Duplex (2 units)</th><td><span class="l">Loan limit</span>$693,050</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Triplex (3 units)</th><td><span class="l">Loan limit</span>$837,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fourplex (4 units)</th><td><span class="l">Loan limit</span>$1,041,125</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">28 of the 55 buildings for sale ask less than FHA's two-unit loan limit.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Loans that fit a building you live in</h3><ul class="ex-plain"><li><b>FHA</b>Rent from the other units can count toward your income. With no rent history, the lender counts 75 percent of the lower of the appraiser's market rent and the lease.</li><li><b>VA</b>A veteran can <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buy a home of up to 4 units with a VA loan</a>, if the veteran will live in it. <a href="/buyers/va-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our VA loan guide</a> covers who qualifies.</li><li><b>Conventional</b>On <a href="https://sf.freddiemac.com/general/maximum-ltv-tltv-htltv-ratio-requirements-for-conforming-and-super-conforming-mortgages" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freddie Mac's</a> standard loans, the top loan on a 2 to 4 unit building you live in matches its top loan on a one-unit home. Freddie Mac's system must accept the loan. Some of its low down payment programs allow more on a one-unit home only.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When every buyer on the loan will live there, FHA asks the same smallest down payment on a duplex or fourplex as on a one-unit home. If a co-borrower, even a family member, will not live in a 2 to 4 unit building, FHA asks for a much larger down payment.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="/buyers/first-time-home-buyer-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our first-time buyer guide</a> has FHA's other rules.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">If you will not live there</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On Freddie Mac's loans, an investor who lives elsewhere borrows a smaller share of the price. <a href="/invest/strategies/dscr-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">A DSCR loan</a> is one choice: the lender qualifies the loan on the rent, not on your income.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The tax on a building you live in</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In South Carolina, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the home you live in is taxed</a> on 4 percent of its value, once you apply. The rented units on the same property are taxed on 6 percent. <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our property tax guide</a> covers the application.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 1 in 6 of these buildings is taxed at the owner's 4 percent rate on all or part of it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="fha-test"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="FHA test">What is the FHA self-sufficiency test for a triplex or fourplex?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For an FHA loan on a triplex or fourplex, <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/Housing/documents/40001-hsgh-Update-18.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the rents must cover the loan</a>. FHA takes the rent from every unit, including yours, and subtracts 25 percent, or the appraiser's figure for empty months and upkeep if that is larger. The monthly loan payment, taxes and insurance must not be more than what is left.</p><div class="ex-card" role="group" aria-labelledby="smfT"><p class="k" id="smfT">Worked example: FHA's rent test on a fourplex</p><ol class="ex-sum"><li><span>Four 2-bedroom units at about $1,000 a month each</span><b>$4,000</b></li><li><span>Less 25 percent for empty months and upkeep</span><b>&minus;$1,000</b></li><li class="t"><span>The rent FHA counts</span><b>$3,000</b></li></ol><p class="n">FHA uses the appraiser's rent estimates, so your building's figures can differ.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lender must also see savings equal to three months of the full monthly payment, taxes and insurance, left after closing. A duplex does not take the test.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying a triplex or fourplex with FHA?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building. Our affiliated lender, BrickWood Mortgage, a separate company, works out whether its rents pass FHA's test.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="airbnb"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Airbnb">Can you Airbnb a duplex in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not on an FHA loan. On an FHA loan for a 2 to 4 unit building, the buyer signs <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/dfiles/OCHCO/documents/92561.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD's form 92561</a>. On it, the buyer promises not to rent any part of the building for under 30 days, or with hotel services, while the FHA loan is in place.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each town on the Grand Strand has its own rules for nightly rentals. <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our short-term rental rules guide</a> covers them. Renting to summer workers by the season is in <a href="/invest/j1-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our J-1 rentals guide</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="duplex-and-fourplex-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Duplex and fourplex FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the FHA loan limit for a duplex in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">$693,050 for 2026. The limit is the largest loan FHA insures on a duplex here, not the price you pay. It is higher for a triplex or a fourplex.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use a VA loan on a duplex?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A veteran can buy a building of up to four units with a VA loan if the veteran will live in one of them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much down payment does a duplex need if I live in it?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On an FHA loan, the same smallest down payment as a one-unit home, when every buyer on the loan will live there. Our affiliated lender, BrickWood Mortgage, a separate company, gives the numbers for one building.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a fourplex a commercial property?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not for an FHA home loan. FHA's home loan programs cover buildings of one to four homes that the buyer lives in.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does the seller of a duplex have to give a disclosure form?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. The seller of a home of one to four units must give the buyer the state's disclosure form. A duplex or fourplex comes with the same form as a house.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can a South Carolina city cap the rent on my units?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. South Carolina does not let a city or county limit rents on privately owned homes.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/default/files/Housing/documents/40001-hsgh-Update-18.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Handbook 4000.1</a>, <a href="https://www.hud.gov/sites/dfiles/OCHCO/documents/92561.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD-92561</a>, <a href="https://entp.hud.gov/idapp/html/hicostlook.cfm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FHA limits</a>, <a href="https://sf.freddiemac.com/general/maximum-ltv-tltv-htltv-ratio-requirements-for-conforming-and-super-conforming-mortgages" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freddie Mac</a>, <a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-types/purchase-loan/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">VA</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c050.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-50</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c039.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-39</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/acs/microdata.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census ACS</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County parcels</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County deeds</a>. For sale: our count of the listing feed on November 10, 2026. Buildings: county parcels, by our reading of the land-use codes. Sales: deeds of October 2025 to September 2026. Distances are straight lines. Rents: Census, 2020 to 2024, most of Horry County.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":782,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The streets behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach","caption":"The streets behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach.","description":"Streets of two-story beach houses among trees behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"U.S. Geological Survey"},"creditText":"U.S","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (U.S. Geological Survey)","license":"https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX","isBasedOn":"https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Crescent Beach, North Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Legal notice.</strong> Chapter3 Realty Corp is a licensed South Carolina real estate brokerage. It does not make loans. BrickWood Mortgage is our affiliated lender, a separate company. Nothing on this page is a loan offer or tax advice.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Found a duplex or fourplex you like?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Call 854.333.2135, or send us an address, the kind of building you want and your budget. We send the buildings that fit, with the rents and costs on each.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us a building</a></div></section></main>
