y="91.1" width="15.9" height="104.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>September 2025: 513 homes</title></rect><rect x="442.5" y="89.3" width="15.9" height="106.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>October 2025: 522 homes</title></rect><rect x="461.4" y="121.6" width="15.9" height="74.4" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>November 2025: 364 homes</title></rect><rect x="480.3" y="103.2" width="15.9" height="92.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>December 2025: 454 homes</title></rect><rect x="499.2" y="102.4" width="15.9" height="93.6" fill="#c4783a"><title>January 2026: 458 homes</title></rect><text x="499.7" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2026</text><rect x="518.1" y="88.3" width="15.9" height="107.7" fill="#c4783a"><title>February 2026: 527 homes</title></rect><rect x="537.0" y="61.3" width="15.9" height="134.7" fill="#c4783a"><title>March 2026: 659 homes</title></rect><rect x="555.9" y="89.7" width="15.9" height="106.3" fill="#c4783a"><title>April 2026: 520 homes</title></rect><rect x="574.8" y="75.0" width="15.9" height="121.0" fill="#c4783a"><title>May 2026: 592 homes</title></rect><rect x="593.7" y="82.5" width="15.9" height="113.5" fill="#c4783a"><title>June 2026: 555 homes</title></rect><rect x="612.6" y="81.1" width="15.9" height="114.9" fill="#c4783a"><title>July 2026: 562 homes</title></rect><text x="620.5" y="76.1" font-size="11" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1c2028">562</text><rect x="44" y="222" width="10" height="8" fill="#e3bf8f"/><text x="58" y="230" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">Earlier years</text><rect x="154" y="222" width="10" height="8" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="168" y="230" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2026</text></svg></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Period</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes permitted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2024</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">7,152</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2025</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6,898</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">January to July 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3,873</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Same months of 2025</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4,453</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">562</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">January to July 2026 is 13.0 percent below the same months of 2025. Most of the permits are single-family houses in planned communities. <a href="/invest/new-construction-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Buying a new house as a rental</a> has the warranty, the incentives and the recorded rules.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is approved and not yet built</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=80af96d3ac864d068045634ac4365405" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's planning office keeps a map of every major subdivision</a> with the units its zoning allows and the units built. Subtracting one from the other gives the homes that can still be built without a new approval. On September 8, 2026 that was 44,735 units in the unincorporated county: 29,704 houses and 15,028 apartments or condos. The cities keep their own records.</p><div style="max-width:640px;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Approved but unbuilt homes by community, unincorporated Horry County" style="display:block;max-width:640px;font-family:var(--sans)"><text x="122" y="17" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Longs</text><rect x="130" y="3" width="440" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Longs: 5,776 units</title></rect><text x="576" y="17" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">5,776</text><text x="122" y="41" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Carolina Forest</text><rect x="130" y="27" width="375" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Carolina Forest: 4,917 units</title></rect><text x="511" y="41" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">4,917</text><text x="122" y="65" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Surfside</text><rect x="130" y="51" width="371" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Surfside: 4,870 units</title></rect><text x="507" y="65" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">4,870</text><text x="122" y="89" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Burgess</text><rect x="130" y="75" width="292" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Burgess: 3,837 units</title></rect><text x="428" y="89" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">3,837</text><text x="122" y="113" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Little River</text><rect x="130" y="99" width="250" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Little River: 3,281 units</title></rect><text x="386" y="113" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">3,281</text><text x="122" y="137" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Conway South</text><rect x="130" y="123" width="136" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Conway South: 1,784 units</title></rect><text x="272" y="137" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,784</text><text x="122" y="161" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Aynor</text><rect x="130" y="147" width="125" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Aynor: 1,638 units</title></rect><text x="261" y="161" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,638</text><text x="122" y="185" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Bear Bluff</text><rect x="130" y="171" width="120" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Bear Bluff: 1,573 units</title></rect><text x="256" y="185" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,573</text><text x="122" y="209" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Upper Conway</text><rect x="130" y="195" width="119" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Upper Conway: 1,564 units</title></rect><text x="255" y="209" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,564</text><text x="122" y="233" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Garden City</text><rect x="130" y="219" width="95" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Garden City: 1,241 units</title></rect><text x="231" y="233" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,241</text></svg></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county says it updates the layer once a year. 811 of its 1,486 records still carry a February 1, 2019 date, and those hold 10,621 of the remaining units. Treat a count from an old record as an old count. The largest developments, with the date on each record:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Development (community)</th><th styl