1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">398</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pine Ridge is the one to watch. <a href="https://horrycounty.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=3&clip_id=3355" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Council passed a development agreement with Pulte Home Company on August 18, 2026</a>. The tract was entitled to 2,506 homes and the builder agreed to a cap of 2,000. In return the county gets a connection of SC 31 from SC 707 to US 17 Bypass, with the builder paying part of the road. The county also gets land for a recreation center. A resident told council at the vote that building would start about 2029.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city of Conway, <a href="https://www.aol.com/myrtle-beach-area-full-developments-100000068.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Warden Station was annexed in January 2024 with more than 3,300 homes planned</a> on about 1,800 acres along US 701 South. The news report counts 1,380 houses, 1,018 townhomes and 920 apartments. The city's own agreement was not found online. It is not in the county layer because it is inside the city.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the 2025 pace of 6,898 permits a year, the 44,735 approved units are about 6 years of building. <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The rent page</a> has what new supply does to the rent in the areas that get it.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying a rental where the building is?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the area and the budget. We run the numbers with the rent from local leases, and check the approved units around the house before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-being-discussed-but-not-yet-approved"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is being discussed but not yet approved?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">None of these is approved. Each one sits somewhere in the county's or a city's process, and any of them can be changed or voted down.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">372 homes on about 187 acres, the Coles Tract</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 905 at Old Reaves Ferry Road, outside Conway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.postandcourier.com/myrtle-beach/news/development-deal-horry-county-conway-subdivision/article_fd486de6-223e-497c-92a8-a7cbaff6d183.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The planning commission took it up in June 2026</a> and held it after residents spoke against it. County council decides the rezoning.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A 448-site recreational vehicle campground</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Osprey Marina, off Enterprise Road on the Intracoastal Waterway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.myhorrynews.com/news/horry-county-planning-commission-gives-thumbs-up-to-new-campground/article_44bba8d5-68d7-4b7e-9f3c-932aee374369.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The planning commission approved the rezoning on June 4, 2026</a>. It needs three readings at county council before anything is built.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A replacement fire station and a bus operations center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Executive Avenue at Robert M. Grissom Parkway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach passed a first reading to annex the land and rezone it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Coles Tract shows the shape of these deals here. <a href="https://www.postandcourier.com/myrtle-beach/news/development-deal-horry-county-conway-subdivision/article_fd486de6-223e-497c-92a8-a7cbaff6d183.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The applicant offered the county $5,800 a home</a>, about $2 million. On top of that: a traffic signal, turning lanes, 1.2 acres for a fire station, and land for widening SC 905 later. The county trades density for roads and land.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A proposal at this stage is not supply and it is not a reason to pay more for a house nearby. Watch it. Do not price it. A rezoning that fails leaves the land as it was.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-hospitals-are-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which hospitals are being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three. <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/2026-09/2026_August_Archived_CON_Applications.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state's license list</a>, updated August 31, 2026, carries all three with their bed counts and their approval dates from 2021. Each was appealed by competing systems and each survived.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Hospital</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Beds</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">McLeod Health Carolina Forest</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">48</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Carolina Forest</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Ribbon cut August 27, 2026; the hospital says it opens this fall; about $90 million by its latest figure</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">South Strand Hospital (Grand Strand Health)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">59</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 17 Bypass at Sheffield Parkway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Ground broken February 9, 2026; completion reported for late 2027; about $220 million</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Health Carolina Bays</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">36, plus a 24-bed long-term care hospital and a 36-bed rehabilitation hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 at SC 707</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Licensed; appeals resolved in 2023; opening projected for 2028</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Free-standing emergency departments</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Little River (open), Murrells Inlet, Conway (Rivertown), Socastee (late 2026), SC 90 at SC 22 (2027)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two systems: Grand Strand Health and Conway Medical Center</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-offers-preview-of-new-hospital-in-carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLeod cut the ribbon on August 27, 2026</a> on a four-story, 48-bed hospital in Carolina Forest, the first new hospital in Horry County since 2011. <a href="https://www.wmbfnews.com/2026/02/09/its-really-about-access-south-strand-hospital-breaks-ground-220-million-facility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Strand Health broke ground on February 9, 2026</a> on the 59-bed South Strand Hospital across from its existing medical center. <a href="https://wpde.com/news/local/tidelands-health-carolina-bays-new-hospital-horry-county-interchange-highway-31-707-acute-care-provider-medical-surgical-services-heart-care-musc-rehabilitation-encompass-open-in-2028-south-carolina-septmeber-27-2023" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tidelands Health's 36-bed hospital at SC 31 and SC 707</a> cleared its appeals in 2023 with a 2028 target. The system's own page could not be opened for this update.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/news/topic/cmc-breaks-ground-for-new-cmc-socastee-free-standing-emergency-department/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conway Medical Center is building two free-standing emergency departments</a> and no hospital. One is in Socastee, opening late 2026. One is at SC 90 and SC 22, in 2027. A hospital brings traveling nurses on 13-week contracts. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Furnished monthly rentals</a> is the rental they use.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="is-interstate-73-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Is Interstate 73 being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.gov/i-73-project" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state transportation department's own page</a> says right of way is bought from I-95 to US 501. It is nearly bought from US 501 to the Marion County line. From there to SC 22 it is still being bought, through 2026. It also says: funding has not been identified to advance construction on any of the three phases. The northern half, into North Carolina, is on hold.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/interstate-connector/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County has $450 million in its road sales tax for the interstate</a>. It is a local match of up to half the cost from SC 22 to the county line. The match is paid only if the state signs a construction contract for the rest. Nothing has been spent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What changes if it is built? <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess126_2025-2026/bills/4982.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state's published figures</a> put the saving at 33 percent of the drive time on the corridor, worth about $172 million a year by 2040. They put the wider effect at about $3.6 billion and about 20,500 jobs by the same year. Getting out ahead of a storm gets faster.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a rental, the land near the interchanges moves before the rest. On this end that is SC 22 and US 501. The road is not funded, so buy the house on what it earns today and treat the interstate as a gain you did not pay for.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-roads-are-under-construction"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which roads are under construction?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/resources/ride-4/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County's one-percent road sales tax</a> funds most of the work. The 2017 to 2025 program paid for the roads finishing now. The 2025 to 2050 program, approved by voters in November 2024, lists $6.6 billion of projects. Design on the large ones starts between 2025 and 2030. Budgets below are the county's or the state's own figures.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Road</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Budget</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501, SC 31 to SC 544</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Six lanes and new signals</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$41 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Estimated completion fall 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501 realignment, downtown Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New alignment to 7th Avenue North at Oak Street</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$13.9 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Estimated completion fall 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 17 Bypass, SC 707 to Harrelson Boulevard</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four lanes to six</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not stated</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SCDOT told a reporter the end of 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 701, SC 319 to SC 22</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Five lanes north of Conway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$65.1 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Under construction</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 9 east of Loris</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four lanes to SC 66</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$21.7 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Completion planned spring 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Forestbrook Road</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Five lanes, US 501 to Dick Pond Road</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$89.1 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Funded; no schedule on the county page</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway Perimeter Road, phase two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New four-lane road, US 378 to US 701</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$18.4 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Funded; no schedule on the county page</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 south, SC 707 to US 17 Bypass</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New parkway connection, paid through the Pine Ridge agreement</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not stated</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Agreement passed August 18, 2026; a resident told council building starts about 2029</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 north, SC 9 to North Carolina</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New freeway to US 17 at Shallotte</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$797 million, both states</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">North Carolina dropped the preferred route in April 2026 and has no construction money</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 90</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two lanes to four, East Cox Ferry Road to US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$745 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Design 2025 to 2030</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 22 extension</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New highway from US 501 near Aynor to Surfside and Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1.56 billion</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not started; environmental study under way</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway river crossing</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New bridge over the Waccamaw</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$860 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not started</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Finished since 2018: International Drive from Carolina Forest to SC 90, and the widening of Carolina Forest Boulevard. Also the Fred Nash Boulevard extension around the airport runway, Postal Way, and US 701 through Loris. <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/us-hwy-501-sc-hwy-31-to-sc-544/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's project pages</a> carry a budget, the money spent and a date stamp for each road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/news/press-releases/Pages/2026/2026-04-22-public-input-shapes-carolina-bays-parkway-project.aspx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Carolina dropped the preferred route for the SC 31 extension on April 22, 2026</a>, citing public feedback and funding. The two states will look at other routes. South Carolina's share is funded for land purchase only, from 2027.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-else-is-changing-on-the-grand-strand"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What else is changing on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/news/myr-unveils-terminal-expansion-with-ribbon-cutting-celebration/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The airport opened a $93.5 million, six-gate terminal expansion on December 1, 2025</a>, six weeks early and under budget by the county's figures. <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Its own passenger tables</a> show 3,530,754 arriving and departing passengers in 2025, 8.0 percent below the 2024 record. January to July 2026 had 1,881,122, 10.0 percent below the same months of 2025. Spirit, its largest airline in 2025, stopped flying in May 2026. Ten airlines serve it today.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://wpde.com/news/local/city-seeks-proposals-from-experts-for-arts-innovation-district-redevelopment-request-for-qualifications-partner-stormwater-infrastructure-sewer-utilities-vertical" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The City of Myrtle Beach has put $97 million into its downtown district</a>, with $15 million from the state. The money goes to utilities, a 300-seat theater on Main Street and land purchases. The theater was scheduled for summer 2026 and is now expected toward the end of the year. The US 501 realignment onto 7th Avenue North is part of the same work.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach finished a $36 million expansion of its sports complex in November 2025, doubling its ball fields. In May 2026 Horry County approved a $115 million civic center and equestrian arena on Hardwick Road near US 501 and SC 22. It also approved $10 million toward a pool in Carolina Forest.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where-can-you-see-the-permits-near-a-house"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Where can you see the permits near a house?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/gis/permits" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county publishes a map of active permits</a> for the unincorporated county, with the address, the type and the value of each. We read it by machine every month. On September 8, 2026 the newest permit on it was issued September 22, 2025, and it showed 0 permits in the last 30 days. The feed has not been updated since that date, so the zero means the map is stale, not that building stopped. In its last live 30 days it showed 313 permits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://egweb.horrycounty.org/EnerGov_prod/selfservice#/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's live permit system</a> still takes applications and shows records by address. North Myrtle Beach and Conway have their own portals. The City of Myrtle Beach and Surfside Beach publish forms and no online records. For one house, <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the rental analyzer</a> flags nearby permit activity with the numbers. After you buy through us, we tell you when a permit is filed near the property.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the permits pulled for one address?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We check the county map, the city's records and the approved units around it before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-the-building-mean-for-a-rental-buyer"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What does the building mean for a rental buyer?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hospitals are demand. Each one brings traveling nurses on short contracts, and the furnished monthly rental is what they rent. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The mid-term rental page</a> has that market.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Roads change the drive to the beach. A house on a road being widened sits next to a construction site for two years. A house on a finished one is easier to rent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the interstate is built, the land near the SC 22 and US 501 interchanges moves first. It is not funded, so it is a gain you did not pay for rather than a reason to pay more today.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="grand-strand-construction-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Grand Strand construction FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many homes are being built in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders were allowed to start 6,898 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro in 2025 and 3,873 from January to July 2026, by the federal permit count. The unincorporated county has 44,735 more units approved and not yet built, most of them in Longs, Carolina Forest, Surfside and Burgess.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Interstate 73 under construction?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The state has bought right of way from I-95 to US 501 and most of the way to SC 22, and has plans. It says funding has not been identified to build any of the three phases. Horry County's $450 million is a match paid only after the state signs a construction contract.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What new hospitals are being built in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three hold state licenses. McLeod Health Carolina Forest, 48 beds, cut its ribbon in August 2026 and opens this fall. South Strand Hospital, 59 beds, broke ground in February 2026 for late 2027. Tidelands Health Carolina Bays, 36 beds at SC 31 and SC 707, is projected for 2028. Five free-standing emergency departments are open or under way.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which roads are being widened in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">US 501 from SC 31 to SC 544 and the downtown 501 realignment finish in fall 2026. US 701 north of Conway is under construction. The US 17 Bypass is going from four lanes to six between SC 707 and Harrelson Boulevard. SC 90 is in design for 2025 to 2030, and the SC 22 extension is not started.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How often is this page updated?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Monthly. The federal permit count, the county's development layer and the county's permit map are read by machine and the page is rebuilt. The current data runs to July 2026 for permits and September 8, 2026 for the county layer.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MYRT845BPPRIV" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census permits, FRED</a>, <a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=80af96d3ac864d068045634ac4365405" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County development layer</a>, <a href="https://horrycounty.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=3&clip_id=3355" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Council packet, Ordinance 73-2026</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.gov/i-73-project" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT, I-73</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/2026-09/2026_August_Archived_CON_Applications.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">State license list</a>, <a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-offers-preview-of-new-hospital-in-carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLeod Health</a>, <a href="https://www.wmbfnews.com/2026/02/09/its-really-about-access-south-strand-hospital-breaks-ground-220-million-facility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WMBF, South Strand Hospital</a>, <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/resources/ride-4/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIDE 4</a>, <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/us-hwy-501-sc-hwy-31-to-sc-544/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county road projects</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/news/press-releases/Pages/2026/2026-04-22-public-input-shapes-carolina-bays-parkway-project.aspx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCDOT, SC 31</a>, <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport passenger tables</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/gis/permits" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county permit map</a>. Educational only. Dates and budgets are the agencies' own and change; a project with no contract has no date.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying near the building? Have us check the address first.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">One call. The permits around it, the approved units next to it, the road plans, and the rent from local leases.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></section></main>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">What is being built</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Permits, hospitals, roads</p><h1 class="detail-h1">What is being built on the Grand Strand right now?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Houses, hospitals and roads.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Builders were allowed to start 4,978 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro from January through September 2026. One hospital opened. Two more are licensed. The interstate is not being built.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses, mostly. Builders were allowed to start 6,511 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro in 2025, and 4,978 from January to September 2026. That is 3.7 percent below the same months a year earlier.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county has 44,732 more units already approved and not yet built. Most of them are in Longs, Carolina Forest, Surfside and Burgess.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The big projects are two licensed hospitals, four road jobs under way, and the airport terminal that opened in December 2025. McLeod's new hospital in Carolina Forest is now open. Interstate 73 has right of way and plans. It has no construction contract and no money to build.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The numbers come from the federal permit count and the county's own data. The sections below have each number, its date and where it came from.</p><div style="margin-top:1.4rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:2rem;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-is-being-built-in-myrtle-beach-right-now" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What is being built in Myrtle Beach right now?</a></li><li><a href="#how-many-houses-are-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How many houses are being built?</a></li><li><a href="#what-is-being-discussed-but-not-yet-approved" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What is being discussed but not yet approved?</a></li><li><a href="#which-hospitals-are-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which hospitals are being built?</a></li><li><a href="#is-interstate-73-being-built" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Is Interstate 73 being built?</a></li><li><a href="#which-roads-are-under-construction" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which roads are under construction?</a></li><li><a href="#what-else-is-changing-on-the-grand-strand" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What else is changing on the Grand Strand?</a></li><li><a href="#where-can-you-see-the-permits-near-a-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where can you see the permits near a house?</a></li><li><a href="#what-does-the-building-mean-for-a-rental-buyer" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What does the building mean for a rental buyer?</a></li><li><a href="#grand-strand-construction-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Grand Strand construction FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-being-built-in-myrtle-beach-right-now"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is being built in Myrtle Beach right now?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The sections below have the detail and the source for each row.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Houses</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4,978 homes permitted in the metro, January to September 2026; 6,511 in 2025</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Approved and not yet built</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">44,732 units approved through the county's planning office</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Hospitals</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">McLeod Carolina Forest, 48 beds, now open; two more licensed and not yet open, 59 and 36 beds; five free-standing emergency departments</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Interstate 73</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Right of way bought, plans drawn, no construction contract and no construction money</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Roads</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501 to SC 544 and the downtown 501 realignment finishing fall 2026; US 701 north of Conway and the US 17 Bypass six-laning under way</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$93.5 million terminal open since December 2025</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nothing is under construction on Interstate 73. No new bridge to the beach has a contract. The section on roads has what is funded and what is only planned.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="how-many-houses-are-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How many houses are being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www2.census.gov/econ/bps/CBSA%20(beginning%20Jan%202024)/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The federal government counts the homes that local governments permit each month</a>. The count covers the Myrtle Beach metro, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/metro-micro/geographies/reference-files/2023/delineation-files/list1_2023.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">which is Horry County</a>. Each month's figure arrives about four weeks after the month ends. The bars show each month's first count. The year totals below are the Census's own, which add late reports and corrections, so the bars do not add up to them exactly.</p><div style="max-width:640px;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 234" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Homes permitted each month in the Myrtle Beach metro, January 2024 to September 2026" style="display:block;max-width:640px;font-family:var(--sans)"><line x1="44" y1="134.66666666666669" x2="630" y2="134.66666666666669" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="138.66666666666669" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">300</text><line x1="44" y1="73.33333333333334" x2="630" y2="73.33333333333334" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="77.33333333333334" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">600</text><line x1="44" y1="12" x2="630" y2="12" stroke="rgba(28,32,40,.12)"/><text x="39" y="16" font-size="11" text-anchor="end" fill="rgba(28,32,40,.78)">900</text><rect x="45.5" y="70.9" width="14.8" height="125.1" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>January 2024: 612 homes</title></rect><text x="46.0" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2024</text><rect x="63.3" y="63.3" width="14.8" height="132.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>February 2024: 649 homes</title></rect><rect x="81.0" y="57.2" width="14.8" height="138.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>March 2024: 679 homes</title></rect><rect x="98.8" y="59.8" width="14.8" height="136.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>April 2024: 666 homes</title></rect><rect x="116.5" y="28.4" width="14.8" height="167.6" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>May 2024: 820 homes</title></rect><rect x="134.3" y="78.6" width="14.8" height="117.4" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>June 2024: 574 homes</title></rect><rect x="152.0" y="73.5" width="14.8" height="122.5" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>July 2024: 599 homes</title></rect><rect x="169.8" y="98.3" width="14.8" height="97.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>August 2024: 478 homes</title></rect><rect x="187.6" y="88.7" width="14.8" height="107.3" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>September 2024: 525 homes</title></rect><rect x="205.3" y="75.8" width="14.8" height="120.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>October 2024: 588 homes</title></rect><rect x="223.1" y="100.1" width="14.8" height="95.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>November 2024: 469 homes</title></rect><rect x="240.8" y="95.2" width="14.8" height="100.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>December 2024: 493 homes</title></rect><rect x="258.6" y="73.1" width="14.8" height="122.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>January 2025: 601 homes</title></rect><text x="259.1" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2025</text><rect x="276.3" y="72.3" width="14.8" height="123.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>February 2025: 605 homes</title></rect><rect x="294.1" y="61.9" width="14.8" height="134.1" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>March 2025: 656 homes</title></rect><rect x="311.9" y="57.8" width="14.8" height="138.2" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>April 2025: 676 homes</title></rect><rect x="329.6" y="56.0" width="14.8" height="140.0" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>May 2025: 685 homes</title></rect><rect x="347.4" y="74.2" width="14.8" height="121.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>June 2025: 596 homes</title></rect><rect x="365.1" y="66.4" width="14.8" height="129.6" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>July 2025: 634 homes</title></rect><rect x="382.9" y="75.0" width="14.8" height="121.0" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>August 2025: 592 homes</title></rect><rect x="400.7" y="91.1" width="14.8" height="104.9" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>September 2025: 513 homes</title></rect><rect x="418.4" y="89.3" width="14.8" height="106.7" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>October 2025: 522 homes</title></rect><rect x="436.2" y="121.6" width="14.8" height="74.4" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>November 2025: 364 homes</title></rect><rect x="453.9" y="103.2" width="14.8" height="92.8" fill="#e3bf8f"><title>December 2025: 454 homes</title></rect><rect x="471.7" y="102.4" width="14.8" height="93.6" fill="#c4783a"><title>January 2026: 458 homes</title></rect><text x="472.2" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2026</text><rect x="489.4" y="88.3" width="14.8" height="107.7" fill="#c4783a"><title>February 2026: 527 homes</title></rect><rect x="507.2" y="61.3" width="14.8" height="134.7" fill="#c4783a"><title>March 2026: 659 homes</title></rect><rect x="525.0" y="89.7" width="14.8" height="106.3" fill="#c4783a"><title>April 2026: 520 homes</title></rect><rect x="542.7" y="75.0" width="14.8" height="121.0" fill="#c4783a"><title>May 2026: 592 homes</title></rect><rect x="560.5" y="82.5" width="14.8" height="113.5" fill="#c4783a"><title>June 2026: 555 homes</title></rect><rect x="578.2" y="81.1" width="14.8" height="114.9" fill="#c4783a"><title>July 2026: 562 homes</title></rect><rect x="596.0" y="88.3" width="14.8" height="107.7" fill="#c4783a"><title>August 2026: 527 homes</title></rect><rect x="613.7" y="98.5" width="14.8" height="97.5" fill="#c4783a"><title>September 2026: 477 homes</title></rect><text x="621.1" y="93.5" font-size="11" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1c2028">477</text><rect x="44" y="222" width="10" height="8" fill="#e3bf8f"/><text x="58" y="230" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">Earlier years</text><rect x="154" y="222" width="10" height="8" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="168" y="230" font-size="11" fill="#1c2028">2026</text></svg></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Period</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes permitted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2024</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">7,331</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2025</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6,511</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">January to September 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">4,978</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Same months of 2025</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5,171</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">September 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">477</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">January to September 2026 is 3.7 percent below the same months of 2025. Most of the permits are single-family houses in planned communities. <a href="/invest/new-construction-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Buying a new house as a rental</a> has the warranty, the incentives and the recorded rules.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is approved and not yet built</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=80af96d3ac864d068045634ac4365405" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's planning office keeps a map of every major subdivision</a> with the units its zoning allows and the units built. Subtracting one from the other gives the homes that can still be built without a new approval. On November 9, 2026 that was 44,732 units approved through the county's planning office: 29,704 houses and 15,028 apartments or condos. The cities keep their own records.</p><div style="max-width:640px;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Approved but unbuilt homes by community, Horry County planning office layer" style="display:block;max-width:640px;font-family:var(--sans)"><text x="122" y="17" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Longs</text><rect x="130" y="3" width="440" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Longs: 5,776 units</title></rect><text x="576" y="17" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">5,776</text><text x="122" y="41" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Carolina Forest</text><rect x="130" y="27" width="375" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Carolina Forest: 4,917 units</title></rect><text x="511" y="41" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">4,917</text><text x="122" y="65" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Surfside</text><rect x="130" y="51" width="371" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Surfside: 4,870 units</title></rect><text x="507" y="65" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">4,870</text><text x="122" y="89" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Burgess</text><rect x="130" y="75" width="292" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Burgess: 3,837 units</title></rect><text x="428" y="89" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">3,837</text><text x="122" y="113" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Little River</text><rect x="130" y="99" width="250" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Little River: 3,281 units</title></rect><text x="386" y="113" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">3,281</text><text x="122" y="137" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Conway South</text><rect x="130" y="123" width="136" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Conway South: 1,784 units</title></rect><text x="272" y="137" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,784</text><text x="122" y="161" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Aynor</text><rect x="130" y="147" width="125" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Aynor: 1,638 units</title></rect><text x="261" y="161" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,638</text><text x="122" y="185" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Bear Bluff</text><rect x="130" y="171" width="120" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Bear Bluff: 1,573 units</title></rect><text x="256" y="185" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,573</text><text x="122" y="209" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Upper Conway</text><rect x="130" y="195" width="119" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Upper Conway: 1,564 units</title></rect><text x="255" y="209" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,564</text><text x="122" y="233" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" fill="#1c2028">Garden City</text><rect x="130" y="219" width="95" height="18" fill="#c4783a"><title>Garden City: 1,241 units</title></rect><text x="231" y="233" font-size="12" fill="#1c2028">1,241</text></svg></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county says it updates the layer once a year. 811 of its 1,486 records still carry a February 1, 2019 date, and those hold 10,621 of the remaining units. The most recent updates on the layer are from August 2026. Treat a count from an old record as an old count. The largest developments, with the date on each record:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Development (community)</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Approved</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Built</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Left to build</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">County record date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sayebrook East (Surfside)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3,040</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">0</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">3,040</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">February 2019</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Pine Ridge (Burgess)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2,506 by zoning, capped at 2,000 by the August 2026 agreement</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">0</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">up to 2,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The agreement</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sayebrook West (Surfside)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,880</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">217</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,663</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">August 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Palmetto Ranch (Longs)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,292</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">0</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,292</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">February 2019</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Collins Tract (Conway South)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">898, rezoning case filed 2026</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">0</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">898</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">August 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Auberon Woods (Bear Bluff)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,188</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">351</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">837</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tupelo Bay Golf Villas (Garden City)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">800</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">180</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">620</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">August 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Berkshire Village (Carolina Forest)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">729</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">113</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">616</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Bluffs on the Waterway (Carolina Forest)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">935</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">358</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">577</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Bella Vita (Carolina Forest)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,807</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">1,409</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">398</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pine Ridge is the one to watch. <a href="https://horrycounty.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=3&clip_id=3355" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Council passed a development agreement with Pulte Home Company on August 18, 2026</a>. The tract was entitled to 2,506 homes and the builder agreed to a cap of 2,000. In return the county gets a connection of SC 31 from SC 707 to US 17 Bypass, with the builder paying part of the road. The county also gets land for a recreation center. A resident told council at the vote that building would start about 2029. Which builders sell the most homes here, and where, is on our page on <a href="/buyers/new-construction/builders/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the new home builders</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city of Conway, <a href="https://www.aol.com/myrtle-beach-area-full-developments-100000068.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Warden Station was annexed in January 2024 with more than 3,300 homes planned</a> on about 1,800 acres along US 701 South. The news report counts 1,380 houses, 1,018 townhomes and 920 apartments. The city's own agreement was not found online. It is not in the county layer because it is inside the city.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The whole county permitted 6,511 homes in 2025, cities included. At that pace the 44,732 approved units are about 7 years of building. At <a href="https://www2.census.gov/econ/bps/Place/South%20Region/so2025a.txt" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the unincorporated county's own 2025 pace of 4,690 homes</a>, they are about 9 and a half years. <a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The rent page</a> has what new supply does to the rent in the areas that get it.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying a rental where the building is?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the area and the budget. We run the numbers with the rent from local leases, and check the approved units around the house before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-being-discussed-but-not-yet-approved"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is being discussed but not yet approved?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">None of these is approved. Each one sits somewhere in the county's or a city's process, and any of them can be changed or voted down.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">372 homes on about 187 acres, the Coles Tract</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 905 at Old Reaves Ferry Road, outside Conway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.postandcourier.com/myrtle-beach/news/development-deal-horry-county-conway-subdivision/article_fd486de6-223e-497c-92a8-a7cbaff6d183.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The planning commission took it up in June 2026</a> and held it after residents spoke against it. County council decides the rezoning.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A 448-site recreational vehicle campground</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Osprey Marina, off Enterprise Road on the Intracoastal Waterway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.myhorrynews.com/news/horry-county-planning-commission-gives-thumbs-up-to-new-campground/article_44bba8d5-68d7-4b7e-9f3c-932aee374369.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The planning commission approved the rezoning on June 4, 2026</a>. It needs three readings at county council before anything is built.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A replacement fire station and a bus operations center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Executive Avenue at Robert M. Grissom Parkway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach passed a first reading to annex the land and rezone it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Coles Tract shows the shape of these deals here. <a href="https://www.postandcourier.com/myrtle-beach/news/development-deal-horry-county-conway-subdivision/article_fd486de6-223e-497c-92a8-a7cbaff6d183.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The applicant offered the county $5,800 a home</a>, about $2 million. On top of that: a traffic signal, turning lanes, 1.2 acres for a fire station, and land for widening SC 905 later. The county trades density for roads and land.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A proposal at this stage is not supply and it is not a reason to pay more for a house nearby. Watch it. Do not price it. A rezoning that fails leaves the land as it was.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-hospitals-are-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which hospitals are being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two. The third, McLeod's in Carolina Forest, is open to patients, <a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-carolina-forest-hospital-now-open/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLeod announced on October 30, 2026</a>. <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/2026-09/2026_August_Archived_CON_Applications.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state's license list</a>, updated August 31, 2026, carries all three with their bed counts and their approval dates from 2021. Each was appealed by competing systems and each survived.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Hospital</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Beds</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">McLeod Health Carolina Forest</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">48</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Carolina Forest</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-carolina-forest-hospital-now-open/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open to patients, McLeod announced October 30, 2026</a>; ribbon cut August 27, 2026; $90 million by its own figure</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">South Strand Hospital (Grand Strand Health)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">59</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 17 Bypass at Sheffield Parkway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="https://www.wmbfnews.com/2026/02/09/its-really-about-access-south-strand-hospital-breaks-ground-220-million-facility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ground broken February 9, 2026</a>; no opening date from the system; <a href="https://www.mygrandstrandhealth.com/about-us/newsroom/grand-strand-health-commits-over-350-million-dollars-to-expand-and-meet-regional-growth" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">$226 million in its 2025 plan</a></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Health Carolina Bays</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">36, plus a 24-bed long-term care hospital and a 36-bed rehabilitation hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 at SC 707</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Licensed; appeals resolved in 2023; opening projected for 2028</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Free-standing emergency departments</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Little River (open), Murrells Inlet, Conway (Rivertown), Socastee (late 2026), SC 90 at SC 22 (2027)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two systems: Grand Strand Health and Conway Medical Center</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">McLeod's four-story, 48-bed hospital in Carolina Forest <a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/locations/carolina-forest-overview/carolina-forest-new-hospital/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">is now open</a>, the first new hospital in Horry County since 2011. <a href="https://www.wmbfnews.com/2026/02/09/its-really-about-access-south-strand-hospital-breaks-ground-220-million-facility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Strand Health broke ground on February 9, 2026</a> on the 59-bed South Strand Hospital across from its existing medical center. <a href="https://wpde.com/news/local/tidelands-health-carolina-bays-new-hospital-horry-county-interchange-highway-31-707-acute-care-provider-medical-surgical-services-heart-care-musc-rehabilitation-encompass-open-in-2028-south-carolina-septmeber-27-2023" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tidelands Health's 36-bed hospital at SC 31 and SC 707</a> cleared its appeals in 2023 with a 2028 target. The system's own page could not be opened for this update.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/news/topic/cmc-breaks-ground-for-new-cmc-socastee-free-standing-emergency-department/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conway Medical Center is building two free-standing emergency departments</a> and no hospital. One is in Socastee, opening late 2026. One is at SC 90 and SC 22, in 2027. A hospital brings traveling nurses on 13-week contracts. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Furnished monthly rentals</a> is the rental they use.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="is-interstate-73-being-built"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Is Interstate 73 being built?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.gov/i-73-project" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state transportation department's own page</a> says right of way is bought from I-95 to US 501. It is nearly bought from US 501 to the Marion County line. From there to SC 22 it is still being bought, through 2026. It also says: funding has not been identified to advance construction on any of the three phases. The northern half, into North Carolina, is on hold.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/interstate-connector/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County has $450 million in its road sales tax for the interstate</a>. It is a local match of up to half the cost from SC 22 to the county line. The match is paid only if the state signs a construction contract for the rest. Nothing has been spent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What changes if it is built? <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess126_2025-2026/bills/4982.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The state's published figures</a> put the saving at 33 percent of the drive time on the corridor, worth about $172 million a year by 2040. They put the wider effect at about $3.6 billion and about 20,500 jobs by the same year. Getting out ahead of a storm gets faster.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a rental, the land near the interchanges moves before the rest. On this end that is SC 22 and US 501. The road is not funded, so buy the house on what it earns today and treat the interstate as a gain you did not pay for.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-roads-are-under-construction"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which roads are under construction?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/resources/ride-4/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County's one-percent road sales tax</a> funds most of the work. The 2017 to 2025 program paid for the roads finishing now. The 2025 to 2050 program, approved by voters in November 2024, lists $6.6 billion of projects. Design on the large ones starts between 2025 and 2030. Budgets below are the county's or the state's own figures.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Road</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Budget</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it stands</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501, SC 31 to SC 544</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Six lanes and new signals</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$41 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Estimated completion fall 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 501 realignment, downtown Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New alignment to 7th Avenue North at Oak Street</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$13.9 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Estimated completion fall 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 17 Bypass, SC 707 to Harrelson Boulevard</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four lanes to six</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not stated</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SCDOT told a reporter the end of 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">US 701, SC 319 to SC 22</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Five lanes north of Conway</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$65.1 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Under construction</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 9 east of Loris</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four lanes to SC 66</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$21.7 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Completion planned spring 2026</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Forestbrook Road</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Five lanes, US 501 to Dick Pond Road</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$89.1 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Funded; no schedule on the county page</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway Perimeter Road, phase two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New four-lane road, US 378 to US 701</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$18.4 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Funded; no schedule on the county page</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 south, SC 707 to US 17 Bypass</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New parkway connection, paid through the Pine Ridge agreement</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not stated</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Agreement passed August 18, 2026; a resident told council building starts about 2029</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 31 north, SC 9 to North Carolina</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New freeway to US 17 at Shallotte</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$797 million, both states</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">North Carolina dropped the preferred route in April 2026 and has no construction money</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 90</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two lanes to four, East Cox Ferry Road to US 17</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$745 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Design 2025 to 2030</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">SC 22 extension</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New highway from US 501 near Aynor to Surfside and Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1.56 billion</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not started; environmental study under way</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway river crossing</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">New bridge over the Waccamaw</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$860 million</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Not started</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Finished since 2018: International Drive from Carolina Forest to SC 90, and the widening of Carolina Forest Boulevard. Also the Fred Nash Boulevard extension around the airport runway, Postal Way, and US 701 through Loris. <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/us-hwy-501-sc-hwy-31-to-sc-544/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's project pages</a> carry a budget, the money spent and a date stamp for each road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/news/press-releases/Pages/2026/2026-04-22-public-input-shapes-carolina-bays-parkway-project.aspx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Carolina dropped the preferred route for the SC 31 extension on April 22, 2026</a>, citing public feedback and funding. The two states will look at other routes. South Carolina's share is funded for land purchase only, from 2027.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-else-is-changing-on-the-grand-strand"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What else is changing on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/news/myr-unveils-terminal-expansion-with-ribbon-cutting-celebration/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The airport opened a $93.5 million, six-gate terminal expansion on December 1, 2025</a>, six weeks early and under budget by the county's figures. <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Its own passenger tables</a> show 3,530,754 arriving and departing passengers in 2025, 8.0 percent below the 2024 record. January to July 2026 had 1,881,122, 10.0 percent below the same months of 2025. Spirit, its largest airline in 2025, stopped flying in May 2026. Ten airlines serve it today.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://wpde.com/news/local/city-seeks-proposals-from-experts-for-arts-innovation-district-redevelopment-request-for-qualifications-partner-stormwater-infrastructure-sewer-utilities-vertical" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The City of Myrtle Beach has put $97 million into its downtown district</a>, with $15 million from the state. The money goes to utilities, a 300-seat theater on Main Street and land purchases. The theater was scheduled for summer 2026 and is now expected toward the end of the year. The US 501 realignment onto 7th Avenue North is part of the same work.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach finished a $36 million expansion of its sports complex in November 2025, doubling its ball fields. In May 2026 Horry County approved a $115 million civic center and equestrian arena on Hardwick Road near US 501 and SC 22. It also approved $10 million toward a pool in Carolina Forest.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where-can-you-see-the-permits-near-a-house"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Where can you see the permits near a house?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/gis/permits" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county publishes a map of active permits</a> for the unincorporated county, with the address, the type and the value of each. We read it by machine every month. On November 9, 2026 the newest permit on it was issued September 22, 2025, and it showed 0 permits in the last 30 days. The feed has not been updated since that date, so the zero means the map is stale, not that building stopped. In its last live 30 days it showed 313 permits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://egweb.horrycounty.org/EnerGov_prod/selfservice#/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The county's live permit system</a> still takes applications and shows records by address. North Myrtle Beach and Conway have their own portals. The City of Myrtle Beach and Surfside Beach publish forms and no online records. For one house, <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the rental analyzer</a> flags nearby permit activity with the numbers. After you buy through us, we tell you when a permit is filed near the property.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the permits pulled for one address?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We check the county map, the city's records and the approved units around it before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/invest/run-the-numbers/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-the-building-mean-for-a-rental-buyer"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What does the building mean for a rental buyer?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hospitals are demand. Each one brings traveling nurses on short contracts, and the furnished monthly rental is what they rent. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The mid-term rental page</a> has that market.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Roads change the drive to the beach. A house on a road being widened sits next to a construction site for two years. A house on a finished one is easier to rent.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the interstate is built, the land near the SC 22 and US 501 interchanges moves first. It is not funded, so it is a gain you did not pay for rather than a reason to pay more today.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="grand-strand-construction-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Grand Strand construction FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many homes are being built in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders were allowed to start 6,511 homes in the Myrtle Beach metro in 2025 and 4,978 from January to September 2026, by the federal permit count. The county's planning office has 44,732 more units approved and not yet built, most of them in Longs, Carolina Forest, Surfside and Burgess.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Interstate 73 under construction?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The state has bought right of way from I-95 to US 501 and most of the way to SC 22, and has plans. It says funding has not been identified to build any of the three phases. Horry County's $450 million is a match paid only after the state signs a construction contract.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What new hospitals are being built in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">McLeod Health Carolina Forest, 48 beds, is now open. Two more hold state licenses. South Strand Hospital, 59 beds, broke ground in February 2026, and the system has given no opening date. Tidelands Health Carolina Bays, 36 beds at SC 31 and SC 707, is projected for 2028. Five free-standing emergency departments are open or under way.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which roads are being widened in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">US 501 from SC 31 to SC 544 and the downtown 501 realignment finish in fall 2026. US 701 north of Conway is under construction. The US 17 Bypass is going from four lanes to six between SC 707 and Harrelson Boulevard. SC 90 is in design for 2025 to 2030, and the SC 22 extension is not started.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How current is this page?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The permit count runs to September 2026. The county's development layer was read on November 9, 2026, and its most recent updates are from August 2026. The county's permit map has not been updated since September 22, 2025.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www2.census.gov/econ/bps/CBSA%20(beginning%20Jan%202024)/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census permits (CBSA files)</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/metro-micro/geographies/reference-files/2023/delineation-files/list1_2023.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OMB metro delineation, 2023</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/econ/bps/Place/South%20Region/so2025a.txt" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census place file, 2025</a>, <a href="https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=80af96d3ac864d068045634ac4365405" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County development layer</a>, <a href="https://horrycounty.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=3&clip_id=3355" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Council packet, Ordinance 73-2026</a>, <a href="https://projectportal.scdot.gov/i-73-project" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOT, I-73</a>, <a href="https://dph.sc.gov/sites/scdph/files/2026-09/2026_August_Archived_CON_Applications.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">State license list</a>, <a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-offers-preview-of-new-hospital-in-carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLeod Health</a>, <a href="https://www.mcleodhealth.org/news-entry/mcleod-health-carolina-forest-hospital-now-open/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLeod Health, now open</a>, <a href="https://www.mygrandstrandhealth.com/about-us/newsroom/grand-strand-health-commits-over-350-million-dollars-to-expand-and-meet-regional-growth" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Strand Health, 2025 plan</a>, <a href="https://www.wmbfnews.com/2026/02/09/its-really-about-access-south-strand-hospital-breaks-ground-220-million-facility/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WMBF, South Strand Hospital</a>, <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/resources/ride-4/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIDE 4</a>, <a href="https://roads.horrycountysc.gov/projects/us-hwy-501-sc-hwy-31-to-sc-544/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county road projects</a>, <a href="https://www.ncdot.gov/news/press-releases/Pages/2026/2026-04-22-public-input-shapes-carolina-bays-parkway-project.aspx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCDOT, SC 31</a>, <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/media/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport passenger tables</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/gis/permits" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county permit map</a>. Educational only. Dates and budgets are the agencies' own and change; a project with no contract has no date.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Buying near the building? Have us check the address first.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">One call. The permits around it, the approved units next to it, the road plans, and the rent from local leases.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></section></main>
