-## Incorporated or unincorporated: what changes
-Incorporated means the address sits inside a city or town that runs its own services and writes its own rules. Unincorporated means the county does both. It does not show up in a listing, and it changes four bills.
+No place has all of these. Remove one choice to see the closest.
 
-### Sales tax
-Nine percent inside the City of Myrtle Beach, eight percent in the county. Groceries are untaxed either way.
+Compare · Yearly cost · City or county · Questions about the towns
 
-### Trash
-Curbside collection is a city service. Outside city limits you arrange it yourself, and the options and costs are on the new resident checklist .
+## 1. Loris: the most land for the money
+Around Loris, a big yard is normal. More than 4 in 10 house lots are an acre or more, and the usual lot is about 0.8 acre. Near the beach, lots are closer to a sixth of an acre.
+Loris began in 1887 as a railroad depot, and the tracks still run through the middle of downtown. On the third Saturday in October, downtown holds the Bog-Off, with a chicken bog cooking contest, an antique car show and live performances. West of town, Cartwheel Bay Heritage Preserve has a 3.5-mile trail on old roads through longleaf pine, and wild Venus flytraps, pitcher plants and orchids grow along it. It is open dawn to dusk, with no fee.
+U.S. government aerial photo, 2023
+Outside Loris: houses on wide lots along two country roads, with sheds, gardens and farm fields across the road.
 
-### Beach parking
-The free resident parking decal is issued by the city to city residents. Living two streets outside the line means paying at the meters.
+More houses for sale here list parking for an RV or a boat than in any other place on this page. Most list no HOA fee. McLeod Health Loris is the nearest hospital for almost every house.
+Houses around Loris sold for about $280,000, half for more and half for less. A house here also costs the least of any place on this page to keep each year. Our list of the most affordable places near Myrtle Beach goes street by street.
 
-### The HOA is separate from all of it
-City limits decide the four bills above. The covenants on your deed decide how you live in the house, and they apply whether you are inside a town or not. Most newer neighborhoods here have an association; older streets and rural land often do not. Before you offer, read what the covenants say about boats, campers, work vehicles, fences, sheds, pools, exterior paint and pets, and read what the dues cover. We pull the documents for any address, and the HOA guides explain dues increases , special assessments and violations and fines before you are living with them.
+Send me houses in Loris
 
-### Golf carts and rentals
-Each town writes its own golf cart rules, and the county writes them for unincorporated areas, so a cart that is street-legal in one neighborhood may not be in the next. Renting your house out works the same way: the town or county decides, and your HOA can say no on top of that. Check the rules for the specific address, not the town name.
