+## How long can a Canadian stay, and when does U.S. tax residency start?
+Six months without a visa , declared at the border. A stay of 30 days or longer must be registered with the U.S. government, and a Canadian who drove in without an entry record does that online.
+Tax residency is a separate count. The substantial presence test adds every day this year, a third of last year's days, and a sixth of the year before. At 183 you are a U.S. tax resident. About four months every year, every year, is enough to reach it. A snowbird who reaches it but keeps a home and a closer connection to Canada files Form 8840 by the return deadline to stay a nonresident. Miss the form and the exception is lost for that year. Canada keeps taxing you as a resident the whole time.
 
