+## How probate works in South Carolina
+Probate is the court process that moves a deceased person's property to the people who inherit it. In South Carolina it runs through the county probate court, and a personal representative, the person named in the will or appointed by the court, manages the estate. The statute is the South Carolina Probate Code, Title 62 .
 
