+### Do I pay taxes when I sell an inherited house in South Carolina?
+South Carolina has no inheritance tax and no state estate tax. For capital gains, inherited property gets a stepped-up basis: your starting value is the home's fair market value at the date of death, not what the deceased paid. If you sell near that value soon after inheriting, there is often little or no taxable gain. Confirm your numbers with a tax professional.
 
