+### How long does probate take in South Carolina?
+The minimum is about eight months, because creditors get that long to file claims after notice is published. Straightforward estates commonly wrap up within a year. Disputes are what stretch it: an agent at Chapter3 sold one Myrtle Beach house that a disagreement between heirs had kept in probate for more than six years.
 
