-## Builder incentives and the preferred lender
-Builders usually offer incentives instead of price cuts: closing cost credits, design center money, and interest rate buydowns. A price cut lowers the appraised comps for every future sale in the neighborhood, so builders protect the list price and give value in other ways.
-Most incentives are tied to using the builder's preferred lender. Sometimes that is still the best deal. Sometimes the credit is built into the loan terms. The only way to know is to compare complete loan estimates side by side. The advertised rate alone does not show the cost. An investor buyer rarely gets these incentives. How new construction works as a rental .
