-## Why is 90 days the number on the Grand Strand?
-Three rules use the same line. The state accommodations tax applies to stays under 90 consecutive days and stops at 90 continuous days to the same person. Horry County's hospitality fee stops at 90 consecutive days at the same location to the same guest. The City of Myrtle Beach does not count a stay of 90 or more consecutive days as a short-term accommodation.
