-## Carolina Forest home prices in 2026
-The two best reads, each with its own lens: Redfin's Carolina Forest page showed a median sale price of $418,000, up 7.7 percent year over year, with homes going under contract in about 105 days as of mid-2026. SC Realtors data for ZIP 29579 showed a $464,710 single-family median in December 2025, up from $426,500 a year earlier, on 129 days of market time. Condos along the corridor, the area's entry tier, ran a median near $215,500, up about 17 percent.
-Context makes those numbers make sense: the Horry County median sits near $329,000 and the City of Myrtle Beach near $266,000, but both are dragged down by condo-heavy stock. Carolina Forest trades at a premium to the county because it is almost entirely single-family product in amenity communities, and local press has described it as a seller's market even while beach condos favor buyers. Trailing twelve months, roughly 1,330 homes changed hands here. Current numbers for any specific community: ask, and see the July 2026 market report for the region-wide picture.
+## How much of the HOA fee can I deduct if I rent and use the condo?
+You deduct the rented share: rented nights as a share of rented nights plus personal nights. Nights the condo sat empty count on neither side.
+A night rented at a fair price counts as rented, even if you were there that day. A fair price is about what a person not related to you would pay. A rent far below what similar condos nearby charge is not a fair price.
