-### What is the difference between condo master insurance and an HO-6?
-The association buys the master policy for the building and your dues pay for it. You buy the HO-6 for your own unit. The building's recorded papers say where one policy stops and the other starts, and every building sets that line differently.
+### Is South Carolina a 50/50 divorce state?
+No. The law has no equal-split rule, so the judge's split of the house can be more or less than half.
 
-### Does the condo master policy cover the inside of my unit?
-Sometimes. Some master policies cover the finishes that came with the unit. Others stop at the bare walls and cover nothing inside them. Read the insurance section of the recorded papers next to the association's policy. Those two documents together give you the answer.
+### Who pays the mortgage during the divorce?
+Both of you owe the lender while both names are on the loan, so a missed payment is missed for both of you. While the case is open, the Family Court can order temporary support. A support order can make one spouse pay debts for the other, such as the mortgage.
 
-### Who pays the master policy deductible in a South Carolina condo?
-The association pays the insurer, then bills the owners for it as a shared cost. Your share is usually the same share you pay of the regular dues. An unpaid amount becomes a lien on your unit, so the bill does not go away.
