-## Rent it out and you can deduct
-Rent the property to someone else and the fee becomes a normal cost of running a rental. You deduct it against the rent you collect, the same way you deduct insurance, repairs and management fees. That works for a condo and for a house in an HOA.
-There is no separate line for it on the tax form. It gets grouped in with other expenses, and your CPA will handle that. Your job is to keep the association's billing statements. If anyone questions the deduction, the statement is what shows the amount and what it paid for.
