700px){main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:not(:last-child)>.wrap{margin-left:max(2rem,calc((100% - 1200px) / 2 + 2rem))!important}}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2){padding:.9rem 0!important}main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{display:block!important;text-align:center!important;background:linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(42,48,64,.95),rgba(28,32,40,.97))!important;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14)!important;box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.14),0 26px 60px -30px rgba(28,32,40,.6)!important;border-radius:28px!important;padding:2.2rem 1.6rem!important;margin-left:auto!important;margin-right:auto!important}@media (max-width:699px){main#main>section[style^="background:var(--navy)"]:has(>.wrap>h2)>.wrap{padding:1.6rem 1.2rem 1.7rem!important;border-radius:24px!important}}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">The Myrtle Beach market in September: the median house sold for $370,000 and the median condo for $230,125.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In September 2026, the median house sold in Horry and Georgetown Counties went for $370,000, and the median condo for $230,125.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">House prices in this market have been about level for three years. Condos cost about 6 percent less than in 2024, and buyers had more condo offers accepted this year than in either of the last two.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Get this month's sales for your street or building.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me the numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#median-price" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Median price</a></li><li><a href="#are-prices-dropping" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Are prices dropping</a></li><li><a href="#time-to-sell" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Time to sell</a></li><li><a href="#homes-for-sale" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Homes for sale</a></li><li><a href="#month-by-month" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Month by month</a></li><li><a href="#reports" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">All reports</a></li><li><a href="#market-report-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Market report: questions</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="median-price"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Median price">What is the median home price in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From January to September, the median house sold for $362,000 and the median condo for $232,000, close to the September figures. The median is the middle sale: half of the homes sold for more, and half for less.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why do other websites show a different median?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These numbers are sales through the <a href="https://www.ccarsc.org/pages/mls-faqs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCAR MLS</a>, the listing service of the local REALTOR association for Horry and Georgetown Counties. A home sold without a listing on the MLS is not in them.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We checked <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/register-of-deeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County's deed records</a>, which hold those sales too. For the 12 months to September, the middle resale price there was about $215,000 for condos and about $350,000 for the other homes, mostly houses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Areas differ too. CCAR's areas follow ZIP codes or MLS areas, not city limits. Its "Myrtle Beach" area is the two ZIP codes 29572 and 29577.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what homes sold for in your area</a>, from the deeds, see our home value page.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="are-prices-dropping"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Are prices dropping">Are Myrtle Beach home prices dropping?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach house prices are not dropping. The median condo price has fallen two years in a row.</p><figure class="c3-gchart mr-line mr-dots"><span class="cap">House prices stayed level. Condo prices fell two years in a row.</span><svg class="mr-n" viewBox="0 0 260 208" role="img" aria-label="Dot chart of the median sale price from January to September, 2024 to 2026. Houses: $360,000, $365,000, $362,000. Condos: $247,500, $239,000, $232,000."><line x1="0" x2="260" y1="182.3" y2="182.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".16"/><text x="39.1" y="201.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#4a4f5c">2024</text><text x="109.2" y="201.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#4a4f5c">2025</text><text x="176.8" y="201.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#4a4f5c">2026</text><path d="M39.1 57.0L109.2 53.6L176.8 55.6" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="39.1" cy="57.0" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="39.1" y="45.5" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$360,000</text><circle cx="109.2" cy="53.6" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="109.2" y="42.1" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$365,000</text><circle cx="176.8" cy="55.6" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="176.8" y="44.2" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$362,000</text><text x="206.5" y="60.4" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" fill="#8a5226">Houses</text><path d="M39.1 133.7L109.2 139.5L176.8 144.3" fill="none" stroke="#2b4c7e" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="39.1" cy="133.7" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="39.1" y="155.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$247,500</text><circle cx="109.2" cy="139.5" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="109.2" y="161.1" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$239,000</text><circle cx="176.8" cy="144.3" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="176.8" y="165.9" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13.5" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$232,000</text><text x="206.5" y="149.0" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" fill="#2b4c7e">Condos</text></svg><svg class="mr-w" viewBox="0 0 620 248" role="img" aria-label="Dot chart of the median sale price from January to September, 2024 to 2026. Houses: $360,000, $365,000, $362,000. Condos: $247,500, $239,000, $232,000."><line x1="0" x2="620" y1="221.4" y2="221.4" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".16"/><text x="74.4" y="241.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2024</text><text x="260.4" y="241.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2025</text><text x="446.4" y="241.0" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#4a4f5c">2026</text><path d="M74.4 65.6L260.4 61.2L446.4 63.8" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="74.4" cy="65.6" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="74.4" y="53.7" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$360,000</text><circle cx="260.4" cy="61.2" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="260.4" y="49.3" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$365,000</text><circle cx="446.4" cy="63.8" r="5" fill="#c4783a"/><text x="446.4" y="51.9" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$362,000</text><text x="477.2" y="68.7" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#8a5226">Houses</text><path d="M74.4 163.3L260.4 170.7L446.4 176.8" fill="none" stroke="#2b4c7e" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="74.4" cy="163.3" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="74.4" y="185.7" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$247,500</text><circle cx="260.4" cy="170.7" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="260.4" y="193.1" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$239,000</text><circle cx="446.4" cy="176.8" r="5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="446.4" y="199.2" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">$232,000</text><text x="477.2" y="181.7" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#2b4c7e">Condos</text></svg><figcaption>Median sale price from January to September of each year. CCAR MLS sales, Horry and Georgetown Counties.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A median depends on which homes sold that month, so it changes more from one month to the next. The January to September figure is steadier. Our condo guide compares <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how condo prices have done next to houses</a>, over more years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condo buyers did not stay away. From January to September this year, sellers accepted 4,105 offers on condos, more than in the same months of either of the last two years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many condo sellers have already come down. In Horry County, more than half of the condos for sale on November 3 had cut their asking price, <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our buying guide found</a>.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.5rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="782" alt="A row of oceanfront condo and hotel towers of 10 to 15 floors with pools in front, above a beach with umbrellas, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront condo towers on the beach in Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">city of Myrtle Beach</a>, nearly every condo for sale in an oceanfront building sits where the city allows nightly rentals.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="mr-oceanfront-condos-cut" data-name="oceanfront condos with a price cut" data-head="Oceanfront condos already priced below where they started"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/">Send me oceanfront condos with a price cut<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Thinking of a condo? Know its building first.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We pull the building's recent sales, its HOA fee and its insurance before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="time-to-sell"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Time to sell">How long do homes take to sell in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses took about 4 months from listing to an accepted offer from January to September, and condos a little longer. The closing comes after the accepted offer, on the date the contract names.</p><div class="mr-tw"><table class="mr-tab mr-two"><caption>How fast homes sold, and for how much of the asking price</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr">Period</span></th><th scope="col">Houses</th><th scope="col">Condos</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="g"><th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">Days to an accepted offer</th></tr><tr><th scope="row">January to September</th><td>122</td><td>131</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">September alone</th><td>118</td><td>137</td></tr></tbody><tbody><tr class="g"><th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">Share of asking price paid</th></tr><tr><th scope="row">January to September</th><td>97.3%</td><td>96.0%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">September alone</th><td>97.3%</td><td>95.9%</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="nt">The share is of the last asking price, after any price cuts. CCAR MLS sales, Horry and Georgetown Counties.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our selling page shows <a href="/sell/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how long houses wait for an offer in each area</a>, and the months buyers sign the most.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="homes-for-sale"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Homes for sale">How many homes are for sale in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fewer houses were for sale at the end of September than a year before, and the same number of condos. Condos for sale would last almost twice as long as houses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That is months of supply: how long the homes for sale would last at the past year's pace of accepted offers, if no new homes were listed.</p><div class="mr-tw"><table class="mr-tab mr-four"><caption>Months of supply grew in 2024 and 2025, then dipped in 2026.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">September of</th><th scope="col">Houses for sale</th><th scope="col">Condos for sale</th><th scope="col">Months of supply, houses</th><th scope="col">Months of supply, condos</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">2024</th><td><span class="l">Houses for sale</span>3,479</td><td><span class="l">Condos for sale</span>2,886</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, houses</span>3.9</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, condos</span>6.8</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2025</th><td><span class="l">Houses for sale</span>3,994</td><td><span class="l">Condos for sale</span>3,235</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, houses</span>4.3</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, condos</span>7.9</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2026</th><td><span class="l">Houses for sale</span>3,855</td><td><span class="l">Condos for sale</span>3,235</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, houses</span>4.2</td><td><span class="l">Months of supply, condos</span>7.5</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="nt">Homes for sale at the end of September of each year. CCAR MLS, Horry and Georgetown Counties.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This year, months of supply has been lower than a year before in every month since April for houses, and since May for condos.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our buying guide answers <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">whether it is a buyer's market, by price and by town</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">See new listings the day they come on.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the town, the kind of home and your price, and we send you the new ones.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send me new listings</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="month-by-month"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Month by month">How did Myrtle Beach home prices change month by month?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Over the past 12 months, the median house price stayed between about $350,000 and $371,000. The median condo stayed between about $220,000 and $249,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The median condo sold for less than a year before in 10 of the last 12 months.</p><figure class="c3-gchart mr-line"><span class="cap">House prices stayed level this year. Condo prices dipped.</span><svg class="mr-n" viewBox="0 0 260 203" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the median sale price each month, October 2025 to September 2026. Houses stayed between $350,000 and $371,250, ending at $370,000. Condos stayed between $220,000 and $248,500, ending at $230,125."><line x1="72" x2="252" y1="160.7" y2="160.7" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="66" y="165.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="13.5" 