und"/><circle cx="612.0" cy="57.6" r="4.5" fill="#8a5226"/><text x="612.0" y="45.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#8a5226" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">Houses $370,000</text><circle cx="612.0" cy="221.8" r="4.5" fill="#2b4c7e"/><text x="612.0" y="243.5" text-anchor="end" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="#2b4c7e" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="4" stroke-linejoin="round" paint-order="stroke">Condos $230,125</text></svg><figcaption>Median sale price each month for the past 12 months, to September. CCAR MLS sales, Horry and Georgetown Counties.</figcaption></figure><div class="mr-tw"><table class="mr-tab mr-mon"><caption>Median sale price every month, October 2025 to September 2026</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Houses</th><th scope="col">Condos</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Oct 2025</th><td>$365,000</td><td>$234,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Nov 2025</th><td>$365,000</td><td>$248,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Dec 2025</th><td>$367,000</td><td>$235,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jan 2026</th><td>$358,198</td><td>$235,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Feb 2026</th><td>$350,000</td><td>$220,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mar 2026</th><td>$355,000</td><td>$223,900</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Apr 2026</th><td>$368,000</td><td>$231,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">May 2026</th><td>$358,000</td><td>$233,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jun 2026</th><td>$359,450</td><td>$244,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Jul 2026</th><td>$371,250</td><td>$237,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Aug 2026</th><td>$367,000</td><td>$230,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sep 2026</th><td>$370,000</td><td>$230,125</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="reports"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="All reports">Which Myrtle Beach market reports can I read?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We read CCAR's report each month and update this page when the next one is posted. Our other reports stay up, newest first. Every guide on the site is on our <a href="/guides/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guides page</a>.</p><div class="mr-tw"><table class="mr-tab mr-four mr-rep"><caption>Our market reports, newest first</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Report</th><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">This page</th><td><span class="l">Month</span>September 2026 numbers</td><td><span class="l">What it covers</span>Prices, days to an accepted offer and homes for sale, for houses and condos, with three years of trend</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/market-reports/july-2026/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">July 2026 report</a></th><td><span class="l">Month</span>June 2026 numbers</td><td><span class="l">What it covers</span>Sales, prices and homes for sale, the median price by Grand Strand area, and building permits</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Related numbers on other pages</h3><ul class="mr-list mr-rel"><li><a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What homes sold for in your area</a><span class="d2">from Horry County's deed records</span></li><li><a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Is it a buyer's market?</a><span class="d2">by price and by town</span></li><li><a href="/sell/best-time-to-sell/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The best month to list</a><span class="d2">from the county's deeds, month by month</span></li><li><a href="/sell/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How long houses wait for an offer</a><span class="d2">in each part of the Grand Strand, and the busiest months</span></li><li><a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How condo prices have done next to houses</a><span class="d2">and whether a condo or a house is the better investment</span></li><li><a href="/sell/sell-my-condo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Selling a condo in Myrtle Beach</a><span class="d2">the condo market for sellers, and pricing to the buyers a building draws</span></li><li><a href="/invest/what-is-being-built/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How many new homes Horry County permits</a><span class="d2">each month, and the communities approved</span></li><li><a href="/invest/rent-prices/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What homes rent for</a><span class="d2">by number of bedrooms and by area</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="market-report-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Market report: questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the median home price in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Half of the houses sold in Horry and Georgetown Counties in September went for more than $370,000, and half for less. For condos, the middle sale was $230,125.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are Myrtle Beach home prices dropping?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not for houses: the median from January to September was about the same in 2024, 2025 and 2026. The condo median was lower in each of the last two years than the year before.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How long does it take to sell a home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses took 122 days on average from listing to an accepted offer this year, and condos 131. The closing comes after that.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many homes are for sale in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 7,100 houses and condos in Horry and Georgetown Counties at the end of September. At the past year's pace of accepted offers, the condos would last almost twice as long as the houses.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why do websites give different median prices?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Websites count different sales and different areas. These numbers are MLS sales in two counties. County deed records also hold sales never listed, and a site's "Myrtle Beach" can be a city, a ZIP code or a whole county.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.ccarsc.org/clientuploads/2026_Market_Stats/October_2026_Monthly_Market_Report.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCAR Monthly Indicators, September 2026</a>, <a href="https://www.ccarsc.org/pages/marketstats/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCAR market statistics</a>, <a href="https://www.ccarsc.org/pages/mls-faqs/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCAR MLS</a>, <a href="https://www.ccarsc.org/clientuploads/2026_Market_Stats/October_2026_All_Cities.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CCAR Local Market Update</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deeds</a>. Market: CCAR's MLS sales in Horry and Georgetown Counties, current as of October 10, 2026; "house" is CCAR's single-family. Deeds: our count of Horry County's deed records, October 2025 to September 2026.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Oceanfront condo towers on the beach in Myrtle Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-12