" scope="colgroup" class="grp">Lowest</th></tr><tr><th scope="row">Near Loris</th><td><span class="l">Middle price</span>$285,000</td><td><span class="l">Half sold between</span>$225,000 to $355,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">City of Conway</th><td><span class="l">Middle price</span>$265,000</td><td><span class="l">Half sold between</span>$220,000 to $340,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">City of Loris</th><td><span class="l">Middle price</span>$234,000</td><td><span class="l">Half sold between</span>$207,000 to $280,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices-now"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices now">Are home prices dropping in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. House prices in Horry County have been about flat for a year, after rising about half in the four years before.</p><figure style="margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:760px"><svg class="hv-n" viewBox="0 0 300 186" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of house prices in Horry County, as the change since mid-2021, by quarter, from the federal house price index. Prices were about 28 percent lower in early 2016, rose to about 51 percent above mid-2021 by mid-2025, and have been about flat since, at 52 percent above in the latest quarter."><defs><linearGradient id="hvFillhv-n" x1="0" x2="0" y1="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#c4783a" stop-opacity=".28"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#c4783a" stop-opacity="0"/></linearGradient></defs><line x1="51" x2="290" y1="151.9" y2="151.9" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="45" y="157.3" text-anchor="end" font-size="15.5" fill="#4a4f5c">−40%</text><line x1="51" x2="290" y1="124.3" y2="124.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text x="45" y="129.7" text-anchor="end" font-size="15.5" fill="#4a4f5c">−20%</text><line x1="51" x2="290" y