miss here falls to 1.65 percent. It is closer then because there is more data about a home for sale. A listing adds what the county's records do not show: the rooms, the updates, the photos and an asking price. Our agent looks at those things with you before you list, and sends the number with the sales behind it. Before you list, read <a href="/sell/repairs-before-selling/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what to fix before you sell</a> and <a href="/sell/best-time-to-sell/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the best month to list</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get a closer number than an online estimate</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send the online number you have, and an agent tells you how close it is for your home, with the sales behind it. Free, and you do not have to list.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Have us check my online estimate</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="county-value"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Quick numbers">Is the county's value or the nearest sales a good guess at my price?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two quick numbers are often used as a price: the middle price of the six nearest sales, and the county's value, which is the market value on the home's county property record. We checked both against the prices of houses sold this year.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><div role="table" aria-label="How far off two quick numbers were on a typical house"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">How far off two quick numbers were on a typical house</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Quick number</span><span role="columnheader">how far off</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Middle price of the six nearest sales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.805" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">16% off</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The county's value</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.44" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">9% off</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county's value was closer, but it is a mass estimate, made for every home at once, for tax. It is above the price on most condos and below it on most houses: about 7 in 10 condos sold for less than it, and 6 in 10 houses sold for more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Your tax bill is a worse guide. About 2 in 3 Horry County homes are taxed on less than the county's value. A sale resets the value as of December 31 of the year the home sold, so <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">your buyer's tax bill</a> can be higher than yours.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-we-price-it"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How we price it">How is a home's value worked out in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We start from the sales most like your home. The nearest sales, or the sales on your street, can be far off. Here is one Carolina Forest house from the county's records.</p><figure style="margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:760px"><svg class="hv-n" viewBox="0 0 300 218" role="img" aria-label="Dot chart on one price line from $250,000 to 