+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to sell a house in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Houses waited 122 days on average for an accepted offer this year, and condos 131. You and the buyer then agree on the closing date in the contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house as is in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. You make no repairs, and a company that buys to resell pays less than it later sells the house for. You still give the buyer the state's disclosure form."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an attorney to sell my house in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A South Carolina attorney must supervise every home closing in the state. Our agent keeps that attorney, the buyer's side and your lender on the same dates."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house and buy another at the same time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Your offer on the next home can depend on selling the one you own now. You and your buyer can also agree that you stay on after closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What changes if I live in another state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The buyer must hold back part of the price for South Carolina income tax, unless the sale is exempt. If you sign the state's form, the buyer holds back a share of your profit only."}}]}</script>
