-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2.4rem;line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:1.25rem">Myrtle Beach is balanced, leaning buyer-friendly.<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Honest pricing wins.</em></h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem">As of 2026, the Grand Strand has approximately 4.3 months of supply for single-family homes, and condo inventory is at about 7.6 months. Homes not priced and marketed correctly average about 121 days on market, and the sale-to-list ratio is 96%. About 79% of active listings have taken at least one price cut, the clearest sign of overpricing at launch. Sellers who price accurately and market well are still closing quickly. Sellers who overprice sit for months, then chase the market down.</p>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:2rem">The best selling window is February through July. Listings launched in late winter see the most showings and the fastest offers. Understanding this market is step one of every Chapter3 listing.</p>
