-<div class="persona-panel" id="persona-outofstate" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem;background:var(--ivory-2);padding:3rem">
-<div>
-<p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:.75rem">Out-of-State and Remote Sellers</p>
-<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem">"I haven't been down in two years. How do I even start?"</h3>
-<p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem">You own a piece of the Grand Strand from 800 miles away. You know the market has shifted. You're not sure what it's worth now and you've never sold from out of state before.</p>
-<p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Chapter3 handles everything on the ground: lockbox, photography coordination, showings, inspection access, and closing prep. You'll never need to book a flight. SC law permits remote online notarization and electronic signature on all listing and closing documents in most transactions.</p>
-<ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:2rem">
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>Weekly video market updates so you see exactly what buyers see</li>
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>SC nonresident seller withholding (5.21% for 2026) explained before closing, not at it</li>
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>Power of Attorney prep coordinated with closing attorney if needed</li>
-</ul>
-<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Start My Remote Sale →</a>
-</div>
-<div style="background:var(--navy);padding:2.5rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.25rem">
-<p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brass-2)">SC Non-Resident Withholding</p>
-<p style="font-size:.85rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.7);line-height:1.7">When a non-resident sells, the buyer must withhold <strong style="color:var(--ivory)">South Carolina's top individual rate, 5.21% for 2026</strong>, or 5% for a corporation. The closing attorney often does this for the buyer and sends it to the SC Department of Revenue.</p>
-<p style="font-size:.85rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.7);line-height:1.7">This is a significant surprise for many out-of-state owners who discover it at the closing table. We explain it during your pricing consultation so you can plan around it. The withheld amount is credited against your SC income tax liability and is not an additional tax.</p>
-</div>
-</div>
-<div class="persona-panel" id="persona-vacation" style="display:none;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem;background:var(--ivory-2);padding:3rem">
-<div>
-<p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:.75rem">Vacation Home, Condotel, and STR Sellers</p>
-<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem">"I have rental bookings through next summer. Does that complicate the sale?"</h3>
-<p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem">It doesn't have to. Under South Carolina Code Section 27-50-250, <a href="/sell/rental-property/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">a buyer takes title subject to existing vacation rental agreements</a> for periods beginning within 90 days of deed recording. Bookings are transferred or honored; rental income is pro-rated at closing.</p>
-<p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Rental history is a strong selling point for investor buyers. We quantify it: trailing 12-month gross revenue, occupancy rate, and ADR. ADR is average daily rate, the average nightly price a rental earns. We put it in front of buyers who are evaluating cap rates along with list price.</p>
-<ul style="list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:2rem">
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>Condotel financing limitations explained to buyers before offers (FHA/VA ineligible on most)</li>
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>STR revenue data packaged as an investment package for investor outreach</li>
-<li style="font-size:.87rem;color:var(--navy);display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:flex-start"><span style="color:var(--brass);flex-shrink:0">→</span>HOA financial health and special assessment review before listing</li>
-</ul>
-<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Discuss My STR Sale →</a>
