+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/sell/">Sell</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Selling From Out of State</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Selling</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Sell your Grand Strand home from another state.<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">You do not have to come back.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Your Horry County home can sell while you stay in your own state. You sign the deed before a notary there, and the closing here goes ahead without you.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">None of the six steps needs you in South Carolina. We price and show the home, and you sign the contract online. A South Carolina attorney supervises the closing, where the home changes hands.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The buyer holds back part of the price for state income tax, unless it was your main home and your gain, or profit, is tax-free under federal law. For 2026, it is 5.21 percent of your gain if you sign the state's Form I‑295, or of the price less your selling costs if you do not.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 10 buyers here are from another state, and we found no sign that they pay more than local buyers.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Live in another state? Get a price and a closing plan for your home.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me a price and plan</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#sell-from-away" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Selling from away</a></li><li><a href="#agent" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What our agent does</a></li><li><a href="#withholding" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What the state holds back</a></li><li><a href="#price" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where the price goes</a></li><li><a href="#disclosure" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your disclosure</a></li><li><a href="#bookings" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Guest bookings</a></li><li><a href="#who-buys" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underli