v class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Selling from out of state: questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is anything held back if I sell at a loss?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not if you sign Form I‑295. The hold-back is figured on your gain, and a home sold for less than it cost you has no gain. Without the form, it is figured on the price less your selling costs.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does the notary have to be from South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. A notary in the state where you live can notarize the deed, and the act counts the same as a South Carolina notary's. The notary writes in their state and the date their commission ends.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I pay unpaid HOA dues at closing?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually, yes. Unpaid dues are put as a lien on the home and taken out of the seller's money at closing. Our agents check for them before closing, so they do not surprise you.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is fall a bad time to sell to out-of-state buyers?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. More buyers from other states closed in October than in any other month. Even in January, the slowest month, about 1 in 4 buyers came from another state.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Parcels</a>, <a href="https://www.sccourts.org/media/opinions/HTMLFiles/SC/25508.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Doe v. McMaster</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t30c005.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 30-5</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t26c003.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26-3</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t26c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26-6</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t62c008.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">62-8</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c008.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-8-580</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c024.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12-24</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c050.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">27-50</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t37c010.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">37-10-102</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c057.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">40-57-350</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t26c001.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26-1-5</a>, <a href="https://www.scbar.org/for-lawyers/quicklinks/legal-resources/ethics-advisory-opinions/ethics-advisory-opinion-05-16/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Bar 05-16</a>, <a href="https://www.scbar.org/for-lawyers/quicklinks/legal-resources/ethics-advisory-opinions/ethics-advisory-opinion-06-11/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">06-11</a>, <a href="https://www.scbar.org/for-lawyers/quicklinks/legal-resources/ethics-advisory-opinions/ethics-advisory-opinion-00-17/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">00-17</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/news/information-about-h-4216" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC tax rate</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/I295.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Form I-295</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/I290.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Form I-290</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/404mgbzc/prereqs.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry deeds office</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc701" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS 701</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS 409</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/individuals/international-taxpayers/firpta-withholding" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS FIRPTA</a>, <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/about-us/blog/mortgage-closing-scams-how-protect-yourself-and-your-closing-funds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CFPB</a>. Buyers: a year of county sales matched to tax-bill addresses. Not legal or tax advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Oceanfront condo towers in North Myrtle Beach, where more than half of buyers are from another state. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops from its center for the page's share image.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/sell-out-of-state-buyers/north-myrtle-beach-oceanfront-condo-towers-2011-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/sell-out-of-state-buyers/north-myrtle-beach-oceanfront-condo-towers-2011-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":782,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Oceanfront condo towers in North Myrtle Beach, where more than half of buyers are from another state","caption":"Oceanfront condo towers in North Myrtle Beach, where more than half of buyers are from another state.","description":"Three tall oceanfront condo towers with pools behind the dunes in North Myrtle Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean, with houses and a water tow