 resales recorded October 2025 to September 2026, counted by us</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:1rem;max-width:720px">Community fees and figures change; we confirm current numbers with each community before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Carolina Forest FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Carolina Forest part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. It is unincorporated Horry County with a Myrtle Beach mailing address and ZIP 29579, sitting between Myrtle Beach and Conway. That distinction is worth money: homeowners pay no city property tax, while City of Myrtle Beach residents pay an additional 83.4 municipal mills.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What schools serve Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Horry County Schools' Carolina Forest attendance area: Carolina Forest High School, Ten Oaks and Ocean Bay middle schools, and five elementary schools, including Ten Oaks Elementary and Pine Island Elementary, which both opened in August 2025 with 1,200 seats each. Carolina Forest High enrolls about 3,181 students, the fifth-largest high school in South Carolina, ranked 33rd in the state by U.S. News.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How far is Carolina Forest from the beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">About 10 to 15 minutes by car to Grand Strand beaches using US 501, SC 31, or International Drive, depending on the neighborhood and the season. It is the trade the area is built on: newer construction and bigger lots than the beach, a short drive from it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Carolina Forest in a flood zone?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Much of it maps outside FEMA's high-risk zones, but pockets of Zone AE exist near ponds and wetlands, so the parcel matters more than the neighborhood. Check any address against the county flood maps in effect since December 16, 2021. Most of Carolina Forest is inland of Carolina Bays Parkway, outside South Carolina's wind pool territory, so wind coverage stays inside a standard homeowner policy. Homes between Carolina Bays Parkway or River Oaks Drive and the Intracoastal Waterway are inside the territory, where a policy can leave wind out.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you Airbnb a house in Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Usually not. Horry County does not prohibit short-term rentals in unincorporated areas, but most Carolina Forest HOAs do: Avalon's recorded rules prohibit any rental under three months, and several communities require one-year minimum leases. Treat it as a long-term rental market and verify the covenants of the specific community before buying for rental income.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What do homes cost in Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">In the year to September 2026, county deed records show houses in Carolina Forest resold for about $440,000 at the middle and condos for about $172,000.</p></div></div></section>
