or="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="0" y="-35" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="0">Beach</tspan></text><text class="m" x="0" y="-19.5" text-anchor="middle">about 25 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(212.2 312.1)"><g class="k"><rect x="-114.5" y="-24.9" width="101.5" height="52.5" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="-114.5" y="-26.2" width="101.5" height="52.5" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-airport" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="-15" y="-11.2" text-anchor="end"><tspan x="-15">Myrtle Beach</tspan><tspan x="-15" dy="16.5">airport</tspan></text><text class="m" x="-15" y="20.8" text-anchor="end">about 27 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(85 130.2)"><g class="k"><rect x="9.9" y="-38.6" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="9.9" y="-39.9" width="90.7" height="36" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-town" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="11.9" y="-24.9"><tspan x="11.9">University</tspan></text><text class="m" x="11.9" y="-9.4">about 10 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(113.4 145.9)"><g class="k"><rect x="-57.2" y="15.3" width="114.5" height="52.5" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="-57.2" y="14" width="114.5" height="52.5" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-hospital" x="-7.4" y="-7.4" width="14.7" height="14.7" color="#1c2028"/><text class="l" x="0" y="29" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="0">Conway</tspan><tspan x="0" dy="16.5">Medical Center</tspan></text><text class="m" x="0" y="61" text-anchor="middle">about 10 min</text></g></g><g transform="translate(45 65.2)"><g class="k"><g transform="scale(0.8)"><ellipse cx="0" cy="1" rx="7" ry="2.4" fill="#1c2028" opacity=".18"/><path d="M0 0C-3-6-13-14-13-26a13 13 0 1 1 26 0c0 12-10 20-13 26z" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.5"/><use href="#c3r-downtown-conway-home" x="-8.5" y="-34.5" width="17" height="17" color="#ffffff"/></g><text class="h" x="15" y="-14.5"><tspan x="15">Downtown Conway</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg></div><figcaption>Drive times by car from downtown Conway, without traffic. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">Is a Conway address inside the city of Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not. Only a little more than 1 in 4 homes with a Conway mailing address is inside the city limits. The rest are in the county, outside any city.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes with a Conway mailing address, rounded"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes with a Conway mailing address, rounded</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where the home is</span><span role="columnheader">Homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inside the city limits</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.379" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8,300</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Outside, in the county</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">22,000</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The same is true of homes for sale. At our last count, only about 1 in 4 houses for sale with a Conway address was inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the city line changes</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, the property tax is about $670 a year more on a typical house you live in. The City of Conway picks up garbage, recycling and yard waste at the curb once a week for homes in the city, and the city has its own police and fire departments.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the city there is no city pickup. Homes in the county, outside any city, are the only ones allowed to use the county's 25 recycling and convenience centers, where owners bring their own trash.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="parts-of-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Five parts of town">Which part of Conway should you look at?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city's homes fall into five parts. Each has something the others do not. The numbers on the map match the entries below. Each price is what a house or townhouse there usually resold for in the past year, from county deeds.</p><figure class="c3-cw-fig"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-parts-map.svg" width="760" height="830" alt="Map of the city of Conway with its homes shown as dots, coloured by part of town and numbered: 1 downtown, by the Waccamaw River; 2 near the university, off US 501 to the southeast; 3 west and south of downtown, the largest; 4 around Crabtree Swamp, north and northwest of downtown; 5 the north edge. Coastal Carolina University and Conway Medical Center are in part 2." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption>Map of the city's homes, each dot a group of homes, coloured by part of town. The dark square is Coastal Carolina University and the red cross is Conway Medical Center. Map data: Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.</figcaption><ol class="c3-cw-key" aria-label="The five parts of Conway"><li><span class="c3-cw-num p-downtown" aria-hidden="true">1</span><a href="#downtown">Downtown</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num p-us501" aria-hidden="true">2</span><a href="#us-501">Near the university, off US 501</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num p-west" aria-hidden="true">3</span><a href="#west-and-south">West and south</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num p-crabtree" aria-hidden="true">4</span><a href="#crabtree-swamp">Around Crabtree Swamp</a></li><li><span class="c3-cw-num p-north" aria-hidden="true">5</span><a href="#north-edge">The north edge</a></li></ol></figure><h3 id="downtown" data-toc="Downtown" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num p-downtown" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Downtown: a walk to Main Street and the river</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown is the old town on the river. Main Street, City Hall, the Riverwalk and Riverfront Park are all here. Kingston Park on Main Street has shaded tables and a fountain, and the Garden Walk off Third Avenue is a walkway with music and lights in the evening.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="conway-downtown" data-name="Downtown Conway"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An older white wood house with black shutters behind a large live oak, with a paved driveway, in downtown Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>An older house under a live oak, in the downtown historic district.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown here means the streets within about a mile of the center of town, on house lots of about a third of an acre. Snowhill, Mayfair, Buckwood, Highland Park and Collinswood are the largest subdivisions. Few homes here come up for sale. Those that did resold for about $275,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Downtown%20Conway">Get the homes for sale in Downtown Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="us-501" data-toc="Near the university, off US 501" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num p-us501" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>Near the university, off US 501: the university and the hospital</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Along US 501 toward the beach, the city reaches past Coastal Carolina University. Conway Medical Center, on Singleton Ridge Road, and the Conway campus of Horry-Georgetown Technical College are in this part too.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="conway-us-501" data-name="Conway near the university"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/coastal-carolina-kimbel-library-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A red brick library building with white doors behind a wide live oak with long low limbs, at Coastal Carolina University in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: LittleT889. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: LittleT889</a></span></div><figcaption>Kimbel Library at Coastal Carolina University, under a live oak.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Wild Wing, Coastal Point West, Kiskadee Parke and Aviary Village are the largest subdivisions, with about 1,430 homes in all, on lots of about four-tenths of an acre. Homes here resold for about $360,000. Only the north edge was higher.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Conway%20near%20the%20university">Get the homes for sale in Conway near the university<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-and-south" data-toc="West and south" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num p-west" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>West and south: the most homes, three city parks and the lowest prices</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West and south of downtown, toward US 378 and US 701 South, is the largest part of the city. The Billy Gardner Recreation Complex on Mill Pond Road holds the Conway Recreation Center, with an indoor pool and walking track, plus ball fields and a playground built for children of all abilities. Smith Jones Park has an outdoor pool, and Collins Park has tennis and pickleball courts.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="conway-west-and-south" data-name="West Conway"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rosehaven, New Castle, Oak Glenn, Woodland Lakes and Jasmine Woods are the largest subdivisions, on lots of about a quarter of an acre. Homes here resold for about $245,000, the lowest of the five parts.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=West%20Conway">Get the homes for sale in West Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="crabtree-swamp" data-toc="Around Crabtree Swamp" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num p-crabtree" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>Around Crabtree Swamp: north and northwest of downtown, with a park on Sherwood Drive</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North and northwest of downtown, around Crabtree Swamp, are about 2,390 homes, most of them 2 to 4 miles out. Sherwood Park on Sherwood Drive has a playground and a sand volleyball court, and across the street a nine-hole disc golf course inside a walking track.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="conway-crabtree-swamp" data-name="Conway near Crabtree Swamp"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Midtown Village, Rivertown Row, Elmhurst, Woodcreek, Kingston Bay, Sherwood and Country Club Forest are the largest subdivisions. The lots are the smallest in the city, about a fifth of an acre, and homes resold for about $260,000.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Conway%20near%20Crabtree%20Swamp">Get the homes for sale in Conway near Crabtree Swamp<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="north-edge" data-toc="The north edge" class="c3-cw-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-cw-num p-north" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span>The north edge: the biggest lots in the city</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the city's north edge, 4 to 5 miles from downtown, a typical lot is about three-quarters of an acre, the largest in the city. Ridgewood West, Country Manor and Maple Hill are the largest subdivisions, with about 560 homes in all.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="conway-north-edge" data-name="North Conway"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Few homes resold here, and the middle price was about $400,000, the highest of the five parts.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=North%20Conway">Get the homes for sale in North Conway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Conway, SC flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A few parts do. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached in 2018. The rest are near the river, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By part of town, none of the homes near the university are in either flood map. Downtown and at the north edge, about 3 in 100 homes are in one. West and south, it is about 5 in 100, and around Crabtree Swamp about 1 in 10.</p><figure class="c3-cw-fig"><div class="c3-cw-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-conway/conway-city-flood-map.svg" width="760" height="830" alt="Map of the city of Conway: dark dots are its homes; light blue is FEMA's high-risk flood zone and darker blue is where Florence's water reached in 2018. The blue lies along the Waccamaw River, Crabtree Swamp north of downtown around Sherwood, and Kingston Lake. Most dots, including all of those near the university, are outside it." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ul class="c3-cw-legend" aria-label="Map colors"><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#1c2028;border-radius:50%;width:.8rem;height:.8rem"></span>Homes</li><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#8fb3c7"></span>FEMA's high-risk flood zone</li><li><span class="c3-cw-sw" style="background:#2f6f8f;opacity:.75"></span>Where Florence's water reached</li></ul>Map of the two flood maps under the city's homes. Map data: Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The worst flood on record came after Hurricane Florence in 2018. The river gauge at the Conway Marina read about 21 feet, its highest ever. That is the height of the river on the gauge, not the depth of water on a street. Major flooding starts at 14 feet.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/buyers-undisclosed-flooding/conway-florence-floodwater-street-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="844" alt="Floodwater covering a street and the yards of single-story houses, with road signs standing in the water, in the Conway area after Hurricane Florence" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-USGov-Military-National_Guard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: SC National Guard. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: SC National Guard</a></span></div><figcaption>Floodwater on a street of houses in the Conway area after Florence.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why the flood comes late and stays</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The flood here comes down the river, days after the storm. Florence came ashore in North Carolina, and the river at Conway was highest 12 days later.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-cw-fig" style="max-width:640px"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">How high the river at Conway rose on its gauge, in feet, after two hurricanes</span><ul class="c3-cw-legend"><li><span class="c3-cw-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Florence, 2018</li><li><span class="c3-cw-line" style="background:#5c6b78"></span>Matthew, 2016</li><li><svg width="26" height="6" aria-hidden="true" style="flex:none"><line x1="0" y1="3" x2="26" y2="3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".7" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/></svg>Major flooding, 14 ft</li><li><svg width="26" height="6" aria-hidden="true" style="flex:none"><line x1="0" y1="3" x2="26" y2="3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".7" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/></svg>Flood stage, 11 ft</li></ul><svg class="c3-cw-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 252" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the Waccamaw River's height on the gauge at Conway, by days after the storm came ashore. After Florence the river rose past flood stage (11 feet) on day 2, was highest, about 21 feet, on day 12, and stayed above flood stage for 29 days. After Matthew it was highest, about 18 feet, on day 10 and stayed above flood stage for 26 days."><rect x="34" y="8" width="318" height="204" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.55)" rx="6"/><rect x="34" y="8" width="318" height="113.3" fill="#2f6f8f" fill-opacity=".07"/><line x1="34" y1="155.3" x2="352" y2="155.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".6" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/><line x1="34" y1="121.3" x2="352" y2="121.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".6" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><line x1="76" y1="8" x2="76" y2="212" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".35" stroke-width="1"/><path d="M34 179.8L40 179.9L46 180.3L52 180.3L58 179.8L64 179.8L70 178.5L76 152.4L82 114.6L88 110.5L94 112.7L100 110.3L106 102.6L112 94.5L118 87.3L124 81.8L130 78.6L136 77.8L142 79.4L148 82.9L154 88L160 94.2L166 101.6L172 108.9L178 115.6L184 122.1L190 128.4L196 133.6L202 138.1L208 142.4L214 146.5L220 150.7L226 154.4L232 158.3L238 162.6L244 166.8L250 170.2L256 174L262 177.2L268 179.1L274 181.5L280 182.5L286 183.3L292 182.6L298 181.7L304 183L310 184.5L316 186L322 187.6L328 188.4L334 193.4L340 193.5L346 194L352 195.9" fill="none" stroke="#5c6b78" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M40 194.3L46 192.4L52 190.4L58 189.6L64 188.7L70 188.8L76 193.6L82 174.9L88 148.4L94 114.1L100 105L106 109.4L112 103.4L118 84.3L124 64.8L130 51.6L136 44.4L142 41L148 40.5L154 42.5L160 46.4L166 51.7L172 57.9L178 66.3L184 75.4L190 85.3L196 95.6L202 105.9L208 114.8L214 122.9L220 129.7L226 134.9L232 138.7L238 141.8L244 145.2L250 149.6L256 153.7L262 157.4L268 160.9L274 163.8L280 167.8L286 171.1L292 172.7L298 173.9L304 173.6L310 171.2L316 170.1L322 170.3L328 170.4L334 170.4L340 174.4L346 179.5L352 182.9" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="148" cy="40.5" r="4" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5"/><text class="cl" x="148" y="30.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#91592b">Highest, day 12</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="193.8" text-anchor="end">8</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="159.8" text-anchor="end">11</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="125.8" text-anchor="end">14</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="91.8" text-anchor="end">17</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="57.8" text-anchor="end">20</text><text class="ct" x="28" y="23.8" text-anchor="end">23</text><line x1="76" y1="212" x2="76" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="76" y="234" text-anchor="middle">0</text><line x1="136" y1="212" x2="136" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="136" y="234" text-anchor="middle">10</text><line x1="196" y1="212" x2="196" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="196" y="234" text-anchor="middle">20</text><line x1="256" y1="212" x2="256" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="256" y="234" text-anchor="middle">30</text><line x1="316" y1="212" x2="316" y2="217" stroke="#9aa5ae"/><text class="ct" x="316" y="234" text-anchor="middle">40</text><text class="ct" x="193" y="250" text-anchor="middle">Days after the storm came ashore</text></svg><figcaption>Daily average height on the river gauge at the Conway Marina. After Florence, the river stayed above flood stage for 29 days, 20 of them in major flood.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">During Florence, the county closed 58 streets in and at the edge of the city for flooding. Long Avenue, Third Avenue, Church Street and Marina Drive stayed closed about four weeks.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which streets flood at each river height</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The National Weather Service lists what floods as the river rises on the gauge:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">River height</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What floods</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Low areas along Long Avenue and Sherwood Drive, near Crabtree Swamp</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Conway Marina, Elm Street and Marina Drive</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">17 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Main Street and Pecan Grove Boulevard may begin to flood</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21 feet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The US 501 Bypass may flood. Florence reached about 21 feet.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Where Florence's water reached, by subdivision</h3><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Subdivision, and where it is</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Homes Florence's water reached</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Sherwood, around Crabtree Swamp</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">98 of 126</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Midland, just north of downtown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">33 of 49</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Pecan Grove, west and south</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">29 of 103</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Country Club Forest, around Crabtree Swamp</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">21 of 57</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Lakeland, just north of downtown</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">18 of 37</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By the county's map, Florence's water did not reach large parts of Conway. No home in Rosehaven, Oak Glenn, Woodland Lakes, Rivertown Row, Kingston Bay or Snowhill is in either flood map.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How often it happens</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Of the 14 floods on record that reached major flood stage at Conway, 6 came in the last 11 years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For Florence, flood insurance paid 109 claims in the city, and the middle claim was about $134,000. After Hurricane Matthew, the city used FEMA grants to buy 86 buildings. Land bought this way must stay open space.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how to find out if a house flooded</a> shows every record we use.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood-insurance"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood insurance">Do you need flood insurance in Conway, and what does it cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Federal law makes a lender require it only when the house is in FEMA's high-risk zone. A lender can still ask for it anywhere.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the high-risk zone, a flood policy on a house usually costs about $560 to $680 a year, depending on the ZIP code.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Flood policy a year, about</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">ZIP 29526</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">ZIP 29527</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Outside the zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$560</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$680</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Inside the zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$980</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$980</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new federal flood policy takes effect 30 days after the application and payment are complete, unless it is bought when a home loan is made. Buy it with the house, not when a storm is coming.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Conway each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a typical $265,000 house you live in inside the city, the property tax is about $1,700 a year, plus a flood policy if you want one.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Each year, for a $265,000 house</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What you pay</th><th scope="col">Inside the city</th><th scope="col">Just outside it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Property tax, a home you live in</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $1,700</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $1,100, with an $89 county fee</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Flood policy outside the high-risk zone, if you want one</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $560 to $680</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $560 to $680</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tax and flood policy together</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $2,300 to $2,400</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $1,600 to $1,700</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Property tax instead, as a second home or rental</th><td data-label="Inside the city">About $4,300</td><td data-label="Just outside it">About $3,300</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homeowners insurance is a third bill, on top of these. Its price depends on the house, its roof and the company. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a> explains the policies a house here can need.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina taxes a home you live in on 4 percent of its value, and a second home or rental on 6 percent. You must apply for the lower rate. Inside the city, that makes a rental's bill about 2.5 times a home's. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> shows how to apply.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="home-prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Conway, SC?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house or townhouse that resold inside the city in the past year usually went for about $265,000. Half sold for between about $220,000 and $340,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At that price, a house in the city is usually three bedrooms and about 1,400 square feet. That is what we found among the houses for sale inside the city near that price at our last count, about 3 in 4 of them with three bedrooms. Some were new, built in the last two years.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold about 120 new homes in the city in the same year, for about $295,000 in the middle. Few resales were condos, and those went for about $150,000.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What a home usually resold for in the past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What a home usually resold for in the past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town, homes resold</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">36 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.559" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$235,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">17 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.613" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$255,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">327 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.632" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$265,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Socastee</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">296 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.694" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$290,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">1,004 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.73" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$305,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">All of Horry County</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">8,569 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.777" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$325,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">418 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.95" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$395,000</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">961 resales</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$420,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses and townhouses resold by their owners, not by a builder, and not condo units. Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Aynor had only 17 resales.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is not the cheapest town in the county. Homes in Loris and Aynor, two smaller inland towns, resold for less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count, about 670 houses were for sale with a Conway address, more than half of them new construction, and about 60 on an acre or more. Our <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">no-HOA homes guide</a> and <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places</a> include Conway.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="renting-out"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting out">What do homes rent for in Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">HUD's fair market rent for a three-bedroom in the Conway ZIP codes is $1,630 a month. HUD counts rent and utilities together, so the rent alone is less. The figure sits a little under the middle of the market.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Bedrooms</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">HUD fair market rent, ZIPs 29526 and 29527</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,320</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Three</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,630</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,900</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Carolina Forest's ZIP code, the three-bedroom figure is about $600 more.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, students near the college look for the cheapest house that fits their group. People moving to be near the college pay more for a nice house close to campus.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience near the college, August is the best month to find a new tenant, because new students arrive. Start marketing a month before the lease ends. Our <a href="/invest/student-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">student rental guide</a> covers renting near Coastal Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For any address, our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental analyzer</a> gives the rent and the costs. For nightly rentals, see <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what a nightly rental earns by town</a> and <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the short-term rental rules by town</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Conway?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the price, the downtown and the university. The hard ones are flooding in a few places, the city tax and the drive to the beach.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Homes cost less than in the county as a whole, and new homes and land are for sale.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A downtown on the river, with Main Street, the Riverwalk and Riverfront Park.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A university and the hospital inside the city, and city trash pickup each week.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>A few parts flood, and the river stays high for weeks.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The city's property tax is higher than just outside it.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The beach is a drive of about 25 minutes, not a walk.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="conway-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Conway, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC a good place to live?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a buyer who wants a river town with a downtown and a university, at prices under the county's middle, yes. The trade is the drive: the beach is about 25 minutes away by car.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is Conway from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 25 minutes by car from downtown Conway to the beach in Myrtle Beach, without traffic, and about 27 minutes to Myrtle Beach International Airport.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Conway, SC flood?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a few places. About 95 in 100 homes in the city are outside both FEMA's high-risk zone and the land Florence's water reached; most of the rest are near the Waccamaw River, Crabtree Swamp and Kingston Lake.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $654 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value for it. Just outside the city, it pays about $368, plus an $89 county stormwater fee. A second home or rental pays about 2.5 times as much inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live in Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 30,600 in 2025, by the Census Bureau's estimate, up from 24,849 at the 2020 Census.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Conway, SC safe?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Inside the city limits, the City of Conway has its own police department and fire department.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which schools serve Conway, SC?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools assigns schools by address, and one of its attendance areas is named Conway. We look up the assigned schools for any house you like.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census estimates</a>, <a href="https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/CNWS1" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NWS river gauge</a>, <a href="https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02110704/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USGS gauge</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-claims-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood claims</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/smallarea/index.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4013" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 USC 4013</a>, <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-44/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-80/section-80.19" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44 CFR 80.19</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/residents_visitors/about_conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City history</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/departments/parks___recreation/parks.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city parks</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/departments/sanitation.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city trash</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/recyclingcenters.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county recycling</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hospital</a>, <a href="https://www.hgtc.edu/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HGTC</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/71000785" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NRHP record</a>, <a href="https://nces.ed.gov/collegenavigator/?id=218724" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCES</a>. Our counts from county parcels, flood maps and the past year's deeds. Listing counts in aggregate from CCMLS. Drives from downtown, without traffic.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The boardwalk along the Waccamaw River, at the edge of downtown Conway. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waccamaw_River_Warehouse_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Conway City Hall on Main Street, once the county courthouse. Photo: Pollinator at en.wikipedia, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki