-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How many submarkets does Chapter3 cover?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Nine core Grand Strand submarkets: Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Surfside Beach, Garden City, Murrells Inlet, Pawleys Island, Little River, Carolina Forest, and Conway.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Why analyze submarkets separately?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Price, inventory, rental demand, and short-term-rental rules vary widely between Grand Strand towns. A number that is true for Myrtle Beach may be wrong for Conway or Pawleys Island.</p></div></div></section>
