alse"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>Run by the county</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">11,711<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The Intracoastal Waterway and Little River Inlet</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#north-myrtle-beach">North Myrtle <span class="nw">Beach<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>A city</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">18,790<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The ocean beach, and the Cherry Grove channels behind it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#myrtle-beach">Myrtle <span class="nw">Beach<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>A city</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">35,682<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The ocean beach</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#surfside-beach">Surfside <span class="nw">Beach<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>A town</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">4,155<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The ocean beach</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#garden-city">Garden <span class="nw">City<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>Run by two counties</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">10,235<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The ocean beach, and the salt marsh behind it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#murrells-inlet">Murrells <span class="nw">Inlet<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>Run by two counties</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">9,740<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The salt marsh and its creeks, open to the sea at the inlet</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#pawleys-island">Pawleys <span class="nw">Island<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>A town: the island only</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">130<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The ocean beach, and a marsh creek behind it</td></tr><tr class="c3-tg-grp"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="4">Inland</th></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#carolina-forest">Carolina <span class="nw">Forest<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>Run by the county</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">23,342<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The Intracoastal Waterway, at its edge</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a class="c3-tg-name" href="#conway"><span class="nw">Conway<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></span></a></th><td class="c3-tg-kind"><span class="l">Kind of place</span>A city</td><td class="c3-tg-ppl">24,849<span class="u"> people</span></td><td class="c3-tg-water"><span class="l">The water</span>The Waccamaw River</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="c3-tg-notes"><li>Each count of people uses the Census Bureau's outline of the place, which can differ a little from our guide's area. Garden City and Murrells Inlet cross the county line, and each count takes in one side only: Garden City's Horry side and Murrells Inlet's Georgetown side.</li><li>Two more towns sit on the beach without a guide here. Atlantic Beach is between Crescent Beach and Windy Hill, and Briarcliffe Acres is between North Myrtle Beach and Myrtle Beach.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside a city or town, the city adds its own tax, trash pickup and rules. Our 13-town comparison shows <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/#city-or-county" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what changes at the city line</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="how-long"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How long">How long is the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the North Carolina line to the south end of Pawleys Island, the ocean shore is about 48 miles long. To the mouth of Winyah Bay, it is about 63. The City of Myrtle Beach calls the Grand Strand a 60-mile stretch of the coast.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two big cities have the longest beaches: about 10 miles inside Myrtle Beach, and a little over 8 inside North Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pawleys Island has about 3 1/2 miles of ocean beach, and Surfside Beach about 2. More than a third of the shore is outside every town: unincorporated land, Myrtle Beach State Park and Huntington Beach State Park.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="winter"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Winter">Which Grand Strand towns are quiet in winter?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the 2020 Census, Pawleys Island and North Myrtle Beach had the most homes kept for vacations: about 7 in 10 and about 5 in 10.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A street of vacation homes is full in summer and quiet from fall to spring. A street of homes people live in looks much the same in January as in July. If the vacation home would be yours, our <a href="/buyers/second-home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">second home guide</a> covers the tax, the insurance and renting it out.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Out of every 10 homes, how many are kept for vacations?"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Out of every 10 homes, how many are kept for vacations?</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Place</span><span role="columnheader">Homes kept for vacations</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pawleys Island</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.687" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 7 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.484" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 5 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.416" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Garden City</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.395" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 4 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.191" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.162" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 2 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.136" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">about 1 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Carolina Forest (inland)</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.046" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">fewer than 1 in 10</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway (inland)</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.017" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">fewer than 1 in 10</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Homes no one lived in at the 2020 Census, held for vacations or part-time use. The group also takes in timeshares and vacation rentals. Inland places are in gray. Source: U.S. Census Bureau.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our guides answer it for one town: <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/#winter" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">is Garden City busy in winter</a>, and <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/#living" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what the off season is like in Myrtle Beach</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">A busy street all year, or a quiet one in winter?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which you want. We pick the towns and streets that fit, and send the homes for sale there.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Pick my towns</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="each-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Each town">What is each Grand Strand town like?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each place below leads with the thing people love there, then what a home costs. Where a city or town has its own rule on renting by the night, the place says so.</p><div class="c3-tg-town"><h3 id="little-river" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Little River">Little River: on the waterway, by the inlet</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From a dock on the Intracoastal Waterway at Little River, a boat can head north to Norfolk or south to Florida without going out on the ocean.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the ocean, boats go out through Little River Inlet, at the North Carolina line, down a marked channel about 2 miles long. The tide here rises and falls about 4 feet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Resold houses in Little River usually sell for about $357,000.</p></div></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-little-river" data-name="Little River" data-head="Little River, where the boats are: homes for sale now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.87869%2C-78.63932&amp;miles=4">Homes for sale around Little River on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Little%20River">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/little-river/">Read our Little River guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town has-ph"><h3 id="north-myrtle-beach" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="North Myrtle Beach">North Myrtle Beach: the shag on Main Street</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The shag, South Carolina's state dance, is still danced on Main Street. At Fat Harold's Beach Club, the home of the shag, DJs play every night from 7.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city is four old beach towns in one. In 1968, Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill voted to join.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resold house usually sells for about $565,000. A nightly-rental owner needs a yearly city business license, with no special zoning or permit beyond it.</p></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 420px" width="1200" height="755" alt="A postcard of a long wooden pavilion on the beach at Ocean Drive, with Roberts Pavilion and Dancing painted on its end wall and old cars parked beside it" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-US-no_notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Postcard, 1941, public domain. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Postcard, 1941, public domain</a></span></div><figcaption>The pavilion at Ocean Drive Beach on a 1941 postcard, with &quot;Dancing&quot; painted on its end wall.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-north-myrtle-beach" data-name="North Myrtle Beach" data-head="Dance the shag on Main Street: homes in North Myrtle Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.82443%2C-78.71079&amp;miles=4">Homes for sale around North Myrtle Beach on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=North%20Myrtle%20Beach">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/">Read our North Myrtle Beach guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town"><h3 id="myrtle-beach" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Myrtle Beach">Myrtle Beach: the Boardwalk, and the airport in town</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Downtown, the Boardwalk is about 1.3 miles long, beside the ocean. The airport is inside the city, with nonstop flights to more than 50 destinations.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach became a town in 1938. It became a city in 1957, when its permanent population first topped 5,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resold house in the city usually sells for about $540,000. Nightly rentals are allowed only in some of the city's zones, and most neighborhoods of houses are not zoned for them.</p></div></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-myrtle-beach" data-name="Myrtle Beach" data-head="The Boardwalk and the airport in town: Myrtle Beach homes"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.70882%2C-78.88539&amp;miles=3">Homes for sale around Myrtle Beach on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/">Read our Myrtle Beach guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town has-ph"><h3 id="surfside-beach" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Surfside Beach">Surfside Beach: a free pier, and a town of under 2 square miles</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's concrete pier reaches 814 feet into the ocean, and walking on it is free.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach was Roach's Beach, then Floral Beach, before it took the name Surfside Beach in 1952. Much of the land was once the Ark Plantation, and the town was incorporated in 1964.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nightly rentals are allowed only in the two zones by the ocean, where a house sold for about $1 million at the middle. On the inland streets, houses sold for about $485,000 to $540,000.</p></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/surfside-beach-pier-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/surfside-beach-pier-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/surfside-beach-pier-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 420px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Surfside Beach from the air: a long pier labelled Surfside Beach Pier runs from the beach into a green ocean, with rows of houses on the streets behind the sand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Surfside Beach pier from the air, with streets of beach houses behind the sand.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-surfside-beach" data-name="Surfside Beach" data-head="A free pier 814 feet out: homes for sale in Surfside Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.60600%2C-78.97500&amp;miles=1">Homes for sale around Surfside Beach on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/">Read our Surfside Beach guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town"><h3 id="garden-city" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Garden City">Garden City: line dances on the pier</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the far end of the Garden City Pier, people learn line dances out over the ocean.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Behind the beach, about 260 houses between Waccamaw Drive and Business 17 sit on the salt marsh or a tidal creek.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About a third of a mile south of the pier, the line between Horry and Georgetown counties crosses the beach. The pier is on the Horry side.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry part, the middle sale for a condo on the ocean side by the pier was about $320,000.</p></div></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-garden-city" data-name="Garden City" data-head="Beach in front, marsh behind: Garden City homes for sale"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.59107%2C-79.00642&amp;miles=1.5">Homes for sale around Garden City on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Garden%20City">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/garden-city/">Read our Garden City guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town has-ph"><h3 id="murrells-inlet" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Murrells Inlet">Murrells Inlet: restaurants and music on the salt marsh</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The MarshWalk is a wooden boardwalk along the salt marsh, lined with restaurants, and its live music is free to hear.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The inlet opens straight to the ocean between jetties. Outside Garden City, about 220 houses sit within about 100 feet of the inlet's salt marsh, almost all on the creek side of US 17 Business.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The nearest ocean beaches are Huntington Beach State Park and Garden City Beach, each about 9 minutes from the MarshWalk by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Horry side, the middle sale for a house was about $450,000.</p></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-marshwalk-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 420px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet, labelled: restaurant buildings and decks along a boardwalk at the edge of the inlet, Business 17 behind them, marsh islands in the creek and a marina with boats at the bottom" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The MarshWalk from above: restaurants along the boardwalk at the edge of the inlet, and salt marsh islands in the creek.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-murrells-inlet" data-name="Murrells Inlet" data-head="Dinner on the MarshWalk: Murrells Inlet homes for sale"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.54500%2C-79.06500&amp;miles=2">Homes for sale around Murrells Inlet on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Murrells%20Inlet">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/">Read our Murrells Inlet guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town has-ph"><h3 id="pawleys-island" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Pawleys Island">Pawleys Island: old cypress houses by the sea</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The old island houses were built mostly of cypress, hewn on the mainland. Each timber was chiseled with Roman numerals so the house could be put together on the island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The island had about 4 homes for every resident in 2020.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the mainland, west of US 17, a house usually sells for about $580,000. On the island, the middle sale for a house over three years was about $2.45 million, and nightly rentals are allowed.</p></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-pawleys-island/pawleys-island-marsh-walkway-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 420px" width="1200" height="1600" alt="A wooden walkway with a small roofed platform over a tidal creek and marsh grass on Pawleys Island" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Phoebe. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: Phoebe</a></span></div><figcaption>A walkway and a covered platform over the creek on the marsh side of Pawleys Island.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-pawleys-litchfield" data-name="Pawleys Island and Litchfield" data-head="Live near Pawleys Island: homes in Pawleys Island and Litchfield"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.50574%2C-79.13559&amp;miles=4">Homes for sale near Pawleys Island on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Pawleys%20Island">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/">Read our Pawleys Island guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town"><h3 id="carolina-forest" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Carolina Forest">Carolina Forest: trails on the waterway</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county's Bike and Run Park, on the Intracoastal Waterway, has about 7 miles of mountain-bike and hiking trails on 70 acres.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">More people lived in Carolina Forest than in North Myrtle Beach in 2020. It has no city or town government, so there is no city tax.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Carolina Forest, a resold house usually goes for about $440,000.</p></div></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-carolina-forest" data-name="Carolina Forest" data-head="Trails on the waterway: Carolina Forest homes for sale"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.77000%2C-78.92500&amp;miles=3">Homes for sale around Carolina Forest on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Carolina%20Forest">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/">Read our Carolina Forest guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><div class="c3-tg-town"><h3 id="conway" class="c3-tg-h3" data-toc="Conway">Conway: a city on the Waccamaw River</h3><div class="c3-tg-text"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Riverfront Park on the Waccamaw has a playground built like a steamboat, the F.G. Burroughs, beside a riverwalk of about 1.5 miles.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway became a town in 1898, the first of the five cities and towns here to do so. It is the one city of the nine away from the ocean.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resold house or townhouse in the city usually sells for about $265,000. For a nightly rental, we check the city's zoning for each address.</p></div></div><div class="c3-tg-homes"><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-conway" data-name="Conway" data-head="The river city: homes for sale in Conway"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-tg-ask c3-tg-cta"><a class="c3-tg-map-a" href="/homes/map/?near=33.84000%2C-79.05000&amp;miles=3">Homes for sale around Conway on the map<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a> <span class="or">or</span> <a class="c3-tg-req" href="/contact/?place=Conway">ask us to send them</a></p></div></div><p class="c3-tg-guide"><a href="/submarkets/conway/">Read our Conway guide<span class="ar"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><ul class="c3-tg-notes" style="margin-top:2.4rem"><li>Each price is the middle sale from county deed records, for the kind of home that town's guide leads with. Our <a href="/buyers/relocating/which-town/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">13-town comparison</a> draws its own town lines, so its figures differ a little.</li><li>Outside the cities and towns, Horry County's list of what a nightly-rental owner must file names a business license and three tax accounts. It names no rental permit. Outside its towns, Georgetown County requires no business license.</li><li>An HOA or the deed can bar nightly rentals even where the town allows them. Our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a> has each town's rule in full.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Found a home in one of these towns?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We confirm its town, its zoning and the HOA's rules on renting, before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rentals"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Buying a rental">Buying a home to rent out on the Grand Strand?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Start with what a rental earns and where the town allows it:</p><ul class="c3-tg-links"><li><a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How much Myrtle Beach Airbnbs make</a>, by town and by size.</li><li><a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where to buy a rental near Myrtle Beach</a>: by the night at the beach, and by the year inland.</li><li><a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Where Airbnb is legal</a>, city by city.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For one home you like, we read the HOA's rental rules and check the zoning before you offer. We also pull the recent sales near it, so you know what it is worth.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="grand-strand-towns-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Grand Strand towns FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why is it called the Grand Strand?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The name dates from 1949. It was the title of a newspaper column by Claude Dunnagan, and the name stuck for the whole region.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many people live in the Grand Strand towns?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the 2020 Census, Myrtle Beach was the largest of our nine places, with 35,682 residents, and Pawleys Island the smallest, with 130. Conway and Carolina Forest, inland, came next after Myrtle Beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Atlantic Beach part of North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Atlantic Beach is a separate town, and it was not part of the 1968 merger that formed North Myrtle Beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why does the 13-town comparison show different prices?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Both come from county deed records, but each counts a different group of homes. In Conway, this page counts houses and townhouses in the city: about $265,000. The comparison counts houses in its own outline: about $271,000.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/DECENNIALPL2020.P1?g=040XX00US45$1600000" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census P1</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table/DECENNIALDHC2020.H5?g=040XX00US45$1600000" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census H5</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/geographies/reference-files/time-series/geo/gazetteer-files.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gazetteer</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/tiger-line-file.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TIGER/Line</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/guests/about_myrtle_beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MB history</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/our_honorary_namesakes.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">namesakes</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess117_2007-2008/prever/1325_20080423.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.1325</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/207/History" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SB history</a>, <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/residents_visitors/about_conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conway</a>, <a href="https://www.townofpawleysisland.com/about-pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pawleys</a>, <a href="https://nauticalcharts.noaa.gov/publications/coast-pilot/files/cp4/CPB4_C12_WEB.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Coast Pilot</a>, <a href="https://tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tides</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry deeds</a>, <a href="https://gis.gtcountysc.gov/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown GIS</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R986.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Boardwalk</a>, <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/212/Surfside-Beach-Fishing-Pier" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SB pier</a>, <a href="https://www.pieratgardencity.com/story" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GC pier</a>, <a href="https://marshwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MarshWalk</a>, <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/pdfhost/docs/nrhp/text/72001211.PDF" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NRHP 72001211</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county parks</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MB zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.parks.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NMB rentals</a>, <a href="https://www.zoneomics.com/code/surfside-beach-SC/chapter_3" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SB code</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/monjnvh0/sales-tax-chart-short-term-rentals.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry filings</a>, <a href="https://www.gtcountysc.gov/Faq.aspx?QID=116" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Georgetown FAQ</a>. Miles: our TIGER/Line measure. Prices: each guide's middle sale, deeds recorded October 2025 to September 2026; Pawleys Island itself, three years.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">A postcard of a long wooden pavilion on the beach at Ocean Drive, with Roberts Pavilion and Dancing painted on its end wall and old cars parked beside it. Photo: Tichnor Brothers, Boston (publisher), <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-US-no_notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ocean_Drive_Beach_-_Roberts_Pavilion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the scan.</div><div role="listitem">The Surfside Beach Pier from the air, with streets of beach houses behind the sand. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="htt