tp://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 3h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2zM12 7.5v9M7.5 12h9"/></svg></span><span><strong>MarshWalk to hospital</strong><span class="t">4 min</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>MarshWalk to beach</strong><span class="t">9 min</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 12, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Murrells Inlet is the seafood village on a salt marsh south of Myrtle Beach, with the MarshWalk on the Georgetown side and golf neighborhoods on the Horry side.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet has two sides, split by the line between Horry and Georgetown counties. The Horry side has the golf neighborhoods, the new houses from builders and 7 in 10 of the homes. Its middle house price in the past year was about $450,000. The Georgetown side has the MarshWalk, the river landing and the houses on the creek. West of the US 17 bypass, its middle house price was about $570,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you want a house on the creek, plan to wait: only about 7 sell in a year. Your tax bill, your schools and the paperwork to rent a house out depend on the county.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us which side you want. We send the homes that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me Murrells Inlet homes</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which county">Is Murrells Inlet in Horry County or Georgetown County?</h2><style>
