+</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Both. Murrells Inlet is not a town, and its ZIP code, 29576, crosses the county line. Each county runs its own side. The address on the mail does not tell you the county, so we look it up for every home before you see it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">US 17 runs through Murrells Inlet as two roads: the US 17 bypass to the west, and Business 17 nearer the marsh. The map shows both, and the four parts of Murrells Inlet that the two roads and the county line make. Garden City, on the beach to the east, shares the ZIP code and has <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">its own guide</a>.</p><figure class="c3-mi-fig"><div class="c3-mi-frame"><svg class="c3-mi-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 1863" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-mi-map-t"><title id="c3-mi-map-t">Aerial map of the Murrells Inlet mailing area. The Horry and Georgetown county line runs east and west across the middle. North of it, shaded blue, is the Horry side, west of the US 17 bypass. South of it, in Georgetown County, are the Georgetown side west of the bypass (green), a narrow band between the bypass and Business 17 (orange) and the creek side along the inlet (purple), where the MarshWalk is. Garden City, on the beach to the east, has its own guide.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-murrells-inlet/murrells-inlet-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="1863" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M217 920L218 902L228 896L243 876L245 853L252 838L271 832L268 818L271 809L282 803L291 788L292 776L313 738L319 732L342 732L339 721L342 700L355 665L347 635L355 626L365 627L379 623L379 613L385 600L384 571L393 544L414 543L425 547L433 543L439 548L437 563L420 566L412 578L414 583L423 585L429 596L423 618L424 623L443 624L451 633L512 631L521 647L532 640L539 625L562 621L560 599L563 593