+</style><style>@media (min-width:700px){main#main .detail-h1{text-wrap:balance}}main#main .detail-h1 em{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.5vw,2.25rem);line-height:1.25;margin-top:.55rem;text-wrap:balance}@media (max-width:959px){main#main .detail-h1 em{color:var(--g-ink,#8a5226)!important}}main#main .c3-glance li{line-height:1.4}main#main .c3-glance span.t{line-height:1.3}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-glance{grid-template-columns:1fr!important;gap:0!important}main#main .c3-glance li{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;flex-direction:row!important;text-align:left!important;justify-content:flex-start!important;gap:.7rem!important;padding:.55rem 0!important}main#main .c3-glance li:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}}@media (min-width:360px) and (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-glance{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr!important;column-gap:1rem!important}main#main .c3-glance li:nth-last-child(2){border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}}main#main nav[aria-label="On this page"]{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;padding:.8rem 0 .5rem!important}main#main nav[aria-label="On this page"] ul{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));column-gap:1.5rem}@media (min-width:700px){main#main nav[aria-label="On this page"] ul{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}main#main nav[aria-label="On this page"] li a{padding:.45rem 0!important}}main#main .c3-mb-life{gap:0!important}main#main .c3-mb-life li{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;padding:.8rem 0!important}main#main .c3-mb-life li:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main figure.c3ph-hero{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;padding:0!important}main#main figure.c3ph-hero figcaption{padding:0!important}main#main .c3-mb-frame{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:12px!important}main#main .c3-cc{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;padding:0!important}main#main .c3-cc thead th{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.3)!important}main#main .c3-cc th:first-child,main#main .c3-cc td:first-child{padding-left:0}@media (max-width:39.999em){main#main .c3-cc tbody tr{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;margin:0!important;padding:.7rem 0 .75rem!important}main#main .c3-cc tbody tr:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main .c3-cc th,main#main .c3-cc td{padding-left:0!important;padding-right:0!important}}main#main .c3-mb-tiles{column-gap:2rem!important;row-gap:0!important}main#main .c3-mb-tile{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;padding:.8rem 0 .4rem!important}main#main .c3-pc>div{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:2px solid var(--brass)!important;padding:.9rem 0 0!important}main#main .c3-pc{column-gap:2.5rem!important}main#main .c3-cc,main#main .c3-gchart,main#main figure.c3-mb-fig,main#main figure.c3ph-hero,main#main .c3-mb-life,main#main .c3-mb-tiles,main#main .c3-mb-sum,main#main .c3-pc{max-width:720px!important;box-sizing:border-box}@media (min-width:1180px){main#main .c3-mb-beside{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,640px) minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:auto 1fr;column-gap:2.5rem;align-items:start;margin:1.6rem 0 1.4rem}main#main .c3-mb-beside>*{grid-column:1}main#main .c3-mb-beside>figure.c3ph-hero{grid-column:2;grid-row:1/3;margin:.35rem 0 0!important;max-width:none!important}}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach is a city of about 40,900 people on the ocean. About 15 percent more people live here than in 2020.</p><ul class="c3-mb-life"><li><strong>The Boardwalk.</strong> Downtown, the <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R986.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Boardwalk</a> is about 1.3 miles long, beside the ocean. It has a raised wooden boardwalk, a wide section for entertainment, and a winding walk along the ocean.</li><li><strong>A large hospital.</strong> Grand Strand Medical Center is inside the city, about a mile from the ocean. It has a heart surgery program and a trauma center for the most serious injuries.</li><li><strong>The airport.</strong> Myrtle Beach International Airport is inside the city too, less than 2 miles from the ocean. It has nonstop flights to more than 50 cities.</li><li><strong>Golf and shops.</strong> Two golf clubs, Pine Lakes and The Dunes, are in the older neighborhoods described <a href="#older-neighborhoods" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">below</a>. The Market Common, on the south end, has shops, restaurants, a movie theater and two parks.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the off season like?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Quieter, not closed. In the off season, nothing closes except tourist attractions and water parks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hotels, restaurants and other leisure businesses in the county had about 30 percent more workers in July than in January last year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where-to-live"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where to live">Where should you live in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In one of three parts of the city where 7 in 10 or more of the houses are their owners' main homes: Grande Dunes, The Market Common or the older neighborhoods near the golf clubs. Or in a condo, on the oceanfront or off it. For a house near $300,000, look at the <a href="#near-300k" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">two smaller neighborhoods</a> after part 3. To pick a neighborhood by what you want close to home, see <a href="/buyers/best-neighborhoods/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the best neighborhoods in Myrtle Beach</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The numbers on the map show where each part is. The orange areas are where the city allows nightly rentals.</p><figure class="c3-mb-fig" id="rental-map"><div class="c3-mb-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/nightly-rental-zones-map.svg" width="760" height="717" alt="Map of the City of Myrtle Beach, a long strip along the ocean. Orange areas are where the city allows nightly rentals: most of the oceanfront, the Broadway at the Beach area and stretches of the main roads inland. Green areas are zoned for homes only, where it does not. Numbers mark 1 Grande Dunes at the north end, 2 The Market Common at the south end, 3 the older neighborhoods of houses north of downtown, and 4 the oceanfront condos. The airport is inside the city." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ul class="c3-mb-legend" aria-label="Map colors"><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Nightly rentals allowed</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#5f8a6e"></span>Zoned for homes: no rentals under 90 days</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#d9cfa6"></span>Planned neighborhoods such as Grande Dunes: not allowed</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#d4d4cf"></span>Other zones: not allowed</li></ul>Where the City of Myrtle Beach allows nightly rentals: the city's own map of those zones, drawn by us on its current zoning lines. The numbers are the four parts of the city described below. Map data: City of Myrtle Beach zoning; Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.<ol class="c3-mb-key" aria-label="The numbers on the map"><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><a href="#grande-dunes">Grande Dunes</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><a href="#market-common">The Market Common</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><a href="#older-neighborhoods">The older neighborhoods</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><a href="#oceanfront-condo">A condo on the oceanfront</a></li></ol></figcaption></figure><h3 id="grande-dunes" data-toc="Grande Dunes" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Grande Dunes: on the Waterway, with a beach club</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Grande Dunes is a planned community on both sides of the Intracoastal Waterway, the inland water route behind the beach. Every homeowner gets a free household membership to the <a href="https://grandedunescommunities.sites.townsq.io/2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grande Dunes Ocean Club</a>. It has a large pool, a dining room, classes and clubs, and its own way onto the beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The community also has a public marina, a public golf course with holes along the water, a private members' golf course and a tennis club.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 4 in 5 houses here are their owners' main homes. Houses, villas and townhouses resold for about $880,000 in the middle, the highest of the parts in this guide.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="grande-dunes" data-name="Grande Dunes"></div><h3 id="market-common" data-toc="The Market Common" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>The Market Common: shops, a lake and parks</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is a town center with shops, restaurants and a movie theater, and apartments above the stores. It was built on land that was the Myrtle Beach Air Force Base. Our <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/market-common/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Market Common guide</a> covers its neighborhoods, what homes there cost and the airport next door.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/parks-playgrounds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Park and Valor Park</a> are next to the shops. They have a lake with a 1.1-mile path around it, sports fields, picnic areas, fishing spots and Savannah's Playground, built for children of all abilities.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="market-common" data-name="The Market Common"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="900" alt="The Market Common from the air: streets of homes outlined in orange beside a lake, a dot labelled Valor Park at the edge of the shops, and ball fields and a lake labelled Grand Park" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Market Common from the air. The homes outlined in orange are next to the shops and to the lake and ball fields of Grand Park.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 2,500 houses are in the neighborhoods around it, among them Emmens Preserve, The Reserve, Sanctuary at Withers Preserve and Belle Harbor. About 6 in 7 are their owners' main homes, the highest share in this guide. Houses, villas and townhouses here resold for about $500,000 in the middle.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city allows nightly rentals in the town center's zone, which includes a few hundred of these houses. It does not allow them in the other neighborhoods around it. Each neighborhood's HOA can still ban them, and we read its rules for you.</p><h3 id="older-neighborhoods" data-toc="The older neighborhoods" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>The older neighborhoods: golf and streets by the ocean</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These neighborhoods are built around two golf clubs. <a href="https://pinelakes.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Lakes Country Club</a> opened in 1927 as Myrtle Beach's first golf course. <a href="https://www.thedunesclub.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Dunes Golf and Beach Club</a>, on the ocean, hosts a PGA Tour event, the Myrtle Beach Classic.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Heights, Oak Park, Forest Dunes and Northwood are here too. On some streets, the houses face the beach across wide lawns.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="pine-lakes" data-name="Pine Lakes" data-head="Homes for sale near Pine Lakes now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Two-story houses on wide green lawns behind the dunes, with wooden walkways to the beach and oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on wide lawns facing the beach, on the older streets north of downtown Myrtle Beach.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nightly rentals are not allowed here, and about 7 in 10 houses are their owners' main homes. Houses resold for about $550,000 in the middle, with a wide range from street to street.</p><h3 id="near-300k" data-toc="Houses near $300,000" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Where are the houses near $300,000?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In a few smaller neighborhoods. Houses in the city resold for about $540,000 in the middle in the past year, and only about 1 in 6 sold for $350,000 or less. Of the 869 homes for sale in the city at $300,000 or less, only 8 are houses. The rest are condos and townhouses.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Where houses resold near $300,000 in the past year (12 to 25 sales each)</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Neighborhood</th><th scope="col">Middle resale price, houses</th><th scope="col">Houses in the high-risk flood zone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Bent Oak Estates</th><td data-label="Middle resale price, houses">About $245,000</td><td data-label="Houses in the high-risk flood zone">Almost none</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Meridian</th><td data-label="Middle resale price, houses">About $350,000</td><td data-label="Houses in the high-risk flood zone">About 2 in 5</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Summit at Meridian</th><td data-label="Middle resale price, houses">About $420,000</td><td data-label="Houses in the high-risk flood zone">About 2 in 5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Bent Oak Estates, off Pridgen Road, had the most house sales at $350,000 or less. It has about 150 houses, about a mile from the beach and from the airport. About 7 in 10 are their owners' main homes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Meridian and Summit at Meridian, west of the airport, are one planned development of 513 houses. Of the city's zoning districts with 50 or more houses, it has the highest share in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. Nightly rentals are not allowed in any of the three.</p><h3 id="oceanfront-condo" data-toc="A condo on the oceanfront" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>A condo on the oceanfront</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can live in a condo too. Nearly every oceanfront condo building is where the city allows nightly rentals, so most of your neighbors there will be guests. Only about 1 in 18 condos there is someone's main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Off the oceanfront, where nightly rentals are not allowed, about 1 in 3 condos is its owner's main home. Those condos resold for about $270,000 in the middle, more than oceanfront condos, but there were only a few dozen sales. The <a href="#oceanfront-buildings" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">oceanfront buildings</a> are next.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Tour the part of the city you like</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which part of Myrtle Beach fits you. We set up showings of the homes for sale there.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Book a showing in Myrtle Beach</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="nightly-rentals"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Nightly rentals">Can you rent a home by the night in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most condos, yes. Almost every house, no. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, nightly rentals are legal only in the zones where the city allows them, and any stay shorter than 90 days counts.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those zones include most of the oceanfront hotel and condo strip, the Broadway at the Beach area, stretches of the US 17 Bypass and US 501, and The Market Common's town center. They are the orange areas on the <a href="#rental-map" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">map</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city bans nightly rentals in every zone for homes, except one zone set aside for visitor stays. A house outside the allowed zones cannot be switched over to nightly rentals. Breaking the rule is a misdemeanor, with a fine, jail time or both for each violation.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Which homes in the City of Myrtle Beach can rent by the night</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Kind of home</th><th scope="col">Homes in the city</th><th scope="col">Can rent by the night</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Condos</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 16,900</td><td data-label="Can rent by the night">About 3 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Houses</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 10,300</td><td data-label="Can rent by the night">About 4 in 100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Villas and townhouses</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 850</td><td data-label="Can rent by the night">About 3 in 5</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="c3-mb-beside"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Older two-story houses on lawns along the beach at left, and two tall condo towers on the beach at right, with streets of houses under oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses and condo towers on the same beach in Myrtle Beach. The houses on the left are in a zone where nightly rentals are not allowed. The towers on the right are in one where they are.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes for sale today split the same way. Nearly every oceanfront condo for sale is in an allowed zone. Only about 1 in 5 houses and townhouses for sale in the city is.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fewer than 30 houses in the zones for homes may still be rented by the night, because they were rented that way before the current zoning. No new ones can be added.</p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">If a listing says short-term rentals are allowed, can you rent it nightly?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not always. 35 houses and townhouses for sale in the city say so in the listing. We checked each of them against our map, and 3 are not in an allowed zone. Many HOAs also ban rentals of any length. We check the zone and the HOA's rules for any home you like, and we leave out the homes where your plan is not allowed.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What does a nightly rental need?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city business license</a>. Every rental in the city needs one, short or long, and its fee is based on the rent you collect.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests pay about 13 percent in lodging taxes on top of each stay under 90 days. When a guest books through Airbnb, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb collects these taxes</a> for the state, the county and the city. On a booking you take yourself, you collect and pay them.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Find out if you can rent a home by the night</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. Before you offer, we tell you if the city and its HOA let you rent it by the night.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check a home's rental rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="oceanfront-buildings"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Oceanfront condos">What are oceanfront condos like in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 460 condos in oceanfront buildings inside the city resold in the past year. They range from hotel-style studios to three-bedroom condos. For a one-bedroom on the oceanfront, plan on about $160,000, the middle asking price today.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Building by building, the fees, sale prices and units for sale are on our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">oceanfront condo buildings page</a>.</p><div class="c3-mb-beside"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lowest prices are for studios of about 400 square feet at Tides, Driftwood and Oasis. Many of these buildings have a rental program for their owners.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="A row of oceanfront condo and hotel towers of 10 to 15 floors with pools in front, above a beach with umbrellas, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront condo towers south of downtown Myrtle Beach, near three of the busiest buildings in the table above. This stretch is in a zone where nightly rentals are allowed.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most buyers here live out of state. About 3 in 4 buyers of these oceanfront condos have their tax bill mailed outside South Carolina.</p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you get a loan on an oceanfront condo?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, but in many of these buildings not the most common kind. <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae</a> will not back a loan in a building managed like a hotel: with a front desk, daily cleaning, or a rule that owners put their unit in the rental program.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our preferred lender can tell you which loans work in the building you like. At closing, buyers usually also pay an HOA transfer fee and a few months of HOA dues in advance.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Get the oceanfront condos for sale in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-a-condo-earns"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What a condo earns">Does an oceanfront condo in Myrtle Beach pay for itself?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At typical figures, it covers its running costs and property tax, with about $8,100 a year left. That money must pay the HOA fee, a policy on the unit itself and any loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For the example below, we used the middle asking price for a one-bedroom on the oceanfront, about $160,000. We used the income of a typical one-bedroom nightly rental in the Myrtle Beach market, not this unit's own.</p><div class="c3-mb-sum" role="group" aria-label="A year for an oceanfront one-bedroom rented by the night, at typical income and price"><span class="cap">A year for an oceanfront one-bedroom rented by the night, at typical income and price</span><ol><li><span>What a typical one-bedroom nightly rental took in for a year, counting listings open only part of the year</span><strong>About $17,000</strong></li><li><span>Running costs for an owner who runs it without a manager: the Airbnb fee, cleaning, utilities, supplies, repairs, a short-term rental policy and the permit</span><strong>About $6,500</strong></li><li><span>Property tax at the rate for second homes, on $160,000</span><strong>About $2,400</strong></li><li class="tot"><span>Left each year for the HOA fee, a policy on the unit itself and any loan</span><strong>About $8,100</strong></li></ol></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether the unit pays for itself depends on the building's HOA fee, which is different in every building.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Most of the year's rental income comes in summer</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average listing takes in about 5 times as much in July as in January. June, July and August bring in almost half of a year's revenue.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-mb-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">What the average Myrtle Beach nightly rental takes in, by month</span><ul class="c3-mb-legend"><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#c4783a"></span>June to August</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#5c6b78;opacity:.55"></span>The other months</li></ul><svg class="c3-mb-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 232" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of what the average Myrtle Beach nightly rental takes in each month: January $1,340, February $1,680, March $2,530, April $2,800, May $3,270, June $6,070, July $6,800, August $4,400, September $2,550, October $2,150, November $1,620, December $1,590."><line x1="8" y1="196" x2="352" y2="196" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".25"/><rect x="11" y="165" width="22.7" height="31" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="22.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="39.7" y="157.1" width="22.7" height="38.9" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="51" y="218" text-anchor="middle">F</text><rect x="68.3" y="137.4" width="22.7" height="58.6" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="79.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="97" y="131.2" width="22.7" height="64.8" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="108.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="125.7" y="120.3" width="22.7" height="75.7" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="137" y="218" text-anchor="middle">M</text><rect x="154.3" y="55.5" width="22.7" height="140.5" rx="4" fill="#c4783a" fill-opacity="1"/><text class="ct" x="165.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="183" y="38.6" width="22.7" height="157.4" rx="4" fill="#c4783a" fill-opacity="1"/><text class="ct" x="194.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">J</text><rect x="211.7" y="94.2" width="22.7" height="101.8" rx="4" fill="#c4783a" fill-opacity="1"/><text class="ct" x="223" y="218" text-anchor="middle">A</text><rect x="240.3" y="137" width="22.7" height="59" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="251.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">S</text><rect x="269" y="146.2" width="22.7" height="49.8" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="280.3" y="218" text-anchor="middle">O</text><rect x="297.7" y="158.5" width="22.7" height="37.5" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="309" y="218" text-anchor="middle">N</text><rect x="326.3" y="159.2" width="22.7" height="36.8" rx="4" fill="#5c6b78" fill-opacity=".55"/><text class="ct" x="337.7" y="218" text-anchor="middle">D</text><text class="cl" x="11" y="157" text-anchor="start" fill="#4a5763">$1,340</text><text class="cl" x="194.3" y="30.6" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a5226">$6,800</text></svg><figcaption>Each month is the average of the past two years. The figures cover the whole Myrtle Beach market, which reaches past the city limits. Source: AirROI.</figcaption></figure><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">See if one oceanfront condo pays for itself</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building. We get its HOA fee and run the figures in the table above for that condo.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us run the numbers on a condo</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">Are Myrtle Beach home prices dropping?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For condos, yes. The typical condo value in Myrtle Beach is about 14 percent below its high in 2024, and it is still falling. For houses, no: the typical house value has stayed about the same since 2022.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-mb-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Typical home value in Myrtle Beach, houses and condos</span><ul class="c3-mb-legend"><li><span class="c3-mb-line" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Houses</li><li><span class="c3-mb-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Condos</li></ul><svg class="c3-mb-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of Zillow's typical home value in Myrtle Beach from 2019 to 2026. Single-family homes rose from about $243,000 to about $386,000 in 2022 and have held near $375,000. Condos rose from about $136,000 to about $239,000 in April 2024 and have fallen to about $207,000."><rect x="60" y="10" width="240" height="204" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.55)" rx="6"/><line x1="60" y1="146" x2="300" y2="146" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="54" y="151" text-anchor="end">$200k</text><line x1="60" y1="78" x2="300" y2="78" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="54" y="83" text-anchor="end">$300k</text><line x1="60" y1="10" x2="300" y2="10" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-opacity=".1"/><text class="ct" x="54" y="15" text-anchor="end">$400k</text><text class="ct" x="60" y="236" text-anchor="middle">2019</text><text class="ct" x="122.6" y="236" text-anchor="middle">2021</text><text class="ct" x="185.2" y="236" text-anchor="middle">2023</text><text class="ct" x="247.8" y="236" text-anchor="middle">2025</text><path d="M60 116.6L62.6 116.7L65.2 116.8L67.8 117L70.4 117.1L73 117.1L75.7 116.9L78.3 116.8L80.9 116.6L83.5 116.1L86.1 115.1L88.7 114.1L91.3 113.3L93.9 112.9L96.5 112.5L99.1 112.1L101.7 111.8L104.3 111.2L107 109.9L109.6 107.9L112.2 105.4L114.8 102.9L117.4 100.4L120 98L122.6 96.1L125.2 94L127.8 92L130.4 89.4L133 86.3L135.7 82.5L138.3 78.4L140.9 74.4L143.5 70.6L146.1 66.5L148.7 62.2L151.3 58L153.9 53.1L156.5 48.1L159.1 42.5L161.7 36.9L164.3 31.1L167 25.7L169.6 21.7L172.2 19.7L174.8 19.5L177.4 19.8L180 20.3L182.6 20.9L185.2 21.8L187.8 22.8L190.4 23.8L193 24.3L195.7 24.4L198.3 23.9L200.9 23.4L203.5 23.3L206.1 23.5L208.7 23.6L211.3 23.7L213.9 23.5L216.5 23.2L219.1 22.8L221.7 22.4L224.3 21.8L227 21.4L229.6 21.7L232.2 22.2L234.8 22.5L237.4 22.6L240 22.7L242.6 23.2L245.2 23.6L247.8 23.7L250.4 23.8L253 24.1L255.7 24.8L258.3 25.9L260.9 27L263.5 27.9L266.1 28.3L268.7 28.5L271.3 28.7L273.9 28.8L276.5 28.8L279.1 28.5L281.7 28L284.3 27.6L287 27.5L289.6 27.4L292.2 27.3L294.8 27.1L297.4 27L300 26.7" fill="none" stroke="#2f6f8f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M60 189.5L62.6 188.8L65.2 188.2L67.8 188L70.4 187.7L73 187.4L75.7 187.2L78.3 187.1L80.9 186.8L83.5 186.4L86.1 185.8L88.7 185.3L91.3 185L93.9 185L96.5 185L99.1 184.9L101.7 184.7L104.3 184.6L107 184.5L109.6 184.2L112.2 183.4L114.8 182.4L117.4 181.2L120 180.2L122.6 179.3L125.2 178.5L127.8 177.7L130.4 176.6L133 175.2L135.7 173.1L138.3 170.5L140.9 167.8L143.5 165.2L146.1 162.6L148.7 160L151.3 157.4L153.9 154.6L156.5 151.7L159.1 148.3L161.7 144L164.3 138.9L167 133.1L169.6 128.4L172.2 125.2L174.8 123.9L177.4 123.3L180 123.1L182.6 122.9L185.2 123.2L187.8 123.8L190.4 124.5L193 124.5L195.7 123.8L198.3 122.4L200.9 121.2L203.5 120.3L206.1 119.7L208.7 119.4L211.3 119.4L213.9 119.7L216.5 119.7L219.1 119.6L221.7 119.4L224.3 119.2L227 119.5L229.6 120.7L232.2 122.4L234.8 124L237.4 125.3L240 126.6L242.6 127.8L245.2 128.8L247.8 129.5L250.4 130L253 130.8L255.7 132L258.3 133.6L260.9 135.1L263.5 136.7L266.1 137.9L268.7 138.9L271.3 139.6L273.9 140L276.5 140.3L279.1 140.4L281.7 140.5L284.3 140.2L287 140.2L289.6 140.6L292.2 140.9L294.8 141.2L297.4 141.3L300 141.5" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="224.3" cy="119.2" r="4" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5"/><text class="cl" x="224.3" y="109.2" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a5226">Condo high</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="31.7" fill="#2f6f8f">$375k</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="146.5" fill="#8a5226">$207k</text></svg><figcaption>Zillow's typical value, monthly from January 2019. Houses here means single-family homes.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos also sell far more slowly than houses. At the past year's pace, it would take about a year and a half to sell every condo for sale now.</p><div class="c3-mb-tiles"><div class="c3-mb-tile hot"><span class="big">About 18 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every condo for sale in the city, at the past year's pace</span></div><div class="c3-mb-tile"><span class="big">About 4 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every house and townhouse for sale in the city</span></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That gives a condo buyer <a href="/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">room to negotiate</a>. On the house side, there are fewer homes for sale than buyers in a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year, condos in the city resold for about $175,000 in the middle: half sold for more, half for less. Houses resold for about $540,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">Is a Myrtle Beach address in the City of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not. About 3 in 4 houses and buildings with a Myrtle Beach mailing address are outside the city limits. Outside the city, the county's rental rules apply, not the city's.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest and Forestbrook are almost all outside the city, and Socastee is entirely outside it. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers that area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is a separate city. A short-term rental there needs a business license, and for now there is no special zoning or permit process beyond it. Our <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Tax and flood insurance">What do property tax and flood insurance cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a second home or rental pays almost four times the property tax of a home you live in. You apply for the lower rate on the home you live in, and our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> shows how.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Property tax each year inside the City of Myrtle Beach</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The home</th><th scope="col">A home you live in</th><th scope="col">A second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Every $100,000 of value</th><td data-label="A home you live in">$404</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">$1,528</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $540,000 house</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $2,180</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $8,250</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $175,000 condo</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $710</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $2,670</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Will you need flood insurance?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For most houses, no. Only about 1 in 23 houses in the city is in the high-risk flood zone of FEMA, the Federal Emergency Management Agency. About 1 in 4 condos is, many of them at the ocean's edge.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the high-risk zone, your lender will require flood insurance. On a house there, it usually costs about $800 a year. Outside that zone, federal rules do not require it, and a policy usually costs about $600.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo's HOA insures the building itself and adds the cost to the HOA fee.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the tax and the flood zone for one address</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its property tax as your main home and as a second home, and look up its flood zone.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out a home's tax and flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the house neighborhoods, the beach and the price of a condo. The hard ones are the condo market, the season and the flood zone at the ocean.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The house neighborhoods are mostly owners' main homes.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The beach, the Boardwalk, golf, a large hospital and the airport are all inside the city.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Condos cost far less than houses, a way to own at the beach for less.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>More people live in the city every year.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Condo prices are falling, and condos take far longer to sell than houses. <span class="c3-pc-do">We help you pick the building and negotiate the price.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Rental income comes mostly in summer. <span class="c3-pc-do">We plan the year with you before you buy.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Many oceanfront condos are in the high-risk flood zone. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the flood zone and the building's insurance for you.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Most houses cannot be rented by the night. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the zone of any address you send us.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-beach-real-estate-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach real estate FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you do short-term rentals in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, only in the zones where the city allows them, which hold most condos and almost no houses. The city bans rentals under 90 days in every zone for homes, except one zone set aside for visitor stays.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's market?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For condos, yes: there are about 18 months of condos for sale, and prices are falling. For houses, no: there are about 4 months of houses for sale.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Carolina Forest in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Carolina Forest has a Myrtle Beach address, but only about 1 in 75 houses and buildings in its ZIP code, 29579, is inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax on a second home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $1,528 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value inside the city. A home you live in pays about $404.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the difference between Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach are two separate cities with different rental rules. Myrtle Beach allows nightly rentals only in some zones. North Myrtle Beach, for now, asks only for a business license, with no special zoning or permit process beyond it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R1468.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city rentals</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city licenses</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R729.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">air base</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R986.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Boardwalk</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/photos_of_the_week/pow090420.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Park</a>, <a href="https://grandedunescommunities.sites.townsq.io/2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grande Dunes</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/parks-playgrounds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Market Common</a>, <a href="https://pinelakes.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Lakes</a>, <a href="https://www.thedunesclub.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dunes Club</a>, <a href="https://www.mygrandstrandhealth.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hospital</a>, <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb taxes</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">flood policies</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census</a>, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/cew/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA maps</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax levy</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NMB rentals</a>. Counts are ours, from city zoning, county parcels, FEMA and deeds. Listings in aggregate from CCMLS. 