63" y="770.1" text-anchor="middle">About ¼ mile</text><text class="lb hl" x="470" y="590" text-anchor="middle">Town center</text><text class="lb" x="987.1" y="304.6" text-anchor="end">Runway</text><text class="lb it" x="1250" y="1360" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-42 1250 1360)">Atlantic Ocean</text></svg></div><ul class="mc-legend"><li><i style="background:rgba(232,120,42,.55);border:2px solid #ffb35c"></i>Where planes are too loud for homes on the airport's map: a yearly average of 65 decibels or more</li><li><i style="background:rgba(255,231,194,.5);border:2px dashed #b9863f"></i>The town center district</li></ul><figcaption>The shaded area covers both the airport's map for today and its forecast for 2038. We traced it from the airport's drawing, so its edge is close but not exact. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Noise lines: Myrtle Beach International Airport layout plan, sheet 14. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The loud area runs along the runway and out past both ends, where planes take off and land. A small loud spot also sits around a helicopter pad near US 17 Business, at the runway's south end, used for oceanfront helicopter flights.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The airport's map uses a yearly average. A single takeoff is louder than the average, and planes are heard across the area.</p><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="How far the homes are from the loud area"><li><strong>The town center</strong>The closest part. Its nearest home is about a quarter mile from the loud area, and a little over half a mile from the runway's center line.</li><li><strong>The neighborhoods to the west</strong>The nearest home in them is about 0.9 mile from the loud area. In Belle Harbor and the Sanctuary section of Withers Preserve, at the west end, the nearest is about 1.8 miles.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="drives"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Beach and drives">How far is The Market Common from the beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is about 5 minutes by car with no traffic, at the city's beach access at 29th Avenue South, which is marked fully accessible. On foot it is about 45 minutes. Summer traffic on US 17 adds time to every drive.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From Valor Park to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The beach access at 29th Avenue South</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Walmart Neighborhood Market, Walton Drive</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Publix, Wood Duck Drive</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">South Strand Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">7 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport terminal</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">9 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Coastal Grand Mall</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">11 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Grand Strand Regional Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The airport terminal is across the runway, so the drive is longer than the distance looks on the map.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">See it on a Saturday</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which neighborhoods you like. We line up showings, and you walk the town center between them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us set up showings</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="compare"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compared">How does The Market Common compare with Carolina Forest and Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Market Common house costs more than one in Carolina Forest and less than one in Surfside Beach. Its townhomes cost more than either. Its share of houses in a high-risk flood zone sits between the two.</p><div class="mc-cmp"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase"></th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">The Market Common</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Carolina Forest</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Surfside Beach</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A house, the middle price</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$525,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$440,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$745,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A townhome, the middle price</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$375,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$230,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$250,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Houses in a high-risk flood zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">62 of about 2,480 (2.5%)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">13 of about 7,920 (0.2%)</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 31%</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">By car from Valor Park, no traffic</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Starting point</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 25 min, to its public library</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13 to 14 min, to its pier</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><ul class="mc-rules one mc-cmp-m" aria-label="The three areas compared"><li><strong>The Market Common</strong>A house about $525,000. A townhome about $375,000. Houses in a high-risk flood zone: 62 of about 2,480 (2.5%).</li><li><strong>Carolina Forest</strong>A house about $440,000. A townhome about $230,000. Houses in a high-risk flood zone: 13 of about 7,920 (0.2%). By car from Valor Park: about 25 min, to its public library.</li><li><strong>Surfside Beach</strong>A house about $745,000. A townhome about $250,000. Houses in a high-risk flood zone: about 31%. By car from Valor Park: about 13 to 14 min, to its pier.</li></ul><p class="mc-note">Past year. The Market Common and Carolina Forest: resales in Horry County deeds; Carolina Forest is the Census area of that name. Surfside Beach houses: every house sale in the town, its own page's figure.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest is a much larger inland area, with more than twice as many homes, about 25 minutes north by car. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers it in detail.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Surfside Beach is a beach town about 13 to 14 minutes south, where about 3 in 10 houses are in a high-risk flood zone. Our <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach guide</a> covers its two sides of the highway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is one part of Myrtle Beach. Our <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers the city's other parts and its rules on nightly rentals.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="before"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Before">What was The Market Common before?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common stands on the old Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, which closed in 1993. The town center opened on part of it in 2008.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Air Force has closed 229 cleanup sites on the old base since the 1990s. In 2019 it said 15 were still open, among them old landfills and groundwater sites. It said every site is being cleaned up to the standard for homes, and that no limit on the soil or groundwater rules out homes there.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero mc-side" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-warbird-park-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-warbird-park-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-warbird-park-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="799" alt="An A-10 jet seen from behind and an A-7 jet beside it, on display on a brick plaza with flags at Warbird Park" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Erechtheus. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Erechtheus</a></span></div><figcaption>Warbird Park on Farrow Parkway: an A-10, the kind of attack plane the base flew, and an A-7 beside it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three Air Force jets still stand in Warbird Park on Farrow Parkway: an F-100 Super Sabre, an A-7D Corsair and an A-10 Warthog. They are on permanent loan to the city from the Air Force.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="the-market-common-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">The Market Common FAQ</h2><style>.c3-faq details{border-top:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq details:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.2rem 0}.c3-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.c3-faq summary h3{margin:.9rem 0!important;flex:1}.c3-faq summary::after{content:"+";font:400 1.5rem/1 var(--sans);color:var(--brass);flex:none;width:1.5rem;text-align:center}.c3-faq details[open] summary::after{content:"\2212"}.c3-faq details p{margin:0 0 1rem!important}.c3-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brass);outline-offset:3px}</style><div class="c3-faq"><details open><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is The Market Common part of Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Every home in it is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, so the city's zoning and tax rate apply. Nearly every home has a Myrtle Beach mailing address in ZIP code 29577.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I rent out a Market Common home by the night?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only in the town center. The city's zones for rentals under 90 days include the town center's zoning district, but not the neighborhoods around it. Each HOA's rules also decide, and we read them for the home you pick.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Cresswind a 55-plus community?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Kolter Homes built Cresswind as what it called an active adult community, aimed at older buyers. Its rules on who may buy or live there are not published online. We read them for any Cresswind home you are thinking about.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I buy one of the apartments over the shops?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The apartments above the town center's shops are rented by the year. The area's 37 condos are in High Market, south of Valor Park.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do the neighborhoods have pools?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the 2023 aerial photo, seven of them have one. Cresswind has a clubhouse with a pool and courts. Emmens Preserve, Belle Harbor, Balmoral, Park Place and The Reserve each have a pool with a pool house or small clubhouse. Withers Preserve has a pool with a pool house in its Sanctuary section.</p></details></div><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R729.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">air base</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess117_2007-2008/bills/1230.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Senate</a>, <a href="https://www.afcec.af.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/2041781/brac-team-earns-us-epa-award-for-myrtle-beach-cleanup-redevelopment/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cleanup</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R400.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Warbird Park</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/directory/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">directory</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/events/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">events</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/parks-playgrounds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parks</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/photos_of_the_week/pow090420.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lake path</a>, <a href="https://waccamawmarkets.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">farmers market</a>, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20130321052307/http://www.kolterhomes.com:80/blog/2012/11/kolter-homes-introduces-cresswind-myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cresswind</a>, <a href="https://www.usgs.gov/centers/eros/science/usgs-eros-archive-aerial-photography-national-agriculture-imagery-program-naip" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NAIP aerial</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/services/accessibility_information/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">beach access</a>, <a href="https://aeronautics.sc.gov/sites/default/files/2025-03/14-MYR-LDU-36x48.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport plan</a>, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2024-title14-vol3/pdf/CFR-2024-title14-vol3-part150-appA.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAA rule</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">flood law</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC tax law</a>, <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenStreetMap</a>. Our counts: county parcels, flood zones and deeds; amenities read on the 2023 aerial; CCMLS listings in aggregate; the airport's noise lines on county parcels; routes on OpenStreetMap.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">A corner of the town center. Photo: DiscoA340, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_of_The_Market_Common,_Myrtle_Beach_(May_2023)_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Warbird Park. Photo: Erechtheus, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WarbirdPark.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The lake in Grand Park. Photo: DiscoA340, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Market_Common,_Myrtle_Beach_(13_May_2023)_35.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":800,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"A corner of the town center, with shops on the ground floor","caption":"A corner of the town center, with shops o