or="middle">Park Place</text><text class="lb" x="690" y="972" text-anchor="middle">West Lake</text><text class="lb" x="330" y="905" text-anchor="middle">Belle Harbor</text><text class="lb" x="900" y="525" text-anchor="middle">The Reserve</text><text class="lb" x="1214" y="950" text-anchor="middle">Sweetgrass</text><text class="lb" x="1214" y="988" text-anchor="middle">Square</text><text class="lb" x="268" y="700" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-63 268 700)">US 17 Bypass</text><text class="lb it" x="1840" y="1215" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-42 1840 1215)">Atlantic Ocean</text><text class="lb hl big" x="1165" y="640" text-anchor="middle">Town center</text><text class="lb hl" x="1138.3" y="750.4" text-anchor="start">Valor Park</text><text class="lb" x="1415" y="300" text-anchor="end">Airport runway</text><circle cx="1795.6" cy="952.4" r="11" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="5"/><text class="lb" x="1773.6" y="930.4" text-anchor="end">Beach access</text></svg></div><figcaption>The white outlines are the neighborhoods, and the dashed line is the town center district. The dot is Valor Park, where the walk and drive times on this page start. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Outlines: Horry County parcels and City of Myrtle Beach zoning. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each neighborhood has its own streets and its own amenities. A lot of 0.15 acre is about 6,500 square feet. Prices are what a house resold for in the past year, the middle price.</p><ul class="mc-rules one" aria-label="The neighborhoods of The Market Common"><li><strong>The town center's own streets</strong>About 500 homes, about half townhomes and half houses, on small lots: a house lot is about 0.08 acre. The shops and the lake are about an 8-minute walk. A house resold for about $570,000 and a townhome for about $400,000. The builder sold 9 new townhomes here in the past year.</li><li><strong>Emmens Preserve</strong>The largest, with about 730 homes: about 610 houses and 120 townhomes. A house lot is about 0.15 acre. Its pool and pool house sit beside a lake, and it has a park with a pavilion. A house resold for about $440,000, the lowest of the neighborhoods, and a townhome for about $380,000.</li><li><strong>Belle Harbor</strong>About 480 homes at the west end, by the US 17 Bypass, most of them houses, on house lots of about 0.17 acre. Its amenity area has a pool, a small clubhouse and a sports court. A house resold for about $545,000.</li><li><strong>Cresswind</strong>400 houses on lots of about 0.16 acre. Kolter Homes started it in late 2012 as what it called an active adult community, aimed at older buyers. Kolter's plans gave its clubhouse a fitness center, and the clubhouse has a pool, tennis and pickleball courts and a lake path beside it. A house resold for about $540,000.</li><li><strong>Withers Preserve</strong>About 220 houses in three sections, Highlands, Estates and Sanctuary, on lots of about 0.19 acre. A house there resold for about $520,000.</li><li><strong>Park Place</strong>About 190 houses on lots of about 0.15 acre, with a pool and pool house. A house resold for about $525,000.</li><li><strong>West Lake</strong>About 140 houses on lots of about 0.15 acre. Only 6 resold in the past year, too few for a fair middle price.</li><li><strong>Balmoral</strong>About 120 houses on the largest lots here, about 0.21 acre, with a pool and pool house. A house resold for about $685,000, the highest of the neighborhoods.</li><li><strong>The Reserve</strong>About 110 houses on lots of about 0.15 acre, with a pool and pool house. A house resold for about $520,000.</li><li><strong>Sweetgrass Square</strong>66 houses inside the town center district, about a 13-minute walk from Valor Park.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Kolter Homes' word for Cresswind was "age targeted", which is not the same as limited by age. Its rules on who may buy or live there are not published online, so we read them for any Cresswind home you pick. Our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55-plus communities guide</a> covers the area's age-restricted communities.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">What do homes cost in The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year a typical house in The Market Common resold for about $525,000: half sold for less and half for more. The middle half sold between about $475,000 and $567,000. A condo resold for about $310,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A townhome resold for about $375,000 across the whole area. In the town center it was about $400,000, and in Emmens Preserve about $380,000. The neighborhood list above gives each one's house price.</p><p class="mc-note">Resales recorded in Horry County deeds in the past year. A neighborhood's price is given when it had 10 or more sales.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">New homes cost more. The only builder sales in the past year were 9 townhomes on the town center's streets. They sold for about $580,000, about $180,000 more than a resale townhome on the same streets.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On November 8, 2026, 66 homes were for sale in the area: 43 houses, 20 townhomes, 2 condos and 1 lot.</p><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="Homes for sale on the day we counted"><li><strong>43 houses</strong>Asking about $530,000 at the middle. Most have 3 or 4 bedrooms and about 2,190 square feet.</li><li><strong>20 townhomes</strong>Asking about $420,000 at the middle. Each has 2 or 3 bedrooms, about 1,710 square feet at the middle.</li></ul><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><div class="hx-strip" data-place="market-common-townhomes" data-name="Market Common townhomes" data-head="Townhomes for sale in The Market Common"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you own here and want to sell, our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value page</a> explains how we price a home from recorded sales.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get today's count of homes for sale</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We run this count again on the day you ask, sorted by neighborhood, and send each home with its HOA fee and flood zone.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us run the count again</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does a Market Common home cost to own each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Besides the mortgage and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a>, a typical house here that you live in costs up to about $3,900 a year in property tax and HOA fee. A town center townhome costs about $6,400 to $7,600 a year, mostly because its HOA fee is higher.</p><div class="mc-cost"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">House</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Town center townhome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $2,100</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $1,600</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">HOA fee</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to $1,800</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,800 to $6,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Together</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to $3,900</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$6,400 to $7,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="mc-note">About, as your main home: a house bought for about $525,000 and a town center townhome bought for about $400,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fees are what the homes for sale list: most houses $150 a month or less, and town center townhomes about $400 to $500. Before you offer, we get the HOA's budget for the home you pick, so you know what the fee covers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, a home you live in pays about $404 a year in property tax for every $100,000 of the county's value. A second home or rental pays about $1,528, about 3.8 times as much.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When a home sells, its county value becomes about the price a buyer pays, so your tax starts from your price. The lower rate needs an application to the county. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> explains both rates.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zones">Is The Market Common in a flood zone?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost none of it is. Only 62 of about 3,000 homes in The Market Common sit in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, all of them houses:</p><ul class="mc-rules one" aria-label="Homes in the high-risk flood zone"><li><strong>Cresswind</strong>38 houses.</li><li><strong>Balmoral</strong>14 houses.</li><li><strong>The town center</strong>10 houses, on its own streets.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No other neighborhood has a home in the zone. At all 62, a big flood can bring rising water, but not ocean waves. A mortgage from a federally backed or regulated lender on a home in that zone requires flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Another 30 homes are in the moderate zone, where a lender does not require flood insurance. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">flooding a seller may not mention</a> explains how we look into a home's flood history.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Check one home before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We check its flood zone, its HOA fee and its tax as a main home, and tell you what we find.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us check a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="airport-noise"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Airport noise">How loud is the airport next to The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You will hear planes here, because the airport's runway runs along the town center's east side. Even so, no home in The Market Common is inside the area the airport's own map marks as too loud for homes. The FAA treats homes outside that area as suitable next to an airport, with no limits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We placed every home's lot on the airport's map, for today and for its forecast in 2038. The closest home is about a quarter mile outside the loud area, on the town center's east edge.</p><figure class="mc-fig narrow"><div class="mc-frame"><svg class="mc-map mc-noise" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1600 1619" role="img" aria-labelledby="mc-noise-t"><title id="mc-noise-t">Aerial map of the town center of The Market Common and the airport next to it. A shaded band marks where the airport's yearly average airplane noise reaches 65 decibels or more. It runs along the runway and out past its south end toward the beach. The town center's homes sit to the south-west of the band, about a quarter mile from it at the closest point.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-noise-aerial.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1600" height="1619" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M509.3 839.4L504.8 814.7L537.7 807.8L542.8 815.8L550.8 811L550 798.4L542.6 795.4L539.9 779.9L569.9 773.4L574.6 775.3L578.4 771.6L623.5 761.6L632 798.4L635 801.6L640.2 796.8L635.1 770.9L647.8 769.4L662.8 844.1L668.7 847.3L671.5 841.8L654.6 760.6L667.1 760.8L686.6 851.5L671.1 854.5L667.9 861.5L654.5 864.4L649.1 861L645 865.8L602.4 874.8L597.6 873L594.1 876.5L563.8 882.8L554.5 839.2L571.7 835.1L575.6 837.4L590.1 835.5L592.2 831.9L591.6 820.7L585.3 815.9L581.5 819.8L544.8 826.9L543.4 831.4L550.4 865.1L541.5 870.4L544 886.1L520.6 891.8L515.1 867.9L524.2 862L520.6 842.2L517.5 838.4L509.3 839.4ZM490.9 751.2L482.4 709.8L492.6 707.4L495.3 703.4L486.8 679.5L509.5 673L514.3 674.5L551.6 661L555.1 674.9L558.6 677.9L603.5 664.5L609.7 691.6L612.6 694.8L618.4 690L637.9 687.2L641.4 681L650.8 679.7L661.3 729L627.1 732.9L622.3 729.6L617.9 734.8L597.2 739L594.7 728.5L597.2 722.6L591 692.5L587.8 689.6L580.8 690.5L576.6 696.6L560.1 698.9L556.9 702.4L564.9 745.9L533.8 752.6L529.3 750.9L504.5 758.5L500.6 750.7L490.9 751.2ZM481.1 631.7L478.6 617.7L498.3 613.6L501.3 626.6L499.5 632.5L503.4 636.9L505.9 650L486 654.3L482.6 641.5L484.3 635.5L481.1 631.7ZM333.9 794L324.6 741.5L320.4 738L319.3 731.6L332.8 728.3L337.6 746.3L369 745L377.3 750.8L403.3 781.9L377.8 811L377.8 817.7L383.4 823.1L393.5 820.9L401.3 810.8L411.9 788.2L444.6 800.8L490.1 805L497.9 841.9L458.9 844L453.2 842.8L448.4 835.1L427.2 839L418.9 832.2L370.4 839.1L360.2 792.2L356.3 789.8L333.9 794ZM406.8 709.3L407 700.1L422.1 700.2L426.8 696.1L424.9 680.9L432.8 676.6L431.7 665.4L438.6 659.7L435.3 645.9L425.6 644L425.3 632.7L420.5 628.6L418.1 616.6L439.6 612.7L443.3 627L453.3 627.6L463.6 676.7L462