i:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main ol.c3-nmb-steps li::before{left:0!important;top:.95rem!important}main#main .c3-nmb-ex{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-left:3px solid var(--brass)!important;padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1.2rem!important}main#main .c3-pc>div{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:2px solid var(--brass)!important;padding:.9rem 0 0!important}main#main .c3-pc{column-gap:2.5rem!important}main#main .c3-cc,main#main .c3-gchart,main#main figure.c3-nmb-fig,main#main ol.c3-nmb-steps,main#main .c3-nmb-ex,main#main .c3-pc{max-width:720px!important;box-sizing:border-box}@media (min-width:1180px){main#main .c3-nmb-entry{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,640px) minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:repeat(14,auto) 1fr;column-gap:2.5rem;align-items:start;margin:2.6rem 0 2rem}main#main .c3-nmb-entry>*{grid-column:1}main#main .c3-nmb-entry>h3.c3-nmb-h3{margin-top:0!important;grid-column:1/-1}main#main .c3-nmb-entry>figure.c3-nmb-side{grid-column:2;grid-row:2/-1;margin:.35rem 0 0!important;max-width:none!important}}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city has eight parts a buyer can tell apart, and each gives you something the others do not. Five run along the ocean; the other three lie inland. Under each one are the homes for sale there now.</p><div class="c3-nmb-list"><p class="c3-nmb-grp">On the ocean, from north to south</p><ul><li><a href="#cherry-grove">Cherry Grove</a><span>A dock behind the house, and a pier at sunrise</span></li><li><a href="#tilghman-beach">Tilghman Beach</a><span>Houses by the ocean, most of them the owner's main home</span></li><li><a href="#ocean-drive">Ocean Drive</a><span>Main Street and its shag clubs</span></li><li><a href="#crescent-beach">Crescent Beach</a><span>A house near the ocean for less, with little flood zone</span></li><li class="c3-nmb-ab"><b>Atlantic Beach</b><span>A separate town, not part of the city</span></li><li><a href="#windy-hill">Windy Hill</a><span>Beach houses at some of the lower prices by the ocean</span></li></ul><p class="c3-nmb-grp">Inland</p><ul><li><a href="#little-river-neck">Little River Neck</a><span>Woods and trail rides north of the Cherry Grove marsh</span></li><li><a href="#west-of-us-17">West of US 17</a><span>Newer houses a few minutes' drive from the beach</span></li><li><a href="#across-the-waterway">Across the waterway</a><span>Four golf courses, a marina and almost no flood zone</span></li></ul></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="cherry-grove" data-toc="Cherry Grove" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Cherry Grove: a dock behind the house, and a pier at sunrise</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cherry Grove is the part for a boat at the back door. Channels were dug into its marsh in the 1970s, and about 680 houses now back onto them or the marsh edge. Many have <a href="/buyers/waterfront-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">a dock behind the house</a>, and boats reach the ocean through Hog Inlet.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="Cherry Grove from above: rows of houses on narrow lots between dug channels, with docks behind them, the marsh beyond, and the ocean along the bottom, labelled Boat ramp, Heritage Shores, Channel houses and Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Cherry Grove from above, 2023 aerial: houses on the dug channels, many with a dock behind them, the marsh, the boat ramp and Heritage Shores.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the city's boat ramp on 53rd Avenue North, you can paddle a kayak about a mile and a half through Hog Inlet, past pelicans and ospreys, to the empty beach on Waties Island. People walk the shore there looking for shells and fossil shark teeth, including megalodon teeth.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Walk 985 feet out on Cherry Grove Pier to the two-story deck at the end, where people watch the sun rise over the ocean and look for dolphins, then eat at the Driftwood restaurant on the pier. In 1964 a fisherman landed a 1,780-pound tiger shark from this pier, and the pier still lists it as a world record.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Looking up the beach in Cherry Grove from a height: low beach houses and mid-rise condo buildings along the road, the marsh behind them, and a long fishing pier reaching into the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Melikamp. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Melikamp</a></span></div><figcaption>Cherry Grove from a height in 2012: older low beach houses beside mid-rise condos, the marsh behind them, and Cherry Grove Pier.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the Fourth of July, the city puts on a free fireworks show over the ocean at the pier. People carry beach chairs onto the sand to watch it, after checking the tide. Heritage Shores Nature Preserve has walking paths on an island in the marsh, and the Russell Burgess Coastal Preserve has a boardwalk.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house on the channels resold for about $715,000 at the middle (38 sales), and elsewhere in Cherry Grove about $665,000. The trade-off is flood insurance: almost every house here is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, channel houses included. Only about 1 in 4 houses is the owner's main home.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-cherry-grove" data-name="Cherry Grove"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Cherry%20Grove">Send me homes in Cherry Grove<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="tilghman-beach" data-toc="Tilghman Beach" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Tilghman Beach: houses by the ocean, most of them main homes</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tilghman Beach suits a buyer who wants a house by the ocean among owners who make it their main home. About 2 in 3 houses here are, the most of any beach part.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: houses around lakes labelled Tilghman Beach, a row of houses along the beach, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Tilghman Beach from above, 2023 aerial: a row of houses along the ocean, and streets of houses around the lakes behind them.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From about May to mid-August, loggerhead turtles about three feet long come up this sand at night and lay about 120 eggs each. Volunteers from the Sea Turtle Patrol watch over and protect the nests, and 45 to 65 days later the hatchlings dig out at night and head for the moonlit water.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tilghman Beach grew from one large tract that Charles T. Tilghman Jr. developed in 1948. Its houses sell for the most of any part. In Tilghman Estates, its largest neighborhood, the middle of 19 house resales was about $1.05 million. Seabrook Plantation resold for about $750,000, the middle of 9 sales.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of its homes in the flood zone are condos, not houses.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-tilghman-beach" data-name="Tilghman Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Tilghman%20Beach">Send me homes in Tilghman Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="ocean-drive" data-toc="Ocean Drive" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Ocean Drive: Main Street and its shag clubs</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Drive is the part with Main Street, which runs back from the ocean. McLean Park, built around a small lake, is about a 5-minute walk from it.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="Ocean Drive from above: Main Street running back from the beach, a park with a small lake labelled McLean Park, condo towers along the beach and the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Ocean Drive from above, 2023 aerial: Main Street running back from the beach, McLean Park and its lake, and the condo towers along the ocean.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The shag is South Carolina's state dance. In the old beach towns of Ocean Drive and Crescent Beach, a pavilion and amusement park drew crowds to dance it.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="755" alt="A postcard of a long wooden pavilion on the beach at Ocean Drive, with Roberts Pavilion and Dancing painted on its end wall and old cars parked beside it" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-US-no_notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Postcard, 1941, public domain. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Postcard, 1941, public domain</a></span></div><figcaption>The pavilion at Ocean Drive Beach on a 1941 postcard, with &quot;Dancing&quot; painted on its end wall.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is still danced on Main Street, all year:</p><ul class="c3-nmb-cal"><li><strong>Every night.</strong> At Fat Harold's Beach Club, a DJ plays beach music from 7. Couples take shag lessons on Monday nights, and Tuesday night is for learning the state dance.</li><li><strong>January, April and September.</strong> Thousands of shag dancers fill the clubs on Main Street for the Society of Stranders: Midwinter Break, Spring Safari and Fall Migration.</li><li><strong>March.</strong> People set up beach chairs and golf carts along Main Street by 8:30 a.m. for a St. Patrick's Day parade of more than 100 entries, then stay for a free festival until 4.</li><li><strong>November.</strong> The Carolina Beach Music Awards weekend brings beach music bands to the stages of the shag clubs.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve, which the city calls its last maritime forest, has dunes 30 feet tall and a half-mile trail. Houses in the Ingram Beach neighborhood resold for about $1.35 million at the middle (12 sales).</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Prices here spread wide: the middle half of house resales ran from about $385,000 to $980,000. Most of its homes in the flood zone are oceanfront condos; about 1 in 10 houses is in it.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-ocean-drive" data-name="Ocean Drive"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Drive">Send me homes in Ocean Drive<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="crescent-beach" data-toc="Crescent Beach" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Crescent Beach: a house near the ocean for less</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Crescent Beach suits a buyer who wants a house near the ocean at a lower price. Its houses resold for the least of the beach parts, and only about 1 house in 100 is in the flood zone, the fewest of the beach parts.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The loggerheads nest on this beach too, and the Sea Turtle Patrol's volunteers watch over the nests until the hatchlings head for the water.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses on the original Crescent Beach lots resold for more. The county records those lots under two names, and their middle prices were about $665,000 and $718,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 18th and Edge pocket park is its own small green space. Crescent Beach ends at Atlantic Beach, a separate town that did not join the city.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: a small town outlined in brass and labelled Atlantic Beach, running from the highway to the ocean, with streets labelled Crescent Beach on one side and Windy Hill on the other" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Atlantic Beach, outlined, is a separate town between Crescent Beach and Windy Hill, from US 17 to the ocean (2023 aerial).</figcaption></figure></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-crescent-beach" data-name="Crescent Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Crescent%20Beach">Send me homes in Crescent Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="windy-hill" data-toc="Windy Hill" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Windy Hill: beach houses south of Atlantic Beach</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Windy Hill suits a buyer who wants a beach house at one of the lower prices by the ocean. Local history says it got its name in 1791, when George Washington rode this stretch of beach on a windy day and his hat kept blowing off.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: streets of houses among trees labelled Windy Hill, a row of condo buildings along the beach, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Windy Hill from above, 2023 aerial: streets of houses under the trees, condo buildings along the ocean, and a marsh creek at the left.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Investors from Conway built it up after World War II. Houses on the original Windy Hill Beach lots resold for about $439,000 at the middle (10 sales). Most of its houses are outside the flood zone; most of its condos are in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yow Park and the 41st Avenue South pocket park are its neighborhood parks.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-windy-hill" data-name="Windy Hill"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Windy%20Hill">Send me homes in Windy Hill<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="little-river-neck" data-toc="Little River Neck" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Little River Neck: woods and trail rides north of the marsh</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River Neck suits a buyer who wants a house among owners who live there. It lies north of the Cherry Grove marsh, along Little River Neck Road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inlet Point Plantation Stables is two miles down a one-lane dirt road through the woods. From there, an hour-long trail ride passes deer, wild turkeys and an alligator sunning by a lake, follows the Intracoastal Waterway across from Calabash, and ends at the marsh behind Waties Island.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Open Space Institute has bought more than 600 acres on and around Waties Island and the mainland at Little River Neck. The state plans to make parts of it a new state park and parts a Heritage Trust preserve, open to the public.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tidewater Plantation is its largest neighborhood, and about 8 in 10 of its houses are the owner's main home. Builders are still selling new houses here: 53 in the past year. The Neck also holds most of the city's manufactured homes, about 660 of 800.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-little-river-neck" data-name="Little River Neck"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Little%20River%20Neck">Send me homes in Little River Neck<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="west-of-us-17" data-toc="West of US 17" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">West of US 17: newer houses a few minutes from the beach</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of US 17 suits a buyer who wants a newer house close to the beach, with little flood zone. From a typical house here, the drive to Ocean Boulevard is about 4 minutes.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: new streets and ponds cleared for houses labelled West of US 17, ball fields labelled Central Park, and the highway labelled US 17" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>West of US 17 from above, 2023 aerial: new streets cleared for houses, Central Park's ball fields, and US 17.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every Monday night in summer, Barefoot Landing, on the waterway at US 17, has a fireworks show at 10 p.m.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold 94 new houses here in the past year, and the city's 20-acre Central Park is in this part. Chestnut Greens is the largest neighborhood, and its houses resold for about $515,000 at the middle.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sunset Harbour resold for about $760,000 (9 sales), but 68 of its homes are in the high-risk flood zone. Condos here cost the least in the city, about $175,000 at the middle.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-west-of-us-17" data-name="North Myrtle Beach west of US 17" data-head="Homes for sale west of US 17 now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=West%20of%20US%2017">Send me homes west of US 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><div class="c3-nmb-entry"><h3 id="across-the-waterway" data-toc="Across the waterway" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3">Across the waterway: golf, newer houses and almost no flood zone</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across the Intracoastal Waterway suits a buyer who wants golf, a newer house and almost no flood zone: 2 homes of about 5,200 are in it. More of the city's new houses sold here than anywhere else.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Barefoot Resort's four golf courses were designed by Greg Norman, Davis Love III, Tom Fazio and Pete Dye. Seven holes of the Norman course run along the waterway, and the resort has a deep-water marina with a bar and grill on the water.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero c3-nmb-side" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: shops around a lake labelled Barefoot Landing, the wide Intracoastal Waterway with a marina on its far bank labelled Across the waterway, and US 17" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Barefoot Landing on the Intracoastal Waterway at US 17, 2023 aerial, with the neighborhoods across the waterway on the far bank.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Barefoot Landing, the shops and restaurants on the waterway at US 17, is about 11 minutes by car from Main Street. From a typical house here, the drive to Ocean Boulevard is about 11 minutes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses in Grande Dunes North resold for about $374,000 at the middle, and in Waterside for about $385,000. We pull the HOA papers and fees for any house here.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nmb-across-the-waterway" data-name="North Myrtle Beach across the waterway" data-head="Homes for sale across the waterway now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Across%20the%20waterway">Send me homes across the waterway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The eight parts side by side</h3><div class="c3-nmb-parts"><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The eight parts side by side: middle sale prices over the past year, from county deeds</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Typical resold house</th><th scope="col">Typical condo</th><th scope="col">Main homes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#cherry-grove" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Cherry Grove</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $695,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $310,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#tilghman-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Tilghman Beach</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $725,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $325,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 2 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#ocean-drive" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Ocean Drive</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $600,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $360,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 4 in 10</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#crescent-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Crescent Beach</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $410,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $340,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#windy-hill" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Windy Hill</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $460,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $360,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#little-river-neck" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Little River Neck</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $590,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $320,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#west-of-us-17" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">West of US 17</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $475,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $175,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#across-the-waterway" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Across the waterway</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $480,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $275,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The last column shows how many houses are the owner's main home. Where that share is low, more houses are second homes or rentals, and fewer people live there all year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="living-here"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Living here">What is North Myrtle Beach like to live in?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach has about nine miles of ocean beach, running south-west from Hog Inlet. Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill voted to become one city in 1968.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the 1970s, condo and hotel towers began replacing houses on the oceanfront. Today condos outnumber houses about 3 to 2.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 18,800 people lived in the city at the 2020 Census, about 37 percent more than in 2010. Close to half its homes were kept for seasonal or vacation use. Our <a href="/submarkets/little-river/#living-here" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Little River guide</a> compares that share with the towns nearby.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How is North Myrtle Beach different from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is not part of Myrtle Beach. It is a separate city in Horry County, with its own city tax and its own rules for nightly rentals. The Myrtle Beach oceanfront, at the SkyWheel, is about 30 minutes south by car without traffic.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The map shows the drives from Main Street to the pier, McLeod Seacoast hospital and Barefoot Landing. The airport is about 35 minutes away and Grand Strand Medical Center about 20. Summer traffic on US 17 makes those drives longer.</p><figure class="c3-nmb-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-nmb-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-main-street" viewBox="0 0 360 314" width="360" height="314" role="img" aria-label="Map of North Myrtle Beach: from Main Street, Cherry Grove Pier is about 8 minutes by car, McLeod Seacoast hospital about 9 minutes and Barefoot Landing about 11 minutes." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-main-street text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-main-street .h{font:500 17p