--brass)"] a.btn.btn-brass:hover{border-color:var(--brass)!important;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#fff,rgba(232,201,154,.35))!important}main#main .c3-sb-side+.hx-strip:not(:empty){margin-top:1.4rem}main#main .c3-sb-side+.hx-strip,main#main .c3-sb-side+.hx-strip+.hx-fallback{margin-bottom:2.4rem}main#main .c3-gchart,main#main div[style^="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0"],main#main .c3-cc,main#main .c3-pc,main#main .c3-sb-rules,main#main .c3-sb-note,main#main figure.c3-sb-fig{max-width:720px!important;box-sizing:border-box}</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town calls itself the Family Beach. Its center is the pier, at the ocean end of Surfside Drive.</p><div class="c3-sb-side" style="--sb-rows:auto auto 1fr"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The pier</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's fishing pier is all concrete and reaches 814 feet into the ocean. It opened on the town's 60th birthday, and walking on it is free.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Surfside Beach Pier, labelled, running from a wide beach into a green ocean, with parking lots and rows of beach houses behind the sand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>The concrete pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pier has two restaurants, The Whistling Duck and Surf Diner, plus an ice cream shop and a bait shop. A day of fishing is $14. From April through October it stays open until 1 a.m.</p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A year of town events</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has its own events department, and many of its events are free. Many take place at the pier, on Ocean Boulevard or in Memorial Park.</p><ul class="c3-sb-rules"><li><strong>Spring</strong>A two-day barbecue festival with a cook-off in March. A kite festival at the pier in April. The Memorial Day golf cart parade down Ocean Boulevard.</li><li><strong>Summer</strong>A free concert in Memorial Park, next to the library, on Sundays from 4 to 7 p.m. The Fourth of July golf cart parade, free to join.</li><li><strong>Fall</strong>An end-of-summer fireworks festival at the pier in September, with free shuttles from the town's parking lots.</li><li><strong>All season</strong>An arts and crafts market every Thursday from March to November, at Surfside Drive and Willow Drive. The Yuletide golf cart parade in December.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Golf carts</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most trips here need a car or a golf cart. To drive a cart on the street, South Carolina law requires a DMV permit decal, liability insurance and a licensed driver 16 or older.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carts may use only roads posted at 35 mph or less, and never the sand. A cart driven at night must have working headlights and taillights. The town passed its own golf cart ordinance in 2025.</p><div class="c3-sb-side" style="--sb-rows:auto auto 1fr"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has 36 public beach accesses and 12 beach parking lots. Five accesses have wheelchair access, and beach wheelchairs are available through the town police department.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A row of two- and three-story beach houses in blue, yellow and gray behind low dunes, seen across a wide sand beach under a blue sky at Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: BullDawg2021. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: BullDawg2021</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses along the sand at Surfside Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free parking passes per household for the town's lots. The town's lots charge by the hour from March through October. Dogs stay off the beach from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May through Labor Day.</p></div><div class="hx-strip" data-place="town-surfside-beach" data-name="Surfside Beach" data-head="Homes for sale in Surfside Beach now"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Get the homes for sale in Surfside Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from the pier, without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 Business is slower.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the Surfside Beach Pier to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Food Lion on US 17 Business</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Garden City Pier</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">11 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="own-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Its own town">Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with its own council, police department and beach rules. Its mailing ZIP code is 29575.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A "Surfside Beach" address does not prove a home is in the town. Of the homes for sale with that address when we counted, about two in three were outside the town limits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those homes are on county land, where the town's rental rules do not apply. Horry County's zoning has no limit on how long a home there may be rented, but a subdivision's recorded rules can. We read those rules for the home you like.</p><div class="c3-sb-note"><b>How the town began.</b> Much of its land was once the Ark Plantation. The beach was later called Roach's Beach, then Floral Beach, and took the name Surfside Beach in 1952. Hurricane Hazel in 1954 destroyed 18 of the 65 houses then at the beach.</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What do you own at Ocean Lakes?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Lakes Family Campground is next to the town's north end, about 7 minutes from the pier by car, and it is not in the town. It has about 2,600 sites leased by the year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At Ocean Lakes you buy the house, mobile home or camper on the site, not the land. The site comes with a yearly lease from the campground, and we go through it with you before you offer.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Lakes">Ask about a home in Ocean Lakes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rental-map"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rental map">Where can you rent by the night in Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nightly rentals are allowed only on the blocks near the ocean, the orange band on the map. The town calls them its R3 and C3 zones, and its own zoning sheet names R3 "High Density/Weekly Rental".</p><figure class="c3-sb-fig"><svg class="c3-sb-defs" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden"><defs><g id="c3-sb-mapg"><rect x="0" y="0" width="5227" height="1851" fill="#f1ece3"/><rect x="0" y="1851" width="5227" height="520" fill="#cfe2e8"/><path d="M5224 946L5221 972L5226 977L5219 1052L5191 1128L5182 1165L5180 1262L5173 1306L5152 1368L5054 1348L4958 1822L3932 1838L4189 828L4499 868L5199 943L5224 946Z" fill="#e6e0d5" stroke="#8a8378" stroke-width="10" stroke-dasharray="40 26"/><path d="M3967 523L3627 483L3621 536L3472 520L3431 531L3359 527L3362 453L2967 435L2965 497L2804 490L2805 483L2777 501L2698 498L2701 436L2667 435L2665 485L2620 485L2620 480L2591 479L2098 459L2125 409L2254 414L2260 400L2206 397L2291 186L2175 140L2138 223L2092 349L2034 449L2001 451L1824 443L1827 382L1800 381L1797 441L1637 435L1632 429L1614 426L1618 368L1590 367L1588 431L1396 424L1399 358L1344 355L1341 421L1165 410L1173 205L1105 206L1096 252L1080 252L1079 242L946 236L919 403L764 396L771 358L376 341L339 544L359 566L260 1836L580 1836L706 1843L714 1839L1267 1829L1539 1836L1557 1831L1640 1836L1859 1832L1859 1840L1938 1840L1938 1851L1989 1851L1992 1833L2337 1838L2337 1826L2352 1826L2919 1836L3643 1837L3658 1775L3654 1775L3730 1472L3739 1475L3744 1454L3788 1465L3790 1456L3793 1443L3749 1433L3751 1425L3742 1422L3784 1245L3838 1256L3847 1215L3849 1210L3795 1199L3831 1045L3886 1050L3891 1031L3837 1020L3858 931L3912 942L3924 885L3933 884L3938 858L3876 853L3907 721L3971 729L3977 671L3950 668L3967 523Z" fill="#fbf8f3"/><path d="M3388 1487L3448 1483L3586 1510L3596 1518L3597 1538L3549 1525L3450 1530L3425 1525L3393 1508L3386 1494L3388 1487ZM3030 1680L3178 1681L3180 1775L3030 1774L3030 