a mile</text></svg></div></div><figcaption>Where nightly rentals are allowed in the Town of Surfside Beach, with its streets. Map drawn by Chapter3 from the town's zoning map and Horry County parcel and street records.</figcaption><ul class="c3-sb-key" aria-label="Map key"><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#d9823b"></span><span><b>Near the ocean: nightly rentals allowed.</b> The town's R3 and C3 zones, about 4 in 10 of its homes.</span></li><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#5f9a6e"></span><span><b>Inland: no rentals under 30 days.</b> The R1 and R2 zones, close to half of the town's homes.</span></li><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#c8c2b8"></span><span><b>Other districts:</b> the pier's entertainment district, planned developments and commercial land. We check the parcel.</span></li><li><span class="c3-sb-sw" style="background:#e6e0d5;border:2px dashed #8a8378"></span><span><b>Ocean Lakes Family Campground:</b> next to the town, not in it.</span></li></ul></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North of the pier, the line follows Dogwood Drive North, and houses on that street fall on both sides. South of the pier, it follows Willow Drive South for about 0.3 mile, to about 6th Avenue South. From there it follows Lakeside Drive: houses on the ocean side of Lakeside are on the rental side, and houses on its inland side are not.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the pier, the town's entertainment district breaks the band. Inland, the green streets reach back to the commercial strip on US 17 Business. On those streets the town allows rentals of a year or more, and none under 30 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The gray areas are planned developments and commercial land. Each planned development has its own approved uses, so we read the approval for the parcel.</p><div class="c3-sb-side" style="--sb-rows:auto auto 1fr"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the line looks like from the air</h3><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-rental-line-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of Surfside Beach near the pier. A green line circles the inland streets of houses under trees, labelled no nightly rentals, R1 and R2. An orange line circles the blocks of beach houses near the ocean, labelled nightly rentals allowed, R3." loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Near the pier, from the air. Inside the green line: inland streets, no rentals under 30 days. Inside the orange line: nightly rentals allowed. Land outside both lines is in other districts. Lines drawn by Chapter3 from the town's zoning map.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two sides look different. Near the ocean, tall beach houses stand close together on small lots. Inland, houses are farther apart, under the trees.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is the house you like on the rental side?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing or the address. We place it on the town's zoning map and tell you which rules apply before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the listing</a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Home prices">What do homes cost in Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house near the ocean costs about twice an inland house. In the past year, houses near the ocean sold for about $1 million at the middle, and inland houses for about $485,000 to $540,000.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Near the ocean, houses sold for about twice the inland ones in the past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Near the ocean, houses sold for about twice the inland ones in the past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Side and kind of home, lot or kind</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses near the ocean</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">nightly rentals allowed</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,000,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses inland, largest lots</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">lots of 9,000 sq ft or more</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.542" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$540,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses inland, smaller lots</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">lots of 6,000 sq ft or more</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.487" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$485,000</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos near the ocean</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">nightly rentals allowed</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.38" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$380,000</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Every sale Horry County recorded inside the town limits in the past year.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two sides are built to different rules. Near the ocean, the town allows taller buildings on smaller lots:</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The town's building rules near the ocean and inland</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">Nightly rentals</th><th scope="col">Tallest building</th><th scope="col">Smallest lot for a house</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Near the ocean (R3)</th><td data-label="Nightly rentals">Allowed</td><td data-label="Tallest building">55 feet</td><td data-label="Smallest lot for a house">3,600 sq ft (3,000 attached)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Inland, smaller lots (R2)</th><td data-label="Nightly rentals">Not allowed</td><td data-label="Tallest building">35 feet</td><td data-label="Smallest lot for a house">6,000 sq ft</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Inland, largest lots (R1)</th><td data-label="Nightly rentals">Not allowed</td><td data-label="Tallest building">35 feet</td><td data-label="Smallest lot for a house">9,000 sq ft</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nearly half of the recent buyers whose deed we could match gave a mailing address outside South Carolina.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses for sale in the town had no HOA (homeowners association) fee when we counted, about 6 in 7. Our page on <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA</a> covers what that lets you park and build.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know what one Surfside Beach home is worth</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull the recorded sales on its street and its side of the line, and tell you what they say about the price.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us pull the sales</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Surfside Beach each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Besides the mortgage and home insurance, the yearly cost here is mostly property tax and flood insurance. Both depend on where the house is and how you use it.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year, about</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">An inland house you live in</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">A house near the ocean, rented or a second home</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The county's value for tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$490,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$860,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Town and county tax, before credits</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,100</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$11,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Flood policy, the typical one on these streets</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$700</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,250</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>Total, besides the mortgage and home insurance</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>$2,750</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>$12,300</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A buyer's tax starts from the county's value, which resets toward the price at the sale. Owners who bought years ago often pay less because of the state's 15 percent cap on reassessment.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why a main home pays about a third as much</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">South Carolina does not tax the whole value of a home. For your main home, the tax rate applies to 4 percent of the county's value, and the school operating tax is skipped.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a second home or rental, the rate applies to 6 percent of the value, with every tax. On the same home, that makes the tax about 3 times as much. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax calculator</a> has every town's rate.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood insurance near the ocean and inland</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the pier to the south end of town, most homes are on the rental side. There, a typical flood policy on a house costs about $1,250 a year. On the inland streets it is about $700.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">FEMA takes 15 percent off flood insurance in the town, for the town's flood rules and programs.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the yearly cost of one address</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its tax as a main home and as a rental, and get a flood quote for the house.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price the tax</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="flooding"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flooding">Does Surfside Beach flood?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inland, few homes are in a high-risk flood zone: 2 percent on the smaller-lot streets and 15 percent on the largest lots. Near the ocean it is most homes, and every home on the ocean side of Ocean Boulevard.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, inland and near the ocean"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, inland and near the ocean</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Where</span><span role="columnheader">Share of homes</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inland, smaller lots</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.02" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2 percent</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Inland, largest lots</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.155" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">15 percent</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The whole town</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.39" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">39 percent</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Near the ocean</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.783" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">78 percent</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>FEMA's high-risk flood zones on Horry County's flood map, at each home's parcel.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A federally backed or regulated mortgage on a home in a high-risk zone requires flood insurance.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The 48 percent rule</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This town rule matters most for an older, low house. It covers a building whose lowest floor is below the 100-year flood level, the flood height on FEMA's map.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If repairs or improvements cost 48 percent or more of the building's value, the whole building must be raised. It goes up to that flood level plus 3 feet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town uses the county assessor's building value, land excluded, unless the owner submits a licensed appraisal. Half the town's homes were built before about 1985.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you offer on an older house near the ocean, we pull its flood zone and the county's building value. You then know how much work the rule allows before the house must be raised.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What the storms did</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pier was first built in 1953. Hurricanes Hazel and Hugo each destroyed it, and after Hugo it was not rebuilt until 1993. Hurricane Matthew in 2016 took more than half of its length.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our pages on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">finding out whether a house has flooded</a> and <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance</a> show what else we look at.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the flood facts for one Surfside Beach house</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull its flood zone and the county's building value, and tell you where the 48 percent line falls.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us check for flooding</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="airbnb"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting it out">Can you Airbnb a house in Surfside Beach, and what does it earn?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on the blocks near the ocean, with a town business license for each rental property. The owner also files the town's hospitality fee and local accommodations tax every month, even when nothing is due.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Guests pay about 12 percent in lodging taxes on top of the rent, to the state, the county and the town. You collect it and send it on.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a Surfside Beach area rental takes in</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">AirROI, a rental data company, counts about 550 active Airbnb listings in its Surfside Beach market, which reaches past the town limits. The average one took in about $43,000 in gross bookings over the past year, before costs.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That was up about 7 percent on the year before. Most of the money comes in summer: the average listing takes in about five times as much in July as in January.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="In a month, the middle Surfside Beach area rental takes in about $3,800"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">In a month, the middle Surfside Beach area rental takes in about $3,800</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Listings</span><span role="columnheader">Gross bookings in a month</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Bottom quarter of listings</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.088" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,800 or less</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The middle listing</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.188" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,800</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Top quarter</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.365" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$7,500 or more</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Top tenth</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.625" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$12,800 or more</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>AirROI, the active Airbnb listings in its Surfside Beach market. Gross bookings, before cleaning, platform and management costs.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Worked example: a condo near the ocean, rented by the night</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take a condo near the ocean at about $380,000, the middle condo sale there in the past year. Say it books what the average listing books, with no loan.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">One year of nightly renting</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Gross bookings, the average listing in AirROI's area</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$43,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Town and county tax as a rental, if the county values it at the price paid</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$4,880</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That leaves about $38,000 before every other cost: the condo dues, cleaning, management, insurance, utilities and any loan. Those depend on the building, so we price them for the exact unit before you offer.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Thinking of renting a Surfside condo or house by the night?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We confirm it is on the rental side, and price the tax, the dues and the insurance for that unit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask about renting it out</a></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What Airbnbs take in across eight towns is on our <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb income page</a>. The rules by town are on our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules page</a>, and the yearly rental math on our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">long-term rental page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pros-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Surfside Beach?</h2><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>About 2 miles of beach with 36 public accesses.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>A new concrete pier, free to walk, with two restaurants.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Free summer concerts in Memorial Park and golf cart parades on Ocean Boulevard.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Owners who live elsewhere park free in town lots with two passes.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Near the ocean, only about 1 home in 8 is taxed as its owner's main home. <span class="c3-pc-do">On the inland streets with the largest lots, about 7 in 10 are.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Flood insurance costs more near the ocean, and big work on a low house there can mean raising it. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the zone and the building value first.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Two in three "Surfside Beach" listings are outside the town, under county rules. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the town limits and the subdivision's rules for every listing.</span></span></li></ul></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Comparing beach towns? Our guides to <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Garden City</a>, <a href="/submarkets/murrells-inlet/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Murrells Inlet</a> and <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach</a> cover their own rules and prices.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="surfside-beach-sc-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Surfside Beach, SC FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with the ZIP code 29575.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you Airbnb in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only on the blocks near the ocean, in the town's R3 and C3 zoning districts. Rentals under 30 days are not allowed in the inland R1 and R2 districts.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you drive a golf cart in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on town streets posted at 35 mph or less, with a state permit decal, insurance and a licensed driver 16 or older. Never on the beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are dogs allowed on Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. At other times, leashed dogs are welcome.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is parking free in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Town lots charge from March 1 to October 31, 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free passes per household.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On a home the county values at $500,000, the town and county tax is about $2,100 a year as your main home. As a second home or rental, it is about $6,400.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What schools serve Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Horry County Schools, which assigns schools by address. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What about crime in Surfside Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We do not rate places for crime. The town has its own police department, and the FBI publishes the crime each police agency reports.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/surfside_beach/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=CH17ZO" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town code</a>, <a href="https://surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/3026/New-Zoning-Map" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town zoning map</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/i0pfcm2o/appendix-b-zoning-ordinance-upated-912026.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenFEMA</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">42 U.S.C. 4012a</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/392/48-Percent-Rule-PDF" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">48 percent rule</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/212/Surfside-Beach-Fishing-Pier" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the pier</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/178/Events" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town events</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/200/Beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town beaches</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/202/Parking" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parking</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t56c002.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 56-2</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Minutes/_08262025-1302" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">council minutes</a>, <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/DocumentCenter/View/148" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">license guide</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-575</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/surfside-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www.oceanlakes.com/lodging-2/annual-lease-sales/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Lakes</a>, <a href="https://data.census.gov/table?g=160XX00US4570585" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census 2020</a>. Our counts: town zoning on county parcels and streets, flood maps and deeds. Listings in aggregate. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The concrete pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors and added a label.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses along the sand at Surfside Beach. Photo: BullDawg2021, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>,