-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:1rem">Working with a Chapter3 agent is built around the study we run on any property you are serious about, before a cent of earnest money is on the line. It includes:</p>
-<ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.85;max-width:760px;margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.2rem">
-<li>The <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">HOA bylaws</strong> and as many of the association&rsquo;s <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">financials</strong> as we can get our hands on.</li>
-<li>The building&rsquo;s <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">litigation history</strong>, where it is obtainable.</li>
-<li>A full <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">investment analysis</strong>: long-term and short-term rent expectations, the average nightly rate, and occupancy month by month. From those we build <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">net operating income</strong>, the income left after expenses; <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">cap rate</strong>, the yearly return if you paid all cash; <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">cash-on-cash return</strong>, yearly cash profit divided by the cash you put in; and expected appreciation.</li>
-</ul>
-<p style="margin-bottom:0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px">Even if you never intend to rent it out, that analysis tells you whether you are paying a fair price for what you are getting.</p>
-</div></section>
