-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do you keep working after I buy?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px">Yes. Every month after closing you get fresh property facts, an updated investor report, nearby-permit alerts, and appreciation updates. Most agents stop at closing; we do not.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is in the building study you run before I make an offer?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px">HOA bylaws and financials, the building&rsquo;s litigation history where we can get it, and a full investment analysis, so you know exactly what you are buying before any money is at risk. The section above lists every figure it includes.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do I have to be an investor to get the investor report?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px">No. We build the investor report on every purchase, even for buyers who will never rent the home, because it is the clearest way to know whether the price is fair.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What does data-forward mean here?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">You get property-level intelligence, including permit activity, pipeline developments, rezoning, and rental data, in addition to a comparative market analysis.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Chapter3 only for investors?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. The data approach helps buyers and sellers too. Investors use the tools the most.</p></div></div></section>
